contact-us\">Dr.Sumitz Clinic</a>:-</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>First Floor, Krishna Avenue, Above Dominos, Opposite DMART, Baner, Pune - 411045</strong></p>\r\n','uploads/product/119001128_27_01_2021_11_26_35.jpg','2021-01-27 05:56:35','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(16,'how-to-strengthen-the-lower-back','How to strengthen the lower back','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Exercising to strengthen the lower back can help reduce and prevent low back pain. It can also strengthen core, leg and arm muscles. Exercise also inc...','<p>Exercising to strengthen the lower back can help reduce and prevent low back pain. It can also strengthen core, leg and arm muscles. Exercise also increases blood flow to the lower back, which can reduce stiffness and speed up the healing process.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Below, we explain how to do exercises that strengthen the lower back and can help people manage lower back pain:</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>1. Pelvic Tilts</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Pelvic tilt exercises can release tight back muscles and keep them flexible.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To practice this lower back flexibility:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Laying the arms back on the floor, keeping the arms flat and knees flat.</li>\r\n	<li>Gently lean backwards and push the belly out.</li>\r\n	<li>Hold for 5 seconds, then relax.</li>\r\n	<li>Level the back and pull the belly button towards the floor.</li>\r\n	<li>Hold for 5 seconds, then relax.</li>\r\n	<li>Increase the number of repeats daily, to 30.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>2. Cat Stretches</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Cat Stretches\" src=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/public/uploads/gallery/722682013_26_02_2021_01_50_11.jpg\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Cat stretching can help to lengthen the back, strengthen it and reduce muscle tension.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To perform the cat stretch:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Separate hands and knees from hip-width to knees.</li>\r\n	<li>Arch at the back, pulling the bellybutton towards the spine.</li>\r\n	<li>Slowly relax the muscles and allow the stomach to slide towards the floor.</li>\r\n	<li>Return to the starting position.</li>\r\n	<li>Repeat 3-5 times twice a day.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>3. Superman</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>A person needs strong back extensor to maintain good posture. These muscles run on both sides of the spine.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Weak back extensors can reduce spinal and pelvic support, but doing an exercise called &quot;Superman&quot; can help.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To Superman:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Lie on the floor and spread both hands in front of the body, so that the feet are more flat on the ground.</li>\r\n	<li>Raise both hands and feet, and create a gap of about 6 inches between them and the floor.</li>\r\n	<li>Try to pull in the bellybutton, lifting from the floor to engage the core muscles.</li>\r\n	<li>To prevent neck injury, keep the head straight and look at the floor.</li>\r\n	<li>Extend the arms and legs as far as possible.</li>\r\n	<li>Hold the position for 2 seconds.</li>\r\n	<li>Return to the starting position.</li>\r\n	<li>Repeat 10 times.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>4. Seated Low Back Rotational Curls</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The seated lower back rotational stretch relieves pain, helps the core muscles to work and strengthen the lower back.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To perform the seated lower back rotational stretch:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Sit on a floor without a stool or chair, keeping the feet flat.</li>\r\n	<li>Fold the hips to the right while keeping the spine square and the spine long.</li>\r\n	<li>Place the hands behind the head or the left hand on the right knee to support the stretch.</li>\r\n	<li>Hold the position for 10 seconds.</li>\r\n	<li>Repeat the exercise on the left.</li>\r\n	<li>Repeat 3 to 5 times each day.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>5. Draw in maneuvers</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The draw-in maneuver serves as transversus abdominis. This muscle is on the front and side of the stomach, stabilizing the lower abdomen and lower back.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To perform a draw-in maneuver:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Laying the arms back on the floor, keeping the arms flat and knees flat.</li>\r\n	<li>Take a deep breath.</li>\r\n	<li>By exhaling, tighten the abdominal muscles, keep the abdominal muscles strong and the hips steady.</li>\r\n	<li>Hold the position for 5 seconds.</li>\r\n	<li>Repeat 5 times.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Takeaway</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Exercising to make core muscles work can prevent injury, increase stability, and improve flexibility. People with lower back pain should also pay attention to their normal posture and how they carry heavy objects to identify movements that may be responsible.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anyone experiencing lower back pain that is severe or does not go away with a gentle stretch should contact a doctor for exercise.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If any of these make back pain worse, they should be stopped immediately and consult a doctor.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/454797750_26_02_2021_01_57_11.jpeg','2021-02-26 08:27:11','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(17,'how-to-stretch-your-neck','How to stretch your neck','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','If you&#39;ve got a stiff neck or a pharyngitis, you&#39;ve got heaps of company. Neck pain is the most commonest form of pain in folks. But like othe...','<p>If you&#39;ve got a stiff neck or a pharyngitis, you&#39;ve got heaps of company. Neck pain is the most commonest form of pain in folks. But like other parts of your body, exercises and stretches will create the muscles in your neck stronger and a lot of limber. Attempt these moves to loosen a tense neck, banish pain, and gain flexibility.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Bonus:</strong> A strong neck can help prevent problems with your shoulders, upper back and arms as well.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you have already got <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/back-and-neck-pain\">pain in your neck</a> or elsewhere, see your doctor before you begin. You&#39;ll feel some tension in your neck muscles once you stretch. However you shouldn&rsquo;t have pain if you stop directly.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Side Tilt</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Side Tilt\" src=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/public/uploads/gallery/629336080_26_02_2021_03_46_54.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Stand while doing this, with your feet hip-width apart and arms down your sides.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Gently tilt your head toward your right shoulder and touch it together with your ear. Stop after you feel the stretch. Do not raise your shoulder.</li>\r\n	<li>Hold the stretch for 5&ndash;10 seconds, then return to the start position.</li>\r\n	<li>Repeat on your left side. You will be able to do multiple sets and work your way up to 10 repetitions.</li>\r\n	<li>For further stretch, place the hand on an equivalent aspect of your inclined head on top of your head, and press gently together with your fingertips.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Forward and Backward Tilt</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>This can be done while you are sitting or on your feet. Keep your moves slow and smooth.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Keep your shoulders with your head and your back straight.</li>\r\n	<li>Lower your chin towards your chest and hold for 15-30 seconds. Relax, and raise your head slowly.</li>\r\n	<li>Tilt your chin towards the ceiling and bring the base of your skull towards your back. Hold for 10 seconds, then return to the start position.</li>\r\n	<li>Repeat the set for 3 -4 repetitions. Do it daily.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Shoulder roll</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>It stands out the best.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Raise your shoulders straight up and move them in a circle moving forward. Do this 8 times.</li>\r\n	<li>Return to the start position, and draw another 6 circles, this time going backwards.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Side Rotation</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>You can do this even while sitting or standing.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Keep your head straight on your shoulders and your back.</li>\r\n	<li>Slowly bend your head to the right until you feel a stretch in the side of your neck and shoulders.</li>\r\n	<li>Hold the stretch for 15&ndash;30 seconds, and then slowly move your head forward again.</li>\r\n	<li>Repeat on your left side. Perform upto 15 sets.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n','uploads/product/657131085_26_02_2021_03_51_41.jpg','2021-02-26 10:21:41','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(18,'tips-for-healthy-legs-in-2021','Tips for healthy legs in 2021 ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','If you&rsquo;re like the majority, you wish robust, fit, and healthy legs. Only 1 downside, few people skills to induce them, or how to take care of t...','<p>If you&rsquo;re like the majority, you wish robust, fit, and healthy legs. Only 1 downside, few people skills to induce them, or how to take care of them once we have them.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Wouldn&rsquo;t or not it&#39;s nice if there was a listing of easy tips, belongings you might do straight away to induce the healthy, handsome legs you want?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>That is precisely what we have a tendency to square measure attending to show you with straightforward habits you&#39;ll be able to begin nowadays to induce improbably healthy legs within and out. Keep reading!</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>1. Take straightforward steps to keep up a healthy weight</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>There are many ways to keep yourself at a healthy weight. Following these straight steps may not only cut back your odds of developing unhealthy veins, although you will be able to reduce your risk of developing arthritis, the loss of animal tissue within the joints.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Lower the number of times you gulp the unwanted extra calories each day.Keep moving - When you are active throughout the day, then your body burns calories, which will help in maintaining a healthy weight gradually. Additional on this in step 2!</li>\r\n	<li>Drink additional water &ndash; correct association is crucial for maintaining your overall health.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>2. Keep active with regular <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/physical-therapy-for-athletes\">exercises</a></h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Take a 30-minute walk daily -</strong> it won&#39;t be much, although the health edges are only several measurements of walking, and walking will probably be a huge difference for you.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Go swimming or do water cardiopulmonary exercise &ndash;</strong> These square measure nice low-impact ways in which to exercise with a good come in calorie-burn.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Run or Hike &ndash;</strong> With the proper type and also the right footwear, these exercises are fun and get you outside!</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Stretching or taking yoga categories &ndash;</strong> Maintaining flexibility in your body could be a very important part of any exercise set up.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Don&rsquo;t over-think it &ndash;</strong> If none of those choices square measure appealing to you, strive diversion in your front room. Be creative! the purpose is just to maneuver your body.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>3. Get snug with compression</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Compression socks offer higher circulation One tool that you just could haven&#39;t thought of is medical-grade compression stockings. Additional individuals together with skilled athletes have begun to have confidence in them to enhance circulation, minimize swelling, and cut back recovery time when a troublesome exercising or an extended day spent on your feet. They conjointly offer you another bonus of serving to stop unhealthy and spider veins.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Find a honored dealer of medical-grade stockings.</li>\r\n	<li>Choose the planning that&#39;s right for you.</li>\r\n	<li>Enjoy the advantages of improved circulation in your legs.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>4. Support healthy blood flow by not sitting for too long</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The job of your veins is to induce your blood back to the guts. after you move your legs, your calf muscles work to pump and squeeze the blood up and out of your legs. Follow these simple steps to keep your blood moving.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>If you sit for long periods of your time, set several times throughout the day when you can get up and move around.</li>\r\n	<li>If you are working from home, do not keep all your food and drink on your table - it can make you stand up again and again throughout the day.</li>\r\n	<li>Set a timer if you won&rsquo;t keep in mind to induce up each hour approximately and walk around for a number of minutes.</li>\r\n	<li>If you&#39;ll be able to complete some work standing up take advantage of those times to work while standing. This may facilitate stop unhealthy veins!</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>5. Relax with a massage</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Get a massage to assist circulation in your legs. Massage helps improve circulation throughout your body and makes you feel rested and relaxed.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Massages facilitate improve circulation throughout your body and cause you to feel rested and relaxed.</li>\r\n	<li>Check with your doctor and create a regular schedule for massage.</li>\r\n	<li>Find Associate in Nursing commissioned massage expert with smart reviews. Relax!</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n','uploads/product/965587002_26_02_2021_05_15_24.jpg','2021-02-26 11:32:16','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(19,'how-to-live-a-healthy-lifestyle','How To Live A Healthy Lifestyle','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','The phrase &#39;healthy lifestyle&#39; is the short definition of how you should live if you want to live a vibrant, active life with a healthy body a...','<p>The phrase &#39;healthy lifestyle&#39; is the short definition of how you should live if you want to live a vibrant, active life with a healthy body and a healthy mind. Devising a healthy lifestyle does not have to mean extreme commute. Making small changes steadily to your diet and activity habit can have a major impact.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>What Is A Healthy Lifestyle?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>You know the evident etiquettes that express someone who is healthy and take care of themselves. A healthy person does not smoke, tries to maintain a healthy weight, eats healthy food with fruits, vegetables and fiber and of course, exercises regularly. Then there are other constituents to add to the list. A healthy person also knows how to manage anxiety, gets a good quality sleep each night, doesn&#39;t drink too much, doesn&#39;t sit too much - basically, does everything in leniency all the time. When you look at all the things that could conceivably go in a healthy lifestyle, you can see how hard all of those things are in our current world.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The satisfactory news is that you do not need to transpose everything at the same time. In fact, the trick to staying healthy is making small changes- taking more steps each day, 1 adding fruit to your cereal, having an extra glass of water, or saying that a potato made of butter is no other help. One thing you can do now to make your lifestyle healthy is to grow more.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Benefits of Physical Activity</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>You know that you need to Work-out, but there are many excuses for not doing so. You are very busy, do not know where to start, you are not motivated or you are afraid that you will injure yourself. Maybe you think work-out is really hard or it is not good enough.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Whatever your definition of work out is or is not, the bottom line of it is that exercise is development. Whether it is walking around the block or running a marathon, this development is work out and every time you do more than you normally do, it matters.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Healthy Maintenance</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Even if you choose for small changes, the advantages are very astonishing. For instance, increasing the intensity of your workout will help you to reach and maintain a chiseled physique. If you are currently overweight, small steps towards that goal can have an impact.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In fact, you don&#39;t even have to set goal of losing weight, especially if you have problems sticking to a program. After getting some healthy habits under your belt, why not start worrying about losing weight and stay healthy?</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Other Advantages</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The enormous thing about moving forward is that there can be other abiding advantages of just a few minutes a day, many of which you may not even be aware of. Just a few advantages include:-</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Enhance dignity.</li>\r\n	<li>Helps maintain pliability as you age.</li>\r\n	<li>Improves joint steadiness.</li>\r\n	<li>Ameliorate memory in elderly people.</li>\r\n	<li>Enrich tendency and reduces symptoms of anxiety and depression.</li>\r\n	<li>Maintain Bone Mass.</li>\r\n	<li>Prohibit osteoporosis &amp; fractures.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>A Word From <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\">Dr. SumitZ Clinic</a></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"Health\" src=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/public/uploads/gallery/719897818_19_03_2021_05_06_13.jpg\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Creating a healthy lifestyle does not mean rigorous changes. When you don&#39;t need to overhaul your entire life, you can make changes for the better. Just choose one thing and work on that one thing every day, so that the rest of your life and habits remain the same. You might be surprised that those small changes can really make a difference.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So, Stay Healthy &amp; Stay Safe!</p>\r\n','uploads/product/505601811_19_03_2021_05_10_33.jpg','2021-03-19 11:40:33','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(20,'8-rules-for-a-healthy-back','8 Rules for a Healthy Back','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','A lot of people are affected by back pain in their daily life. And beyond living with this type of severe pain, this type of situation can reduce the...','<p>A lot of people are affected by <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/orthopaedic-treatment\">back pain</a> in their daily life. And beyond living with this type of severe pain, this type of situation can reduce the quality of your life, causing you to miss work and social activities that give you pleasure and enable you to complete simple everyday tasks.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In fact, lower back pain is the leading cause of job-related disability. Taking care of your spine - ie your back and neck - will now help you reduce your chances of experiencing back pain later. Many of the steps you take to improve the overall health of your spine are nothing more than practicing better body mechanics, or how you shake yourself and hold it while performing daily tasks and activities.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Take care of your spine</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Here are simple and important rules to keep your back healthy:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li><strong>Exercise regularly:-</strong>Exercise is important for muscle strength - and strong back muscles. Help support your spinal column. Wall squats and leg lifts are good for your back, and many yoga poses help to keep your back muscles strong.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Lift Right:- </strong>If you do not use the proper form when lifting an object, it is very easy to bend the wrong way and damage your spine. Here&#39;s how to lift correctly, Stand as close to the object as possible, and use your legs and knees instead of your back or upper body to pull the item. This will help if you bend your knees so that your arms are at the same height as the item. Keep your head down and back straight. If the item is heavy, do not attempt to lift it yourself - get help.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Do not stand with legs straight:- </strong>Keeping your knees straight, keep them &quot;soft&quot;. The tension on your spinal column decreases as you stand.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Train your spine muscles every day:- </strong>Teach your spinal muscles to support your spinal column. Exercise to keep them strong.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Be active:- </strong>If you are not active or physically fit, you are at increased risk of lower back pain. Whether you visit the gym regularly, take a walk, bike, swim or play with your children, staying active and keeping your body moving helps to maintain a healthy spine.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Do sports, especially swimming, running, or cycling:- </strong>Many sports provide a good workout seeming to be useless. Exercise by swimming, running, cycling, or engaging in other exercises. Sports that pump your heart and your muscles move.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Stay hydrated: - </strong>Staying hydrated is important for maintaining soft tissue elasticity and fluidity in joints. Our intervertebral (spinal cord) discs are vulnerable to hydration loss and can begin to decrease height. As the spinal disc begins to shrink, you become susceptible to painful disc conditions. Herniated discs, also known as slipped or broken discs, occur when fluid loss causes the disc to become brittle and eventually fall out of place.<br />\r\n	A herniated disc is the most common cause of sciatica, a specific type of back pain that radiates to one of the legs. The bulging disc can also sometimes cause sciatica. Furthermore, as the protective padding of the spine decreases, it further contributes to the loss of structural health.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Note any warning signs:- </strong>Do not ignore spinal problems or pain. Although back pain is common once in a while, it can indicate a more serious problem. Left untreated, your spine problems can worsen and become quite severe. Listen what your body is telling you. Do not overdo it in the gym or at work, or with self-medication to relieve symptoms. Seek medical care to learn more about your spine and the right treatment for your symptoms.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>If you have already tried all these rules and steps and still won&rsquo;t be able to recover from your back pain then you can <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/contact-us\">Contact us</a> as we are giving services and treatments regarding back pain as well that is very effective.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/14791336_31_03_2021_06_46_30.jpg','2021-03-31 13:16:30','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(21,'budget-friendly-nutrition-for-weight-loss','Budget Friendly Nutrition For Weight Loss','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Not all calories are produced corresponding.Different foods pass through different catabolic passageways in your body.They can have a drastically diff...','<p>Not all calories are produced corresponding.Different foods pass through different catabolic passageways in your body.They can have a drastically different effect on your appetite, hormones and the number of calories you burn.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Here are the most budget friendly <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/nutrition-dietitian\">nutrition</a> for weight loss on Earth which is supported by science.</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3>Leafy Greens</h3>\r\n	Leafy greens include kale, spinach, collards, Swiss charts and a few others.<br />\r\n	They have many nutrients that make them perfect for weight loss diets, such as being low in calories and carbohydrates and loaded with fiber.Eating leafy greens is a great way to increase your food intake, without increasing calories. Many studies show that food and diets with low energy density make people eat fewer calories overall.<br />\r\n	Leafy greens are also incredibly nutritious and are very high in many vitamins, antioxidants and minerals, including calcium, which has been shown to aid fat burning in some studies.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3>Cruciferous Vegetables</h3>\r\n	Cruciferous vegetables indulge Broccoli, Cabbage, Cauliflower and Brussels sprouts.Like other vegetables, they are high in fiber and tend to be incredibly filling.<br />\r\n	What else are you looking for, this type of veggies usually contains a fair amount of protein.They are not nearly as high protein as animal foods or legumes, but still higher than most vegetables.<br />\r\n	A combination of protein, fiber, and low energy density makes cruciferous the perfect foods to incorporate vegetables into your diet if you need to lose weight.<br />\r\n	They are very high in nutrition and also prevents cancer.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3>Boiled Potatoes</h3>\r\n	White potatoes seem to have fallen out of applaud for some reason.<br />\r\n	Though, they have many qualities that make them a complete meal - both for weight loss and ideal health.They are an incredibly diverse range of nutrients - almost everything you need.There are some people who only eat potatoes and not any other food and have maintained a good health.<br />\r\n	They are particularly high in potassium, a nutrient that most people do not get enough of and it plays an important role in blood pressure control.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3>Soups</h3>\r\n	Most foods with low energy density are those that contain a lot of water, such as vegetables and fruits.If you want you can also just only add water to your food, i.e. in your soup.Some researches have shown that eating a single meal turns into soup instead of solid food, which makes people feel more satiated and eat significantly fewer calories.<br />\r\n	Just make sure not to add too much fat to your soup, such as cream or coconut milk, as it can significantly increase its calorie content.</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3>Avocados</h3>\r\n	Avocados are a distinctive fruit.<br />\r\n	While most fruits are high in carbs, avocados are loaded with healthy fats.They are exceptionally high in monounsaturated oleic acid, the same type of fat found in olive oil.Despite being mostly fat, avocados contain too much water and fiber, making them less energy-dense than you might think.What&#39;s more, they are perfect for vegetable salads.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>It is very simple and not so complicated to find a good nutrition for weight loss.These are mostly Avocados, Soups, Leaf greens, Cruciferous vegetables, Potatoes boiled.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/529217520_31_03_2021_07_39_49.jpg','2021-03-31 14:09:49','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(22,'tips-to-help-keep-your-bones-strong','Tips To Help Keep Your Bones Strong','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','What happens to my bones according to my age?\r\n\r\nIn childhood and adolescence, most of our bone growth and bone solidity occur. By the age of 18, girl...','<h2>What happens to my bones according to my age?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>In childhood and adolescence, most of our bone growth and bone solidity occur. By the age of 18, girls reach their utmost bone solidity. For boys, it is up to the age of 20 years. In middle age, it is necessary to maintain bone density and try to slow the rate of bone loss. As we get older, the density of our body bones decreases. After menopause, women are particularly at risk of osteoporosis.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How Can I Keep My Bones Strong?</h3>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li><strong>Consume enough nutrients to keep your bones strong</strong>\r\n\r\n	<p>Potassium, vitamin K and magnesium help your body consume and use calcium. Get these important nutrients by eating healthy foods like vegetables and fruits, legumes (beans, peas, lentils), nuts, seeds, whole grains, and fish. Protein helps build muscle, which helps to keep bones strong. Eat protein-rich foods such as meat, poultry, fish, shellfish, legumes (beans, peas, lentils), nuts, and seeds.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Keep Your Caffeine Consumption Limited</strong>\r\n	<p>Consuming too much caffeine can reduce the amount of calcium you absorb. Do not exceed 500mg of caffeine per day for adults (about 2-3 cups of coffee per day). Pregnant and lactating women should not have more than 300 mg of caffeine per day.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Do not consume Alcohol</strong>\r\n	<p>Drinking alcohol can cause bone loss. If you drink, there are no more than 2-3 drinks per day.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Quit Smoking to keep your bones strong</strong>\r\n	<p>If you smoke, you may be at greater risk of rapid bone loss and bone fractures than non-smokers.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<br />\r\n	<li><strong>Regularly Indulge in physical activities to keep your Bone strong</strong>\r\n	<p>Set a goal to be active for at least 150 minutes each week. Here are some remedies to help keep your bones strong. Try:</p>\r\n	&nbsp;\r\n\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>Weight-bearing exercises such as running, walking, hiking, low-impact aerobics, dance, tennis, and golf.</li>\r\n		<li>Resistive activities such as lifting weights or push-ups help build muscles that keep your bones strong.</li>\r\n		<li>Stretching exercises like yoga and tai chi help improve balance and coordination, which will reduce the risk of bones falling and breaking.</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are looking for <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/osteoporosis-treatment\">Bone surgery</a> or you are facing any problems regarding your Bones then you can Contact <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\">Dr.SumitZ Clinic</a> is the best clinic in Pune, Balewadi.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/111722351_30_04_2021_12_53_49.jpg','2021-04-30 07:18:26','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(23,'treatments-at-orthopedic-and-physiotherapy-centers','Treatments at orthopedic and physiotherapy centers','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','If you are resident of Pune and facing any orthopedic problem or you want any physiotherapy treatment then Dr. SumitZ Orthopedic and Physiotherapy cen...','<p>If you are resident of Pune and facing any <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/orthopaedic-treatment\">orthopedic problem</a> or you want any physiotherapy treatment then Dr. SumitZ Orthopedic and Physiotherapy center is the place you have to visit. They have all the treatment for your orthopedic issues. Dr. SumitZ Clinic is taking proper care of sanitization and following all the protocols issues by the Govt. Below we are mentioning the facilities you will get at orthopedic and physiotherapy center in Dr. SumitZ Clinic, Baner, balewadi.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Treatments you get at Dr.SumitZ Clinic, Baner , Balewadi</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Orthopedic Treatment:-</strong>Dr. Sumitz Clinic provides effective orthopedic treatment to its patients with the expert team of doctors dedicated to the diagnosis, prevention and treatment of disorders of joints, ligaments, bones, muscles and tendons. Sumitz Clinic provides orthopedic counseling for all types of muscle problems such as the spine, hip, shoulder, knee, neck, back and ankle. Here you will get treatment for disorders like tendons, muscles, joints and ligaments. Non-surgical interventions, spinal injections and other solutions are used to ensure the best and quickest recovery. You are offered with a complete plan covering physiotherapy, exercise, laser therapy, alternative medicine according to the needs of the patient to ensure long term recovery.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Orthopaedic Paedtriatic:-</strong>Orthopedic (S) is a branch of surgery involving conditions related to the musculoskeletal system. Orthopedic surgeons use both surgical and non-surgical instruments for the treatment of musculoskeletal trauma, spine diseases, sports injuries, degenerative diseases, infections, tumors, and congenital disorders.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>POST-OP Physical Therapy:-</strong>Sumitz is where you need to visit for <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/post-op-physical-therapy\">Quality Post-OP Therapy</a>. At every step, the professional team guides the patients and their families. If you are suffering from this problem then you need to contact Dr. Sumitz Clinic for your help.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Ergonomics:-</strong> There is a scientific discipline dealing with all these, with an understanding of the interactions between humans and other elements of a system, and businesses applying theory, data, and methods to optimize human welfare and overall system performance ergonomics. This normalizes work-life imbalances that save the patient&#39;s valuable time that is likely to be wasted due to ill health or surgery. This saves money by reducing hospital admission and surgery costs.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Knee Arthritis:-</strong>Arthritis is inflammation in the joints or part of the body where two bones come together. At Dr. SumitZ orthopedic and physiotherapy clinic, you are provided treatment for knee arthritis. Joints play a very important role in the movement of body parts. In a specific area, it is a condition that can be experienced in all parts of the body. The types are related to wear and tear of cartilage, such as inflammation associated with osteoarthritis that originates from the hyperactive immune system, such as rheumatoid arthritis.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>There are a lot other treatments provided by Dr. SumitZ Clinic such as Hip Arthritis, Sports Injuries treatments, Back and Neck Pain Treatment, Osteoporosis Treatment and others.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are facing any of these issues , <a href=\"\">contact Dr.SumitZ Clinic</a> which is the best orthodpedic in Baner.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/783317033_04_05_2021_04_01_47.jpg','2021-05-04 10:30:39','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(24,'healthy-nutrition-to-maintain-joints','Healthy Nutrition To Maintain Joints ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Do you know that your bones and joints remains healthy only when you eat clean healthy nutrition.\r\n\r\nOf course, there is no single food cure - all to...','<p>Do you know that your bones and joints remains healthy only when you eat clean healthy nutrition.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Of course, there is no single food cure - all to support joint health. Exercising, eating a balanced diet and generally taking care of yourself play an important role in moving your joints freely. Here are some foods to include in your diet.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Super Oatmeal</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Whole grains such as super oatmeal are associated with lower levels of inflammation. Refined grains such as white flour have the opposite effect.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>While work-out helps strengthen bones and muscles, it also puts pressure on the joints. Eating for exercise is not only about promoting activity, but also eating for recovery and healing. Instead of grabbing a pop-tart or biscuit with cheese and sausage, grab the oatmeal with fruits and nuts and yogurt.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Other Food Options:- Quinoa, Barley, Wheat bran, Granola and Brown Rice.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Curcuma</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Curcuma is a chief in Indian food. It is rich in a chemical called curcumin. One study found that extracts of curcumin work side-by-side with ibuprofen in reducing knee pain and pain. If you are not used to using Curcuma directly, then use curry powder; Curcuma is that which gives characteristic orange color.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Other Food options:- Cinnamon powder has anti-inflammatory properties which is good for health.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Hazelnuts</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Hazelnuts contain many nutrients that combat inflammation, including omega-3 fatty acids. Keep in mind that hazelnuts and other nuts are good for you, but they also contain a lot of calories; So limit yourself to a handful in a day.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Other Food Options:- Flax seeds are best as they also include Omega 3 acids.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Broccoli</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Broccoli and other green vegetables are rich in nutrients that are associated with joint health, including the antioxidant beta-carotene and vitamin C. These are an excellent source of calcium, which helps keep your bones strong.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Other food options:- Collard Greens</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Canned Salmon</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Salmon may not be the first food for strong bones, but nutritionist says that canned salmon with bones is particularly good to consider.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It contains calcium and vitamin D which helps in keeping your bones strong. Salmon also contains omega-3, which helps reduce inflammation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Substitutes:- Low or no-fat plain yogurt or milk, which has high amounts of both calcium and vitamin D. For omega-3s try other naturally oily fish, such as trout or sardines.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Overview Of Dr. SumitZ Clinic</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\">SumitZ</a> is one of the leading orthopedic and physiotherapy clinics in Pune and has been serving patients since 2006.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>We provide active, quality healthcare in a safe and comfortable environment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Your health is our first priority, and we make sure to meet all your needs on time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You are free to <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/contact-us\">contact us</a> anytime regarding any orthopaedic or physiotherapy doubts. We are happy to help you.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/93515923_26_05_2021_06_33_32.jpg','2021-05-26 13:01:16','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(25,'ways-to-protect-your-back','Ways to protect your back','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Back pain is one of the most common concerns for patients visiting their doctors. Most people will experience low back pain at some point in their lif...','<p>Back pain is one of the most common concerns for patients visiting their doctors. Most people will experience low back pain at some point in their lifetime. The causes vary - from acute sprains caused by injuries on the playground to long-term degenerative diseases caused by a variety of factors.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Follow these tips to keep your back healthy:-</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Strengthen your core muscles:-</strong>Your lower back is under tension to support your entire upper body. The muscles around your back need to be toned to support your spine and reduce pressure on your lower back. Our core muscles are rarely used during everyday activities, so they need to be toned through specific, targeted exercises. This can be accomplished through simple exercises that do not take too much time.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Stretch:-</strong>Many problems of back pain are due to tightness of muscles. If your back muscles are tight, they will put extra pressure on the entire spine, including the joints. Make a habit of daily stretches to boost your spinal health.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Avoid sitting in bad posture:-</strong>The discs in your lower spine are overloaded even more with poor sitting posture than standing. If you have to sit for long periods of time, get up and take an intermittent walk.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Walk:-</strong>Walking is very safe and good exercise. Brisk walking at work or outside will help you maintain an appropriate weight.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Lift correctly:-</strong>It is very easy to twist the wrong way which can lead to muscle cramps and pain. Use proper body mechanics and get help if the object is heavy.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Sleep well:-</strong>Sleeping on your back also puts pressure on your spine. Elevating the knees slightly by placing a pillow under them or lying on your side with a pillow between your knees helps reduce the pressure.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Watch your weight:-</strong>Excess weight puts pressure on your back. To compensate for the extra weight, the spine can become bent and disproportionately tense. The back may lose its proper support and develop an unnatural curvature of the spine over time.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Quit smoking:-</strong>Smoking restricts blood flow to the discs that cushion your vertebrae and can lead to accelerated disc degeneration. Smoking also reduces calcium absorption and new bone growth, which increases the risk of osteoporotic fractures.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Even with the best prevention, back injuries can occur and disrupt daily life to the point where intervention is necessary. The <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\">Dr. SumitZ Clinic</a> provides an integrated, multidisciplinary approach to orthopedic issues and also gives physiotherapy treatments. When surgery is necessary, highly experienced neurosurgical and orthopedic surgical teams are on hand with the most advanced technology to offer appropriate surgical treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So, if you are suffering from any orthopedic or physiotherapy issues, you can Contact Dr. SumitZ Clinic which is the best physiotherapy center in Baner.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/188247654_07_07_2021_10_25_20.jpg','2021-07-07 04:55:20','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(26,'best-exercises-for-a-full-back-workout','Best exercises for a full back workout','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Not only is the back one of the largest and strongest body parts in the body, it is also one of the most complex in terms of being a series of interco...','<p>Not only is the back one of the largest and strongest body parts in the body, it is also one of the most complex in terms of being a series of interconnected muscle groups. For the purposes of this feature, we&#39;re dividing the bench into its four main areas:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>Upper and outer latitudes</li>\r\n	<li>Lower Lats</li>\r\n	<li>Mid back</li>\r\n	<li>Lower back</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>Each area requires specific stimulation through the exercises and angles of attack used, and we&#39;ll show you the two best back exercises for each.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>With this menu you can customize your back workout by choosing one exercise from each category to create a total program. Or if one area is lagging, you can choose to have extracurricular activities only in that area. Either way, fully understanding which back exercises hit which parts of your back will allow you to build shape (especially the V-taper), thickness, and width.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Note:</strong>We do not isolate many of the exercises covered here, but instead emphasize certain areas of the back muscles.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>AREA 1: UPPER/OUTER LATS</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Use moves in which you use a wide grip, usually on the outside of your shoulders, to develop the area that makes up your V-taper. You will usually pull from an angle above your head or perpendicular to your body.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Best Exercises:</strong>Pullups (Wide Grip), Bent ower Barbell Row (Wide Grip)</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Pullup (Wide Grip)</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Grab the bar with an overhand grip. In the down position, fully extend your arms and relax your shoulders to stretch your lats.</li>\r\n	<li>As you pull up, imagine keeping your elbows out by your sides and pulling them down to lift yourself up while contracting your lats.</li>\r\n	<li>Pull yourself up as high as you can to fully stimulate your lats.</li>\r\n	<li>If you can&#39;t make it perfectly, consider enlisting the help of a spotter or using an assisted pull up machine.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Target Tip:</strong>To really emphasize the upper/external lats and tiers majors in the down position, squeeze your shoulder blades together as you fully extend your arms.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Bentover Barbell Row (Wide grip)</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Do not stand on a flat bench or platform to increase your range of motion; You&#39;re more likely to round your lower back in a downward motion. If you need more range of motion, use small plates to prop you off the floor instead of trying to balance yourself on a flat bench.</li>\r\n	<li>Using a wider-than-shoulder-width grip allows you to keep your elbows out by your sides and pull them as high as possible for a full contraction.</li>\r\n	<li>Keep your knees bent and stay in a bent position the entire time. It is easier to rise from this position when using heavy weights, but it recruits other muscle groups to assist in the move.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Targeting Tip:</strong>To target those outer lats and key areas, pull the bar toward your upper abs.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>AREA 2: Lower Lats</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Use reverse-grip moves and close-grip pullups/pulldowns to place more emphasis on the lower latitudinal region. One of the few single-joint lat moves, the straight-arm pulldown, does this as well.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Best exercises:</strong>Reverse-grip pulldowns, straight-arm lat pulldowns</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Reverse-Grip Pulldown</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Take an underhand, shoulder-width grip. This allows you to pull your elbows as far back as possible, maximally stimulating the back muscles.</li>\r\n	<li>Keep your torso straight and a small arch in your back as you extend your arms fully overhead. Keep your chest out and flexed throughout the move; This helps to focus more tension on the back muscles.</li>\r\n	<li>Pull your elbows down and back until the bar reaches your upper pecs. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the point of peak contraction.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Target Tip:</strong>To focus on those lower-latitude fibers, keep your chest high and your back arched. As you pull the bar down, bring it toward your lower chest for better contraction.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/251524557_07_07_2021_10_26_27.jpg','2021-07-07 04:56:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(27,'symptoms-that-shows-you-are-deficient-in-vitamin-d','symptoms that shows you are deficient in Vitamin D','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Vitamin D is a very important vitamin for our body to run smoothly. It is also called Sunshine Vitamin because the biggest source of this vitamin is t...','<p>Vitamin D is a very important vitamin for our body to run smoothly. It is also called Sunshine Vitamin because the biggest source of this vitamin is the rays coming from the sun. Unlike other <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments\">vitamins</a>, vitamin D acts like a hormone and affects every single cell in your body in one way or another. When your body is exposed to sunlight, then the cholesterol present in the body starts making vitamin D after coming in contact with sunlight. Apart from this, it also fulfills the deficiency of vitamin D in the body through a variety of foods such as fatty fish and some dairy products. However, it is very difficult to supply vitamin D through diet alone.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Due to these reasons there is a lack of vitamin D in the body</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are facing these symptoms, then you have lack of Vitamin D in your body. Check out:-</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Aging</li>\r\n	<li>Dairy producer and less fish</li>\r\n	<li>Being overweight</li>\r\n	<li>Distance from sunlight</li>\r\n	<li>Always use sunscreen</li>\r\n	<li>Always stay indoors</li>\r\n	<li>Having a dark skin tone.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Check Out The Symptoms &amp; Prevention linked given below</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Feeling tired all the time:-</strong>If there is a deficiency of Vitamin D in your body, then the biggest symptom of this is your feeling tired all the time. If you eat well and get enough sleep throughout the night, even after this, if you keep getting sleepy, then it can be a symptom of vitamin D deficiency.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Pain In Bones:-</strong>Vitamin D actually does the job of absorbing calcium in the body. In such a situation, if you drink plenty of milk and eat calcium-rich food, even after this there is a complaint of pain in the body, then the reason for this may be a lack of vitamin D. Actually, calcium is going into your body, but due to lack of vitamin D, the body is unable to absorb it inside itself.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Injury does not heal quickly:-</strong>If your injury does not heal for a long time, then it may also be due to vitamin D deficiency. Actually vitamin D helps in fighting infection and healing swelling etc. in the body. In such a situation, when there is a deficiency of vitamin D, then any injury takes more time to heal.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Feeling depressed and anxious all the time:-</strong>If you feel like depression and anxiety all the time and your mood is always bad, then this is also a symptom of vitamin D deficiency.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Hair Loss:-</strong>Generally, we attribute hair loss to shampoo, conditioner or food, but let us inform you that if there is a deficiency of vitamin D in the body, then your hair can fall rapidly. In such a situation, going in the sun is very important for your hair too.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>So, we hope that you must have know that how can you prevent the deficiency of Vitamin D now!</p>\r\n','uploads/product/407206091_06_08_2021_12_02_58.jpg','2021-08-06 06:32:58','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(28,'tips-for-synchronizing-work-station-office-chair','Tips for Synchronizing Work Station | office Chair ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','If you work a desk job that involves sitting for hours a day, it&#39;s important to pay attention to the health of your spine. Adequately supporting y...','<p>If you work a desk job that involves sitting for hours a day, it&#39;s important to pay attention to the health of your spine. Adequately supporting your spine and its surrounding tissues while sitting can put a lot of weight on your neck, back, and other joints. With recent advances in design and technology, it&#39;s easy to make new adjustments to your workstation. When you&#39;re seated, make sure you&#39;re doing everything possible to ensure the health of your spine by following these tips. &ldquo;Ergonomics Tips For Synchronizing Your Work Station and Office Chair&rdquo; is what this article is all about.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>1. Keep your upper arms parallel to your spine</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>When you sit at your desk, your upper arms should be comfortably placed connate to your spine and your forearms and hands should be resting on the work surface. At this point, your elbows should be bent at a 90-degree angle. If they are not, adjust your office chair up or down as needed.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Keeping your arms unusually high or low can put pressure on your shoulder joints and upper back, causing pain.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>2. Raise your chair to support your sit-to-stand movement</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If your seat is too low, you will over-bent your upper body when you try to get up, which puts increased stress on your hips, knees, and ankle joints. With extended use, the lower level seat will cause repeated stress and potential pain in these joints.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>3. Elevate your legs for support</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Sometimes, your chair or desk may be too high without an variable option. In such cases, consider using a footstool to support and rest your feet instead of hanging around all day.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Using a footstool will reduce the pressure on your feet and legs, which can reduce foot pain at the end of the day.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>4. Adjust your work surface to match your height</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are tall and have to constantly lean forward to type on your keyboard or read printed material, consider raising the height of your workstation or desk.<br />\r\nElevating your desk will allow you to raise your chair to a more appropriate height, which will reduce strain on your back.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>5. Measure your seat depth</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Your seat depth may not be something you think about, but having the right seat depth can make a difference in your back pain. Seat depth refers to the length between the back edge of your seat and the front edge.<br />\r\nTo check the proper seat depth, first, sit fully in your chair. Then, check the space between the front edge of your chair and your calves by making a fist and pushing on the calf by bringing it to the edge of the chair. If you can fit your full fist between the front edge of the chair and your calf, you probably have enough room for circulation. If not, your chair is likely too deep.<br />\r\nMoving the backrest of the chair, adding a cushion, pillow, or rolled-up towel to support your lower back, or changing your office chair are some possible solutions to this problem.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>6. Adjust the swivel and back support of your chair</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Your work chair should provide back support at an angle of 90&deg; or just behind it. Some chairs may have excessive swivel and recline options, which can be locked to prevent the chair from receding.<br />\r\nSome chairs also have lower back support with an adjustable band that can be moved up or down to fit the smaller of your back for added support.<br />\r\nMake these <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/ergonomics\">ergonomic</a> adjustments today to synchronize your workplace, office chair and your posture to help relieve unwanted stress on your spine and other joints. If you find yourself in the market to buy a new chair, consider the above tips and carefully study the height, width, depth, armrest, backrest, lumbar support and swivel of the seat.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/482996033_06_08_2021_12_41_48.jpg','2021-08-06 07:11:48','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(29,'physiotherapy-tips-for-faster-recovery-after-knee-surgery','Physiotherapy Tips for Faster Recovery after Knee Surgery','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','The most common questions asked by patients after knee surgery are, when will I get relief from pain? When can I start driving? Or what is the likely...','<p>The most common questions asked by patients after knee surgery are, when will I get relief from pain? When can I start driving? Or what is the likely time of full recovery? Etc.&nbsp; most patients take 6-12 weeks post-surgery to heal as it also depends on the type of surgery, whether you&rsquo;ve had an ACL reconstruction, minor arthroscopy, or knee replacement.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The 12 weeks following knee surgery are very crucial for healing and recovery because the risk of stiffness and loss of range of movement in the joint is maximized. To prevent you from such risk, your physiotherapist designs an exercise program that helps you in mobility, pacifies your pain, and also maintains your balance.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>As you begin to recover</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Commit yourself to an exercise plan to stay active in the first 3 weeks will help you heal faster. Given below are some of easy to do exercises for knee replacement that can be easily performed by patients:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Ankle Pumps:</strong> Lay straight on your back. Keep your knees extended, point your toes up so your sole feels flat then smoothly point your toes down. Hold your toes in each stretch for about 4-5 seconds. After completing one round return on your toes so that your foot is perpendicular to the ground.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Knee Press:</strong> Sit on your bed and keep your legs straight. Now keep a towel roll under your ankle, press it down by narrowing your thigh muscle, and hold it for 10 seconds each. Relax and repeat with another leg.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Straight Leg Raise:</strong> Lay straight on your back with a healthy leg bent and your foot should be flat on the surface, now tighten your thigh and lift your leg, do not bend your knee while lifting your leg. Repeat it with another leg.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Sitting Knee Extension:</strong> Sit straight in a chair and keep another chair in front. Put your involved leg gently on the chair, straighten your knee and hold for 10 seconds. Repeat with another leg.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Heel Raises:</strong> Stand straight while holding on to the supportive surface. Lift your both knees off the ground, hold for 10 seconds then gently come back to starting position. Repeat same exercise 4-5 times.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Knee bend:</strong> Sit straight in a chair now cross your healthy leg in front of your operated ankle, push your operated leg backward assist it with the bending of the knee. Hold it for 10 seconds and repeat it 2-3 times.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n','uploads/product/304897500_09_10_2021_03_10_03.webp','2021-10-07 13:19:30','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(30,'why-pehalwan-not-go-for-orthopedic-treatment','Why Pehalwan not go for Orthopedic Treatment','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','You have met or seen a lot of people getting treatment from Pehalwans or traditional healers. But is it really safe? The answer is simple and clear so...','<p>You have met or seen a lot of people getting treatment from Pehalwans or traditional healers. But is it really safe? The answer is simple and clear some of them get treated rightly and many of them end up exaggerating their case. I don&rsquo;t think it is right to take risks with your health and body, your life is not a Squid Game.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Orthopedic Treatment is related to bones which helps in everyday movement. With more than 200 bones in the human body, it demands specialty and utmost knowledge in this field.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It is a medical treatment that helps you in treating your injuries related to bones and joints. Here each area has specialty doctors often known as orthopedic subspecialists.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Some most common conditions that an orthopedist treats:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Joint Pain</li>\r\n	<li>Bone fracture</li>\r\n	<li>Neck pain that began after an injury</li>\r\n	<li>Moderate or advanced arthritis of the knee or hip</li>\r\n	<li>Carpel tunnel syndrome</li>\r\n	<li>Limb abnormalities, such as bowlegs and clubfoot</li>\r\n	<li>Soft tissue injuries, Etc.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Reasons why you should not see Pehalwan for Orthopedic Treatment :</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Unlike medical doctors, pehalwans use massages and oil to treat their injuries, which can result in disaster. Because injuries make your ligaments and bones more vulnerable which can exaggerate your pain. Medical doctors will work first to diagnose your condition then proceed with treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All orthopedists went through a lot of training and practice to further treat and obtain license unlike pehalwans. In addition to this, I also have written some very important reasons why orthopedics are better than pehalwans:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In non-surgical treatments orthopedists treat you by suggesting some easy exercises, unlike traditional healers they use massages and oils to treat your pain which could exaggerate your pain.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Repercussions of not seeking medical assistance at an early stage:</strong>\r\n\r\n	<p>According to a very senior doctor, traditional healers are not qualified enough to treat injuries and could worsen the problem and then doctors have to put in twice as much effort it needed earlier. Just in order to save money, you should never visit traditional healers for they can intensify your pain and could worsen your condition.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Proper Training And Qualifications:</strong>\r\n	<p>A lot of training and knowledge must be obtained in order to become an orthopedic surgeon. Whereas there is no such thing in the case of pehalwans or traditional healers. There is no way to tell if they genuinely have knowledge of the disease you&rsquo;re suffering from, which in turn could give you immense pain and could extend the time of your disease.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/specialists\">Surgical and Non-surgical Treatmen</a></strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/specialists\"><strong>t</strong></a>\r\n	<p>Often there are injuries that require surgical treatment especially if you are injured in the sports field or by indulging in some heavy physical activities. Some examples of operations done by orthopedic surgeons are- joint replacement, internal fixation, fusion, osteotomy, soft tissue repair, and other surgeries. Not all traditional healers know how to perform surgery and fix bones and joints.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are seeking an orthopedist for treatment, then Dr. Sumit is the best choice. You can check the<a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/contact-us\"> website</a> https://www.drsumitz.com for more information.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/360577381_23_10_2021_12_20_57.webp','2021-10-14 07:15:20','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(31,'How-to-Keep-Bones-Strong-Right-from-Childhood','How to Keep Bones Strong Right from Childhood | OrthoPediatrics advice?','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Diet, exercise, and proper nutrition parents take care of everything but often one thing that is overlooked by most of them is bone health. We don&rsq...','<p>Diet, exercise, and proper nutrition parents take care of everything but often one thing that is overlooked by most of them is bone health. We don&rsquo;t hear the term &lsquo;bone health&rsquo; that often!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A recent study shows many children in India are experiencing a deficiency in vitamin D that can lead to the impaired acquisition of bone mass, and it also shows that nearly 30% of children are getting their bones fractured before reaching adulthood. So it becomes very important to take care right from the very childhood.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Here are a few points why bone health is important and what measures you can take to protect your child&rsquo;s bone:</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Why childhood is such an important time for bone development?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Bones are the main component for the growth and structure of the body, it is living tissue that keeps changing with bits of old ones being replaced with new ones. During childhood and in puberty much more bone is deposited than withdrawn. So we much a healthy diet which can complete the requirements of the body.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&ldquo;Building your children&#39;s &ldquo;bone bank&rdquo; account is a lot like saving for their education: The more they can put away when they&#39;re young, the longer it should last as they get older&quot;.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You can adopt some simple lifestyle measures to maintain your child&rsquo;s bone health, read them below:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Include calcium in your child&rsquo;s diet</strong>:\r\n\r\n	<p>You must include sources that are rich in calcium like dairy products, almonds, broccoli, and soy products. As per the recommendations of a pediatrician and orthopedist, a toddler must have 600-700 mg of calcium a day. The recommendation increases to 1,000 milligrams (mg) of calcium a day in case of an adult</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Vitamin D</strong>\r\n	<p>Your health visitor, an orthopedist can advise you on vitamin D supplements for your child. Good sources of Vitamin D include fish, mushrooms, eggs, milk, and cereals all of these are rich in vitamin D. Sunlight also contributes to the body&rsquo;s production of vitamin D, but never expose your babies direct to sunlight as delicate skin can get sunburned.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong>Bone- strengthening Exercises for children</strong></p>\r\n\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li><strong><em>Babies who are not walking yet</em></strong>:\r\n\r\n		<p>They must be encouraged to play actively on the floor. Take them to parks and let them indulge in some physical activities.</p>\r\n		</li>\r\n		<li><strong><em>Children who can walk on their own</em></strong>:\r\n		<p>They should be physically active for at least 180 minutes throughout the day. Ask your health expert about more physical activities.</p>\r\n		</li>\r\n		<li><strong><em>Children aged 5 to 18:</em></strong>\r\n		<p>They just need to perform 60 minutes of physical activity daily. It will help them in lessening fatigue and boost their stamina.</p>\r\n		</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Eating Disorders and bone Health</strong>:\r\n	<p>Eating disorders affect all people despite their age group. You need to maintain a healthy diet in order to maintain your weight epically girls during their teenage years, as their bones are still growing and strengthening as eating disorders can affect their growth. So it is very important to keep your diet healthy during the teenage year.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>You can always consult your doctor for information regarding bone health or you can ask <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/contact-us\">Dr. Sumit </a>for the best advice.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/204731775_16_10_2021_02_31_30.webp','2021-10-16 07:49:14','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(32,'physiotherapy-helps-muscle-strains','Physiotherapy helps Muscle Strains','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Physiotherapy helps Muscle Strains\r\n\r\nMuscle strains are something that can happen to anyone at any time. Every year thousands of patients rely on Phy...','<h2><strong>Physiotherapy helps Muscle Strains</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Muscle strains are something that can happen to anyone at any time. Every year thousands of patients rely on Physiotherapists to overcome injuries, alleviate pain. But still there lingers a confusion about how physiotherapy actually works and how effective it is in case of muscle strain.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Let&rsquo;s look at some ways and understand how effectively it works.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Common Location for <strong>Muscle Strains</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Although muscle strains can occur anywhere in the body of course some parts are more vulnerable than others, like in our lower body hamstring, quadriceps, calf, and groin muscles, and in our upper body, the most vulnerable areas are the biceps and the rotator cuff.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>How Does <strong>Physiotherapy Works</strong> for an Injury?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Physiotherapy starts with an assessment, basically, how did you get that injury or muscle pain and afterward examining to check the severity level. Muscles strains are segregated on the basis of degree level 1st, 2nd, and 3rd, it is necessary to establish a treatment plan.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>After a thorough examination of the injury, your physiotherapists will create a treatment plan to address the severity of the injury and long- term recovery plan to avoid any reoccurrence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The physiotherapist will then start your treatment by choosing the method that suits best your injury. Some common methods used by physiotherapists for muscle pain are:</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/tips-to-help-keep-your-bones-strong\">Learn more </a>about how to keep bones healthy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Heat and Ice</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>This method is useful in terms of alleviating pain and swelling, by heating up the tissue blood flow is increased in the area which helps in reducing pain, and the icing is proven to decrease inflammation and swelling.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Therapeutic Taping</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are several times when physiotherapist uses Tapes to help patient get back to full speed. Because Tape provides compression and support and can also help in relaxing the affected muscles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Stretching &amp; Exercises</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Muscle tightness likely occurs after an injury that affects the muscle&rsquo;s ability to move. By assisting in exercises and stretching that are beneficial for your exercises, because stretching and exercises help in loosening the muscle and in regaining mobility.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Strengthening Exercises</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The most crucial part is re-gain the same strength and ensuring muscle safety at the same time. The physiotherapist directs and assists you in strengthening exercises and ensures safe progress of healing. Eventually, all these exercises will help you gain strength and mobility and you will get back to work sooner. For more help, you can always contact Dr. Sumit, who is an experienced physiotherapist.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For more information visit our <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/about-us\">website</a> or <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/contact-us\">contact us.</a></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n','uploads/product/301701676_22_11_2021_11_17_22.jpeg','2021-11-20 13:50:30','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(33,'how-to-eat-healthy-while-staying-away-from-home-what-nutritionist-suggests','How to eat Healthy while staying away from home? What Nutritionist suggests.','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','We all are easily tempted by fast food especially when there are so many tasty options available and everyone around you is chowing down on that food....','<p>We all are easily tempted by fast food especially when there are so many tasty options available and everyone around you is chowing down on that food. I know it is not possible to ignore and control those screaming urges inside your head, each time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>But eating too much fast food can bring your body down and lead to several consequences like mental functioning, emotional well-being, energy, strength, and especially weight.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So, what to do? I would say choose! Like, choose the food with fewer calories for example: instead of eating pizza go for a grilled chicken sandwich or salad, come on salads are tasty too!</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Here are some tips that help in making a wise choice.</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Following are some that you must keep in mind.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Go for balance:</strong>\r\n\r\n	<p>Eat meals that contain a balance of lean proteins like add veggies and fruits, whole grains (like whole-wheat bread &amp; brown rice), and if you are a non-vegetarian add fish and chicken.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Watch portion sizes:</strong>\r\n	<p>Average people tend to eat double or triple whenever eating at a party or restaurant, which is unhealthy for an obvious reason.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Drink water or low-fat milk:</strong>\r\n	<p>Avoid regular sodas, soft drinks, sweet teas, juices, and any other sugary drinks.</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Tips for eating at a Restaurant</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Here are some restaurant tips:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Generally, restaurant portions are bigger than what we usually eat. Go for half portions or share it with your friend.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Use salsa and mustard oil instead of mayonnaise or oil.</li>\r\n	<li>Choose no fat or low-fat milk instead of shakes.</li>\r\n	<li>Order baked, broiled, or grilled (not fried) lean meats including turkey, chicken, seafood, or steak.</li>\r\n	<li>Choose fresh fruit instead of high-calorie-oriented Desserts.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>But still, if you crave something unhealthy try to eat a smaller portion or try to share it with a friend. Don&#39;t put off eating until you&#39;re so hungry you could inhale everything in sight. Set a time to eat, then stop what you&#39;re doing to take a break, sit down, and savor the food you are eating.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All these tips will help you strengthen your bones and help in leading a healthy life. For more tips on how to keep your bones and joints healthy click on this <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/healthy-nutrition-to-maintain-joints\">link</a> and find out.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you need more help from a nutritionist or pediatrics then <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/specialists\">contact </a>Dr. Pradnya Jagtap. For more information visit&nbsp;https://www.drsumitz.com&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/261963328_22_11_2021_02_36_02.png','2021-11-22 07:21:24','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(34,'tips-to-keep-your-knees-healthy-as-you-age','Tips to keep your knees Healthy as you Age','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Knees are most prone to injuries, like it is said people of all ages have faced some kind of knee pain. Being the largest joint in the Human Body, it...','<p>Knees are most prone to injuries, like it is said people of all ages have faced some kind of knee pain. Being the largest joint in the Human Body, it is used heavily in jogging, running, climbing and jumping and thus exposed to pain and injuries. When this happens, you must see an orthopaedic because normal wear and tear of tissues is inevitable but at least we can get proper treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Maintain a healthy weight</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Excess weight places tremendous pressure on your knees. For every extra weight you put on, the knees will have four times more pressure on them. So, it became very important to maintain a healthy diet especially if you are ageing. If you want to learn about how to maintain a healthy diet then click on this <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/how-to-eat-healthy-while-staying-away-from-home-what-nutritionist-suggests\">link.</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Keep Moving</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Indulge yourself in some physical activities regularly it helps in maintaining joint function along with strength and range of motion in the knees. It is always better to warm up before any activity like running or jumping it will prevent strains. And if you don&rsquo;t run on successive days, try to run every other day.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Strengthen the muscles that support your knees</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Developing strong thigh muscles- especially the quadriceps, hamstring and abductors improves your range of motion. A professor at the University of Montana School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences said, doing squats and lunges twice a week will strengthen and protect your knees. For more, you can always take the help of<a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/specialists/dr-varun-agrawal\"> Dr. Varun</a>, he holds expertise in this field.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Perfect your Posture</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>People often slouch and get more stopped as they get older, which is an unhealthy lifestyle. Because poor posture puts additional stress on the muscles especially on your knees and hips. Perform core strengthening exercises such as planks and back extensions that will help in improving postures and prevent irritation under and around the kneecaps, and help you avoid falling.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Choose the right Shoes</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>An assistant professor of orthopaedic surgery at the University of Cincinnati says that wearing comfortable shoes promotes proper alignment of the joints in your lower extremities. And if you are purchasing shoes for exercise, try buying the one that is exclusively made for exercising and running and the second thing is to try avoiding wearing it whenever you can because it puts extra pressure on your knees.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For more help related to bones and muscles, or if you need any help from a Physiotherapist or Orthopaedic. Visit our<a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"> website </a>or <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/contact-us\">contact</a> us, we are happy to help you always!</p>\r\n','uploads/product/162040124_22_11_2021_03_00_20.png','2021-11-22 08:03:24','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(35,'best-orthopedic-physiotherapists-in-baner-pune','Best Orthopedic & Physiotherapists in Baner, Pune','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Orthopedics\r\n\r\nOrthopedics is a branch of medicine concerned with injuries, and diseases related to muscles, joints, ligaments, tendons, or nerves. Or...','<h2>Orthopedics</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopedic-doctor-in-pune\">Orthopedics</a> is a branch of medicine concerned with injuries, and diseases related to muscles, joints, ligaments, tendons, or nerves. Orthopedists are educated in the workings of the musculoskeletal system, which includes (but is not limited to) diagnosing a condition or disorder, identifying and treating an injury, providing rehabilitation to an affected area or function, and establishing prevention protocol to inhibit further damage to a diseased area.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Some of the Best orthopedics in Baner are:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/specialists/dr-varun-agrawal\"><strong>Dr. Varun Agarwal</strong></a></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Orthopedic, Baner, Pune</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dr. Varun Agarwal has been working as a Joint Replacement Surgeon for more than a decade. He completed his fellowship under Dr. Narendra Vaidya at Lokmanya Group of Hospitals, Pune. He is currently working in <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services\">Dr. Sumitz Hospit</a>al in<strong> Orthopedic Department</strong>. His specialties are Primary and<strong> Joint Replacement Surgery</strong>, Simple and Complicated Trauma Surgery.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>He has handled more than one thousand replacement surgeries including<a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/physiotherapy-tips-for-faster-recovery-after-knee-surgery\"> knee,</a> hip, shoulder, and elbow along with this he has also performed and assisted in several trauma cases including extra-articular fractures, intra-articular fractures, comminuted fractures, malunions, non-unions, implant failures, hand surgeries.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Dr. Ashish Ranade</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Orthopedic, Baner, Pune</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/specialists/dr-ashish-ranade\">Dr. Ashish Ranade</a> is one of the finest orthopedics in Baner, Pune. He is an MBBS, Master of Surgery in Orthopedics, and MRCS from a renowned Institution. With more than 20 years of experience, he has been treating patients and performing complex surgeries. He worked in different countries like U.S and U.K. His work experiences are:</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Highlights</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Worked as an Instructor in orthopedics at the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences - Little Rock, AR, USA.</li>\r\n	<li>Worked at Shriners Hospital for children, Philadelphia, PA, USA</li>\r\n	<li>Worked at Shriners/St. Christopher&rsquo;s Hospital - Philadelphia, PA, USA</li>\r\n	<li>Worked at Sinai Hospital, Baltimore, MD</li>\r\n	<li>Worked at Frenchay &amp; Southmead Hospitals - Bristol, UK</li>\r\n	<li>Worked at Yeovil District Hospital - Yeovil, UK</li>\r\n	<li>Worked as Senior house officer at Weston General Hospital - Weston-super-mare, UK</li>\r\n	<li>Worked at Whittington Hospital - London, UK</li>\r\n	<li>Worked at B V Medical College and Hospital - Pune</li>\r\n	<li>Worked at DYP Medical College and Hospital - Pune</li>\r\n	<li>Worked at Bhide Hospital - Pune</li>\r\n	<li>Worked at Sassoon General Hospitals in BJ Medical College &ndash; Pune</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Physiotherapy</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-treatment\">Physiotherapy</a> is a science-based profession that involves exercise, therapy, and different medications in treatment. It basically helps in injury, illness, and any disability. Furthermore, I have suggested <strong>physiotherapists based in Baner</strong>, Pune. You can always contact him.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Dr. Sumit</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<h3>Physiotherapist, Baner, Pune</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/specialists\">Dr. Sumit Gupta</a> is a renowned Physiotherapist, based in Pune with experience of over 17 years. He has completed his B.PTH from Maharashtra University of Health Sciences F.O.R. from Apollo Hospital, Hyderabad.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>His area of expertise lies in Myotherapy, Electrical Stimulation, <strong>Orthopaedic Physiotherapy</strong>, Taping, and Cryotherapy/Cold Therapy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The above listed are the best orthopedics and physiotherapists based in Baner, Pune. You can visit anytime or simply book your appointment via contact us. For more information, you can follow us on Instagram and Facebook.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/62178757_15_12_2021_02_46_59.jpeg','2021-12-08 11:54:59','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(36,'exercises-to-ease-arthritis-pain-and-stiffness','Exercises to ease arthritis pain and stiffness.','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','What is Arthritis Pain?\r\n\r\nIn layman&#39;s terms, Arthritis is basically a common disorder that affects your joints. The major symptoms of arthritis a...','<h2>What is Arthritis Pain?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>In layman&#39;s terms, <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/hip-arthritis\">Arthritis</a> is basically a common disorder that affects your joints. The major symptoms of arthritis are joint pain and stiffness. This causes pain and inflammation and reduces the flexibility of joints.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are many types of arthritis. Each type has different symptoms and needs different sorts of<a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments\"> treatment</a>. Earlier it was found in old age people but nowadays it can develop in men, women, and children at any age.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Arthritis disease is commonly found in the following body parts of humans &ndash;</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>Feet</li>\r\n	<li>Hands</li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/hip-arthritis\">Hips</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/knee-arthritis\">Knees</a></li>\r\n	<li>Lower back</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>How is arthritis treated?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>As such, there is no cure for arthritis, but there are treatments that can help to improve the condition as it was earlier. A treatment plan will depend on how severe arthritis is, its symptoms, and your body condition. Dr. Ashish Ranade is the best doctor you can consult anytime.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Some common non-surgical treatments include:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Medication: </strong>Anti-inflammatory and pain medications help to relieve arthritis symptoms. Some medications, called biologics, basically target the immune system&rsquo;s inflammatory response.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Physical therapy: </strong>Rehabilitation can help improve overall strength, range of motion, and overall mobility.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Best exercises for arthritis</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>These are some exercises that help in treating arthritis and provide relief from stiffness &amp; Pain.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>1. Stretching</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The first and most common exercise is stretching which helps in improving flexibility and range of motion and also reduces stiffness up to some extent. So we can say that it&rsquo;s the most common but plays important role in curing it.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The stretching<a href=\"https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/stretching-routine\">&nbsp;</a>routine may be as follows:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Should warm up by walking or jogging in place or pumping the arms while sitting or standing for at least 5 minutes.</li>\r\n	<li>Should hold each stretch for 20&ndash;30 seconds before releasing it.</li>\r\n	<li>Should repeat each stretch at least 2&ndash;3 times. Resistance bands can also help in maintaining good form.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>2. Walking</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Walking or jogging is a low-impact form of exercise that helps&nbsp;with aerobic conditioning, heart basically cardiovascular health, and joint health.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It is essential to wear proper and good quality shoes and stay hydrated,&nbsp;even if the walking is not so extreme. A person should start a walking routine on flat, even surfaces before progressing to uphill, downhill, or uneven surfaces.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>3. Flowing movements, such as tai chi and yoga</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Both tai chi&nbsp;and yoga are combinations of deep breathing, flowing movements, gentle poses, and meditation. They increase flexibility, and balance which also results in reducing stress and anxiety.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Now a day&rsquo;s it&rsquo;s to find free online videos or apps like Gaia for tai chi or yoga workouts, including some yoga workouts.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>5. Water exercises</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Water helps our body weight&nbsp;by minimizing gravity, which states that exercises done in water do not have an extreme impact on muscles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Swimming, water aerobics, and other gentle water exercises increase<a href=\"https://www.arthritis.org/health-wellness/healthy-living/physical-activity/other-activities/best-exercises-for-rheumatoid-arthritis\">&nbsp;</a>flexibility, range of motion, strength, and aerobic condition which can result in reducing joint stress and stiffness.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>More studies on the benefits of water exercises on RA are needed.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>6. Cycling</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>It is important to keep the heart as healthy as possible. Cycling can help improve cardiovascular health.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Riding a cycle can be a way to get the joints moving and improve cardiovascular fitness. A person can also ride their bike outdoors to get fresh air.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Along with that cycling can reduce&nbsp;stiffness, increase range of motion and leg strength, and build endurance.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>7. Strength training</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Strengthening the muscles around the affected joints helps in maintaining strength and muscle mass. In that case resistance band is a way to challenge the body and build muscle over time.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>8. Hand exercises</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Arthritis can sometimes lead to limited use of the hands. A person with RA may lose their grip strength or find that they are dropping things because of lack of gripping strength.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Bending the wrists up and down, slowly curling the fingers, spreading the fingers wide on a table, and squeezing a stress ball can help&nbsp;increase strength and flexibility in the hands.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you want to read more articles then check out our <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\">website</a>, you can also book a session and <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/contact-us\">fix an appointment.</a> We are happy to help you!</p>\r\n','uploads/product/977803145_15_12_2021_02_17_37.jpeg','2021-12-15 07:37:39','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(37,'ways-to-prevent-neck-pain-back-caused-by-using-mobile-phone','Ways to prevent Neck pain & Back caused by using mobile phone','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Change Your Life, Change Your Habits\r\n\r\n-Anonymous\r\n\r\nNowadays, most of us are glued to smartphones. And even though they can help us be more producti...','<p><em>Change Your Life, Change Your Habits</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><em>-Anonymous</em></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Nowadays, most of us are glued to smartphones. And even though they can help us be more productive and enhance the quality of our lives, they can also be a major source of distraction.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Despite the amazing benefits, it&rsquo;s becoming more and more obvious that most people have no control over their smartphone use &mdash; negatively impacting their physical and mental health. Neck pain and back pain are some common problems that occur from overusing phones. Bad posture is often a major cause behind it.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Follow these steps if are continuously facing Neck Pain &amp; Back Pain, these measures will help in providing some relief:</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Ways to Prevent Neck Pain and Back Pain caused by mobile phones</h2>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Straighten up</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Maintaining an upright posture and proper neck alignment will decrease the load and the amount of work our neck and shoulder muscles have to do in order to keep our heads up.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Look Forward</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Bring the device up to eye level. This will minimize the bend in your neck and maintain optimal spine posture. If your device is below eye level, look down with your eyes rather than your neck.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Posture Check</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Make an effort to maintain the curve in your low back when sitting and using your device. If you need to use your device for a long period of time, try to find a supportive chair and a surface to rest your arms on <strong>Break Time</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Take frequent micro-breaks to move/stretch your neck and back. Limit your device use to 20-minute sessions. Consider making a phone call rather than spending long-time texting.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Tips to Decrease your Screen-Time</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;<strong>Turn Off Your Notifications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>One of the easiest changes to regain control over your focus is to turn the notifications from email, instant messaging, and other apps off. Notifications and alerts are made to pull your attention away from what you are doing so you grab your phone again.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Therefore, at the bare minimum, make sure your alerts and notifications are off when you&rsquo;re working on your most important tasks. This way, you can direct all of your focus and energy towards working productively.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Change the Location of Your Apps</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>In many cases, I find myself on certain apps without even realizing it. This shows how automatic my phone use is. Often, it&rsquo;s not a conscious decision to visit a specific app, but rather a habitual, automatic motion.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>One way to counter this is by regularly changing the location of your apps. In the first few days, you&rsquo;ll probably click where the app used to be. This only shows you how much of an automatic habit most of our smartphone use is.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Calm Your Mind</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dopamine when releases into the brain, a chemical that creates feelings of pleasure. It&#39;s an essential part of our brain&#39;s rewards system, which is why it&#39;s also gets blamed for addiction.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Meditation, yoga, exercise, and other mindfulness activities have been proven to create a natural release of dopamine, reducing&nbsp;the craving from the dopamine rushes your phone provides.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Never ignore conditions like Neck Pain and Back Pain, in long term, it will exaggerate and not only decrease your productivity but also severely impact your health negatively. If are dealing with these problems then you can always visit us or book a session via<a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/contact-us\"><strong> contact us.</strong></a> For information follow us on Instagram and <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/drsumitz/\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a>.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/652901407_27_12_2021_03_33_01.jpeg','2021-12-23 09:22:14','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(38,'arthritis-everything-you-need-to-know','Arthritis: Everything you need to know!','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Arthritis is a disease that is commonly found in people around us, and its impact has diversified from elderly to youngsters. Generally, arthritis occ...','<p>Arthritis is a disease that is commonly found in people around us, and its impact has diversified from elderly to youngsters. Generally, arthritis occurs out of the normal wear tear of cartilage which leads to joint pain. Joint pain can be an early symptom of arthritis which is quite common in youngsters and is a cause to worry.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>An inactive lifestyle, deskbound work activities, extended duration of sitting on the computer, less exposure to sunlight, and deficiency of essential vitamins, most importantly rising obesity amongst the young population is giving rise to arthritis.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Most Common <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/arthritis-everything-you-need-to-know\">Types of Arthritis</a></strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Do you know that there are more than 100 types of arthritis? But some of the most common <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/arthritis-everything-you-need-to-know\"><strong>types of arthritis forms</strong></a>, what they are, what happens, and their symptoms are listed below:</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Osteoarthritis</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Osteoarthritis commonly affects the body parts that bear our pain like the knee, joints, spine, and hips. It gradually increases over months or years. Generally, your affected joint starts to hurt. But you don&rsquo;t feel fatigued which comes with some other types of arthritis.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>Symptoms</em></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Deep, aching pain.</li>\r\n	<li>Pain while walking.</li>\r\n	<li>Stiffness after resting.</li>\r\n	<li>Morning stiffness that lasts less than 30 minutes.</li>\r\n	<li>Your joint may be swollen or hard to move.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/arthritis-everything-you-need-to-know\"><strong>Rheumatoid Arthritis</strong></a></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>RA attacks your immune system especially joints as it is an autoimmune disease. In several cases, RA leads to inflammation, which might cause severe damage to joints if not treated. Many people who are suffering from this, get lumps on their skin called rheumatoid nodules.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><em>Symptoms</em></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Severe pain, Stiffness, and swelling</li>\r\n	<li>More than one swollen Joint.</li>\r\n	<li>The asymmetrical pattern of knuckles</li>\r\n	<li>Morning Stiffness</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Psoriatic Arthritis</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>People with this arthritis generally have inflammation of the skin and joints. In addition, commonly it is seen in people ages between 30 to 50, but there are fair chances of it happening in childhood.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Psoriatic arthritis can swell the fingers and toes also these people have fingernails that are pitted or discolored.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>We have treatment for each <strong>type of arthritis</strong>&nbsp;and get the best treatment from experienced doctors.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Some Safe Exercises: -</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Since Arthritis most affects knees and joints as it bears the maximum pain, knee problems are very common. But it is crucial to stay active to strengthen the supporting muscles and to prevent any diseases from getting worse. Here is a list of some safe exercises that you can perform without anyone&rsquo;s help:</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Walk Often</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Walking is a perfect low-impact exercise that can help you with mobility and also does not require any equipment. Start with what you can handle and gradually build up to 20-30 minutes a day.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Warm-up &amp; Stretch</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Stretching and warming is such crucial elements before you jump into exercising. Take a few steps and walk slowly, stretch your arms and legs gently. This will reduce your discomfort along with warming up your muscles.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Don&rsquo;t exercise on hard surfaces</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Whenever you are going for a walk prefer grass or a dirt path as these paths are softer than concrete or asphalt lack shock absorption and thus increase pressure on knees. Focus on Shock Absorption.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You can also see <strong>our</strong> <strong>physiotherapist</strong> for more safe exercises that will help in elevating your pain.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A worrying factor is the increasing occurrence of arthritis among women. In urban India, women are increasingly shouldering the dual responsibility of homemaker as well as professional. Therefore, they are increasingly getting exposed to new risks due to a lack of time and motivation. Therefore, awareness is a must.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Although if one is diagnosed with arthritis, he/she can still exercise as mobility is one of the key factors in the management of arthritis and should be done under the proper guidance of an expert. you can always <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/contact-us\"><strong>consult us</strong></a>. For more information follow us on <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/drsumitz/\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a> and Facebook.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/435337419_08_01_2022_04_20_15.jpeg','2022-01-08 09:36:40','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(39,'5-awesome-benefits-of-jogging','5 Awesome  Benefits of Jogging','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Everyone is well aware that regular exercise has a significant impact on our overall well-being. The type of exercise that we are engaged in can bring...','<p>Everyone is well aware that regular exercise has a significant impact on our overall well-being. The type of exercise that we are engaged in can bring about its own unique set of benefits. The <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/benefits-of-jogging-for-your-health\"><strong>specific benefits associated with regular jogging</strong></a> are as below &ndash;</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/exercises-to-get-your-hips-in-shape\">Helps in Weight Loss</a><strong> </strong>&ndash; </strong>Jogging basically boosts metabolism and burns approx. 300 calories in 30 minutes. A healthy diet along with regular jogging will melt those extra inches that you have always wanted to shed. It not only burns fat but also helps in maintaining weight. But in this case a simple calculation of maintenance calories played an important where a person has be in calorie deficit in accordance to his maintenance calories. By doing this body will begin to break down body fat to supply the body with a continuous stream of energy. While nutrition will play a large role in a negative energy balance, exercises like jogging will burn a significant number of calories and consequently contribute to weight loss.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Helps in improving bone strength - </strong>Jogging maintains bone health. When you begin jogging, the bones experience some amount of stress and load. Jogging prepares the bones to bear this additional stress which it starts to endure on a regular basis. Jogging strengthens the bones and prevents bone trauma and injuries.&nbsp;It improves bone thickness and wards off problems like osteoporosis, osteoarthritis and rheumatoid arthritis. It also makes the bones of the hip and the spine stronger.</li>\r\n	<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/how-to-improve-posture-for-a-straight-healthy-back\">Helps in developing muscles</a> - </strong>Jogging helps body to become more toned and sharp. It works on the large muscles like - hamstrings, calf etc. There are a number of muscles that must constantly contract in order to bring about the movements required for jogging. The muscles of the lower extremities such as the glutes, quads, hamstrings, and calves are primarily responsible for bringing about motion. Increasing the strength of the muscles will have a positive impact on how you move and your risk of injury.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Keeps the Mind Healthy - </strong>Jogging plays a major role in improving the mental health of the person. When you jog, your body releases hormones called endorphins that help lift your spirit and make you feel positive about yourself. And that is why you feel calm and rejuvenated after jogging.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Good for our Heart - </strong>Jogging is one of the best cardiovascular activity that boosts the health of your heart. Jogging ensures that blood is pumped faster to the heart and, thus, maintains blood pressure. Cholesterol and blood glucose levels are also under control.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>When you exercise, the body responds with the demands of the exercise by increasing heart rate and breathing rate. The purpose of doing so is to continually provide the working muscles with oxygen-rich blood that they can use for energy. This increase will also allow for the removal of waste products from the body such as carbon dioxide.<br />\r\nBy regularly jogging, the strength and function of the<strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopaedic-center\"> cardiovascular system </a></strong>become more efficient.</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li><strong>Boosts the Respiratory system &ndash; </strong>Just like any&nbsp;other aerobic workout, jogging enhances the lung capacity and strengthens the muscles of the respiratory system. This ensures that the lungs take in more oxygen and efficiently remove carbon dioxide. Jogging, thus, improves the endurance of the<strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/ways-to-prevent-neck-pain-back-caused-by-using-mobile-phone\"> respiratory muscles</a></strong>.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Prevents from Communicable Diseases</strong> - Jogging is known to stimulate the production of lymphocytes and macrophages that combat infection in the body. It helps to fight viral infections like flu and common cold and also some bacterial infections. Regular exercise contributes towards strong muscles and bones and therefore, the risk of developing a muscle and bone wasting disease is also reduced.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Curbs Mental Stress</strong> - It reduces stress and tension and also clears the mind of unnecessary thoughts. Jogging has a positive impact on people and changes their attitudes and outlook for the better. Research has consistently indicated that aerobic exercises can significantly boost one&rsquo;s mental health and prevent the development of mental health illness. For those who do struggle with a mental health illness, such as depression and anxiety, jogging can help to reduce the symptoms.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n','uploads/product/726821602_18_01_2022_03_29_25.jpeg','2022-01-13 07:48:14','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(40,'joint-pain-preventions-treatments','Joint Pain: Preventions & Treatments','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Your bones connect to your joints through your joints. The bones of your skeleton can move with the joints. There are several types of joints:\r\n\r\nShou...','<p>Your bones connect to your joints through your joints. The bones of your skeleton can move with the joints. There are several types of joints:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Shoulders</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hips</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Forearms</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Knees</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Joint pain can refer to pain, aches, and discomfort in any one of the body&rsquo;s joints. Joint pain is a common problem. It does not usually require a hospital stay.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sometimes, joint discomfort is due to an injury or illness. Arthritis is another common cause of joint pain. It could also be caused or exacerbated by other conditions.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What causes pain in the joints?</h2>\r\n\r\n<h2>Arthritis: -</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>It is the leading cause of joint pain. Osteoarthritis (OA), and rheumatoid (RA) are the main types of arthritis. According to research OA is most common among adults over 40 years old. It is slow-growing and can affect common joints such as the: Hands, Hips &amp; Knees etc. OA causes joint pain by causing a loss of cartilage, which acts as a shock absorber and cushion for the joints. RA is the second type of arthritis. The Arthritis Foundation estimates that RA affects approximately 1.5 million Americans. It is more common in women than it is in men.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Over time, it can cause deformities and disability to the joints, as the body&rsquo;s immune system attacks and damages the membranes that line the joints, RA can cause pain, inflammation, fluid buildup, and joint damage.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Other causes: -</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>You can cause joint pain by: Bursitis is an inflammation of the cushions around joints that is lupus &amp; gout. Certain infectious diseases such as hepatitis, influenza and measles can be transmitted. Chondromalacia (or degeneration of the cartilage in your kneecap) is known as chondromalacia.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If we talk about overuse of a joint pain that is Cancer, fibromyalgia, osteoporosis, sarcoidosis &amp; rickets.</p>\r\n\r\n<h1>What are the symptoms and causes of joint pains?</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>You may need to see a doctor for your joint pain in some cases, if you have any questions about your pain or if you experience other symptoms that are not related to it, make an appointment. Also, you should see a doctor if the following are happening with you:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The area around the joints is swollen and red. The pain continues for at least 3 days. There are no symptoms other than a fever. If any of the above occurs, you should go to the emergency rooms. You have suffered a serious accident. The joint appears to have deformed. It is sudden to experience swelling in the joint. The joint is completely immobile. You are experiencing severe joint pain then firstly make an appointment at Dr. Sumitz clinic.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Joint Pain diagnoses sand treatment</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The doctor will most likely perform a physical examination. The doctor may also ask questions about your symptoms and joint pain. This could help you narrow down potential causes. For the diagnosis of arthritis-related joint pain, it may be necessary for a joint X-ray to be taken. If the doctor suspects that there may be another cause, they may order blood tests to test for certain autoimmune disorders. To determine the level of inflammation, they may request a sedimentation rate or complete blood count.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Joint Pain Management</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Home treatment: Both OA &amp; RA are considered chronic conditions by doctors. There is no cure for arthritis. However, there are some ways to manage the pain. It might be beneficial to use topical painkillers or to take nonsteroidal, anti-inflammatory drugs to reduce inflammation, swelling and pain. Maintain a healthy lifestyle and engage in moderate exercise. Stretch before exercising in order to keep your joints healthy. Maintain a healthy body weight. This will lower stress on the joints. If you are not experiencing pain due to arthritis, it is possible to try taking a nonprescription, anti-inflammatory drug, getting massaged, taking a warm tub, stretching regularly, and getting enough sleep.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Medical treatment: Your treatment options depend on the reason for the pain. In certain cases, your doctor may have to draw fluid from the joint in order to determine, if there is a problem. You might be recommended to have the joint replaced. Lifestyle changes and medication can also help RA go into remission. Your doctor will first address inflammation. Once RA has gone into remission your doctor will prescribe medical treatment that focuses on controlling your condition to prevent flareups.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For more information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-clinic\"><strong>Best Physiotherapy Clinic in Pune</strong></a> and follow us on Facebook and Instagram.&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/372375031_01_02_2022_03_03_15.jpeg','2022-01-31 07:19:34','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(41,'connection-between-your-mental-health-and-joint-health','Connection Between your Mental Health and Joint Health','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Joint Pain is often related to injuries or sometimes aging factor plays a role. There is another factor that is often overlooked by people that is men...','<p>Joint Pain is often related to injuries or sometimes aging factor plays a role. There is another factor that is often overlooked by people that is mental health issues. Yes, you heard that right!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Your mental health and physical health are closely connected. Depression, Anxiety, chronic stress, and other emotional disorders can make your physical health Imbalance. Even some studies have found that your physical health, chronic pain can be highly associated with a higher level of stress along with your increased level of cortisol, (cortisol is the stress hormone of the human body).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>No need to panic there are certain ways that you can control it. You just need to practice stress relief techniques and stress management methods.&nbsp; It will not only help you to manage your chronic pain but also help you with daily functions and mood.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Here are some effective ways, you can restore your mental health and ease your chronic pain:</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Stretch and Practice Yoga to Feel More Relaxed</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Yoga has been the most effective way to ease your mind and mental stress whereas stretching will help you eliminate joint pain because along with increasing your flexibility, it widens your range of motion. Practicing yoga stimulates blood flow to your muscles making you more active physically and mentally.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Also, normal body aches like neck pain and back pain are most likely to be eliminated if you are practicing yoga daily. Yoga is most importantly good for people with chronic stress, it makes you feel light and refreshed.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Meditate to Clear Your Mind</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Meditation is one of the best exercises that helps in clearing the mind and provides you peace internally. If you keep worrying about the future or get upset by something that had happened in the past. When you sit in a quiet room, you release pressure on yourself to complete tasks. That&rsquo;s why meditation is so important.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You can perform meditation by sitting alone in a room by humming, chanting, doing breathing exercises, yoga, or listening to a guided meditation. You can find a lot of free guided meditation audios on the internet that will enhance your meditation experience.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Massage Joints for Increased Blood Flow</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Massage is extremely helpful in eliminating joint pain, its benefits are both emotional and physical. For it increases your blood flow, releases muscle tension, and enhances mobility of joints.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Getting a massage makes a good impact on mental health too. You must take some time out to pamper yourself with some good massage.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Combine Mental &amp; Physical health</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Eliminating Stress is so important for joint pain. By performing stress relief techniques more often you&rsquo;ll more relaxed and calm. When your emotions are in a better state eventually you will feel better physically as well.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>And if you combine stress relief techniques with orthopedic treatments like physical therapy or surgery. Most likely, you feel a drastic change in your mental and physical activities. At Dr. Sumitz&#39;s clinic, you will find the best orthopedic surgeons and professionals for your physical therapy. Dr. Sumit is the best physiotherapist who has handled thousands of critical cases.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For consulting best Physiotherapist and Orthopedic you can always contact us and for more information follow us on Instagram &amp; Facebook.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/450552750_04_02_2022_06_37_31.jpg','2022-02-03 10:33:56','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(42,'what-are-the-common-causes-of-hip-pain-in-women','What are the Common Causes of Hip Pain in Women?','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','As similar to other chronic pain women tend to experience Hip pain more often as compared to men. There can be a number of reasons behind it as hip pa...','<p>As similar to other chronic pain women tend to experience Hip pain more often as compared to men. There can be a number of reasons behind it as hip pain is such a wide term from injury to osteoporosis it can be anything.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Make sure you first know what is the exact reason for your pain that you can treat it rightly. This article will let you know the main causes of Hip Pain. It will help you learn more about these conditions and the measures used to achieve the best outcomes possible.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Common Causes of Hip Pain</h2>\r\n\r\n<h2>Inflamed Tendons</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The most common cause for hip pain in women is Inflamed Tendons. It generally occurs due to overworking or too much exercise can also be the reason. Inflamed Tendons are very painful and you must see a doctor if it doesn&rsquo;t heal in a few days.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/knee-arthritis\">Arthritis</a></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>In older adults, Osteoarthritis and Rheumatoid Arthritis are the common reasons for hip pain. It leads to inflammation of the hip and the breakdown of the cartilage that cushions our hip bones. If you are suffering from this, your pain will start growing gradually and people with arthritis also feel stiffness and reduction in range of motion. If you are dealing with any of these symptoms make sure you see a good doctor before it gets worse.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Trochanteric Bursitis</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are hurting on the outsides of your hip, thigh or buttocks, then it might be your bursitis. It causes inflammation in the pillow like fluids sacs that prevent tendons and muscles from rubbing directly against bone.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This type of pain is not related to your day-to-day activity. It hurts even when you are sleeping on your side. However, it gets worse when you are walking or climbing stairs. It generally occurs in older people, aged above 60.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Gynecological or Pelvic Floor Issues</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The pain you are feeling in your can be coming from somewhere else like the pelvis. The pelvis contains many systems and everything is jammed there, close together. So, you must consult with the doctor where this pain is coming from.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>And if the pain is limited to your groin and overlaps with your ovulation at the time of period. Then the reason could be endometriosis or fibroids rather than a problem with the hip. Urological and gastrointestinal issues, such as gastroenteritis and prostate cancer, could also cause pain that&#39;s easily mistaken for a hip injury.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Hip Fractures</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Hip fractures generally occur in old or adults, due to normal wear and tear with age it happens. It causes weakening to the bones due to age and other factors. The hip fracture causes very severe pain, and it needs immediate medical help.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This might need surgery to be corrected. You&rsquo;ll most likely have physical therapy to recover.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>How is Hip Pain Diagnosed?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>For your pain that could be related to the above-written reasons, you must consult a good doctor that will help you in proper diagnosis and treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Your doctor might ask you certain questions like</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Does your pain get worsen at night?</li>\r\n	<li>Does it affect your mobility or walk?</li>\r\n	<li>When did your symptoms first appear?</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>For a complete diagnosis, your doctor will perform some fluid and imaging tests on you. Imaging tests like:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/digital-x-ray-for-diagnosis\">X-ray</a></strong></li>\r\n	<li>CT scan</li>\r\n	<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/digital-x-ray-for-diagnosis\">MRI scan</a></strong></li>\r\n	<li>Ultrasound</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>An imaging test will help your doctor with a detailed view of cartilage, bones, and other tissues.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What is the treatment for Hip Pain?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Treatment of your hip pain depends on the type of your if you are having pain due to arthritis, injury, or a fracture. For best treatment and therapies, you can always consult our experts like Varun Agrawal, he is an experienced orthopedic surgeon who has been handling critical cases of hip arthritis and fracture. For physio you can consult Dr. Sumit, he will you with physical therapies that will reduce your pain and help you with mobility &amp; other functions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For more information, you can follow us on <strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/drsumitz/\">Facebook</a></strong> and <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/drsumitz/?hl=en\"><strong>Instagram</strong></a>.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/530173484_16_02_2022_03_28_23.jpeg','2022-02-16 07:07:30','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(43,'plantar-fasciitis-symptoms-precautions','Plantar fasciitis: Symptoms & Precautions','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','It is very important to treat heel pain to avoid further misalignments &amp; complications.\r\n\r\nTo know further what exactly plantar fasciitis is keep...','<h2>It is very important to treat heel pain to avoid further misalignments &amp; complications.</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>To know further what exactly plantar fasciitis is keep reading the article:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Plantar fasciitis is the name commonly used to mention heel or arch pain on the bottom of the foot. More precisely, plantar fasciitis is an infection of the connective tissue, called the plantar fascia, that extended from the base of the toes, across the arch of the foot where it fixes into the heel bone. Overpronation is the most usual source of plantar fasciitis. As the foot cycle inside intolerably when walking, it smoothens the foot, Drags the arch, and brings build tension to the plantar fascia. Later, this causes swelling.&nbsp;Pain is generally unacceptable in the morning when first getting out of bed or when sitting for extended periods.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Aspects that may increase your possibility of developing Plantar Fasciitis include:</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Age. </strong>Plantar fasciitis is most usually between the ages of 40 and 60.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Sex.</strong> This disease is most commonly found in women compared to men.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Certain types of exercise.</strong> Tasks that place a lot of stress on your heel and connected tissue &mdash; such as great-distance running, Toe dancing, and dance exercises such as Zumba &mdash; can give to the initial onset of plantar fasciitis.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Faulty foot mechanics.</strong> Being <strong>unwavering</strong>, having a high arch, or even having an unusual pattern of walking can badly affect the way weight is allocated when you&#39;re standing and planting and build on stress on the plantar fascia. A tight heel cord, Achilles tendon, and decreased motion of the big toe joint also provide heel pain.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Obesity.</strong> Excess weight put extra stress on your plantar feet.</li>\r\n	<li>Professions that keep you on your feet. Factory workers, teachers, retail workers, and others who occupy most of their work hours walking or standing on hard surfaces like concrete can harm their plantar fascia.</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Improper shoes.</strong> Escape loose, boot-type shoes, as well as shoes without enough arch support or plastic padding to absorb shock. If you regularly wear high heels over 2 inches your Achilles tendon &mdash; which is connected to your heel &mdash; can shrink and shorten, causing pressure on the tissue around your heel. If your &quot;go-to shoe&quot; is over a year old, possibility of your foot pain would be reduced with a new pair of new shoes. Wearing the wrong shoe for your foot type can also come up with heel pain.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>There are numerous triggers for plantar fasciitis, so it&#39;s important to learn how to lower your risk. Being overweight puts extra pressure on your feet, so reducing your weight&nbsp;is a good idea if you fight heel pain.</li>\r\n	<li>The shoes you put on can also make a big difference in how your feet feel, so secure your feet and heels with shoes that offer good support in the arch and abroad, firm heel. Don&rsquo;t wear crumbled shoes; replace them when there is recognizable wear on the sole. Also, do not walk barefoot on hard surfaces.</li>\r\n	<li>Physical activity will also affect plantar fasciitis. Always work out, and never hurry into new activity &mdash; take your time, and let your muscles habituate the exercise. And invest in a pair of shielded running shoes, which should be replaced always.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Simple Steps to Console Heel Pain</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>If heel pain is keeping you down, care for your feet a bit until they&#39;re feeling better again. To relieve the pain:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Use an ice pack to lower swelling, inflammation, and pain.</li>\r\n	<li>Rest your feet by staying off of them as much as possible for a few days when your heels are aching.</li>\r\n	<li>Exercising your feet can be helpful.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>If those suggestions don&#39;t help in reducing heel pain, your doctor may recommend the following treatments:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Wearing a special tube grip at night. This helps by keeping a slight stretch of the plantar fascia while sleeping.</li>\r\n	<li>Physical therapy and exercises</li>\r\n	<li>Custom shoes or inserts (orthotics)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>You can also consult us for <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><strong>Physiotherapy &amp; Orthopaedic treatment.</strong></a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>To know more follow us on <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/drsumitz\">Facebook</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/drsumitz/?hl=en\">Instagram</a>.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/938363487_23_03_2022_04_36_03.jpg','2022-03-17 07:26:03','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(44,'the-best-sports-to-play-for-a-great-workout','The Best Sports to Play for a Great Workout!','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Sports is a great way to work out, where you can enjoy making new friends after office or school. The best kind of workout is that where you enjoy it...','<p>Sports is a great way to work out, where you can enjoy making new friends after office or school. The best kind of workout is that where you enjoy it even if you are not good at it, if you like it will get better eventually.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Basketball, Baseball even Table Tennis can help in increasing your heart rate and in burning calories. The high-intensity sport involves not only calorie burn but also increases your metabolism, so whenever choosing sport as a workout chooses which involves high intense activity. If you are feeling confused about the sport then don&rsquo;t worry! In this article, I am going to tell you about some exciting sports that you can play for workout.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Road Cycling &amp; Mountain Biking</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Cycling is one of the best sports that you can do for overall fitness. Cycling not only allows great aerobic exercise but also provides your legs muscles, especially your quads, glutes &amp; hamstring to feel great burnout.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Cycling can be easy &amp; a good sport, suitable for beginners to intermediate level. Mountain biking is also good for intermediate to advance levels &amp; if you are a beginner then you can start with paved trails.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Running</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>It can be a marathon run or a light jog, running is one of the easiest &amp; most preferred way to lose weight. Of course, there is not doubt that running takes a lot of endurance, stamina &amp; body strength. Many athletes do this religiously to stay fit and active. So, if you are Running regularly or planning to do so that go ahead it is worth your time &amp; surely will give you results.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Rowing</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Various research shows that rowing serves you many benefits besides weight loss, a low risk of injury and increased muscle strength is some of its benefits. Although rowing is considered to be an outdoor exercise you can perform &amp; enjoy it indoors too on the rowing machine.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Swimming</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Swimming is not only an exciting sport for physical exercise but it is also good for your heart also, is a low-stress exercise. It burns a lot of calories, improves lungs functionality, and provides you with overall good health by building muscular strength &amp; endurance.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Tennis</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>It is one the best aerobic exercise you can consider it equal to that of cycling, jogging &amp; running. You can burn up to 500 calories by playing one hour of tennis. Playing tennis also increases your arm strength, coordination, and cardiovascular health.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Wrestling</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Wrestling is a great sport that involves a high-intensity activity that leads to calorie burn &amp; also develops self-defense mechanisms. This is good especially for women as it serves multiple benefits and anyone can participate in the freestyle for fun and fitness.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This amazing sport often leads to developing flexibility, bone strength, stamina, coordination, and overall development.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Basketball</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Basketball involves a lot of running, jumping which increases your heart rate, makes your body shed weight.&nbsp; Playing basketball is very beneficial as it builds endurance, improves balance and coordination. Some studies show that basketball helps in increasing concentration, builds bone strength, self-discipline, and is also great for cardiovascular health.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Volleyball</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>It is included on the list for giving the healthiest players because it offers many benefits. This game involves increased metabolic rate, improves agility, enhances coordination, and boosts your mood along with burning all your extra calories.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Yoga</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>It can improve flexibility, strength, balance, and stamina. Besides its physical benefits, many people who practice yoga say that it eases anxiety and stress and improves mental clarity.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For Physical Therapy, Physiotherapy, or <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopaedic-center\"><strong>Orthopedic services in Pune</strong></a> you can contact us. For more information follow us on Instagram and Facebook.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/67379585_23_03_2022_04_35_51.jpg','2022-03-21 09:47:22','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(45,'top-10-orthopedic-doctors-in-pune','Top 10 Orthopedic Doctors In Pune','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Doctors, who specialize in injuries of the musculoskeletal system which includes bones, joints, ligaments, nerves, and tendons are called Orthopaedic...','<p>Doctors, who specialize in injuries of the musculoskeletal system which includes bones, joints, ligaments, nerves, and tendons are called <strong>Orthopaedic physicians</strong>. The field of orthopedics was first developed to treat children who had crippling or debilitating diseases which means diseases that seriously affect someone or something&#39;s strength or ability If it is a bone fracture or joint pain, or muscle strains, the conditions can become extreme if not treated on time or most people work long hours sitting with one posture, and it causes friction in the bone. On the other hand, people with sports activities in their daily life also face many bone problems. One of the bone problems includes limb abnormalities such as clubfoot or bowlegs pain to carry on with regular activities.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sumit is the leading <strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-orthopedic-physiotherapists-in-baner-pune\">Orthopaedic &amp; Physiotherapy clinic in Pune</a></strong> and serves proactive, quality healthcare in a safe and comfortable environment. It is the list of doctors in Pune who provides the orthopedic treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Dr. Varun Agrawal</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>He is working as an <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/specialists/dr-varun-agrawal\"><strong>Orthopaedic Joint Replacement and Trauma Surgeon</strong></a> and completed a fellowship in Joint Replacement Surgery under Dr. Narendra Vaidya at Lokmanya Group of Hospitals, Pune. His specialty is Primary &amp; Revision Joint Replacement Surgery, and Simple &amp; Complicated Trauma Surgery. He is from the orthopedic department, MBBS, (Govt. Medical College, Yavatmal, Maharashtra).</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Dr. Sachin Khalane</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>He is an Orthopaedician and graduated from Grant Medical College &amp; Sir J.J. Group of Hospitals. This is the top-most government hospital in Maharashtra as well as one of the prestigious medical colleges in India. He has done his post-graduation in orthopedics from Lilavati Hospital and Research Centre, Mumbai. He is a specialist in joint replacement surgeries. He is from Orthopaedic Department, MBBS, MS ORTHOPAEDICS, Diploma in Orthopaedics. He is having 16 years of overall experience and 14 years as a specialist.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"color:black\">Dr. Ashish S. Ranade</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>He is an Orthopaedic Surgery specialist and MBBS, Masters of Surgery (Orthopaedics Surgery), and MRCS from renowned institutions with over 20 years of experience.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dr. Randhir Patil<br />\r\nDr. Patil has expertise in Orthopaedics. He has an experience of over 15 years of. He specializes in Trauma Cases, External / Internal Fixation, Arthroscopy, and Arthroplasty (joint replacement).<br />\r\nDr. Aniruddha Deshmukh<br />\r\nHe is a famous <strong>Orthopaedic Surgeon in Baner, Pune</strong>. Highly skilled, experienced, and specialist by training Dr. Aniruddha Deshmukh tries to offer the best &amp; consistent patient care services.<br />\r\nDr. Anil Ghanshyam Bhatia<br />\r\nHe is one of the best Orthopaedic doctors in Pune. He is a trained professional with experience of more than 31 years. In addition to this, he is currently working as a consultant for Hand &amp; Reconstructive Surgery in Aditya Birla Hospital Pune. Dr. Anil Ghanshyam Bhatia pursued MBBS and MS- orthopedics. The doctor has treated various patients who had paralysis and bone cancer. Graceful as an orthopedic doctor, his experience includes small hand reconstructive surgery.&nbsp;<br />\r\nDr. Mangesh Darekar<br />\r\nHe is expertise in performing shoulder surgery using arthroscopy methods. Specialize in performing partial, total, and corrective knee replacement surgery and expertise in sports medicine also. He is M.B.B.S., D&#39;Ortho, D.N.B. (Orthopaedics), fellowship in Joint replacement and Knee Surgery, and fellowship in Shoulder. He is having experience of 10 years of as an Orthopaedic Surgeon. He is currently working at Global Hospital and Research Center (Dattawadi), Pune.<br />\r\nDr. Yogesh Panchwagh<br />\r\nHe is a very knowledgeable surgeon with expertise in treating orthopedic trauma, ligament &amp; meniscus tears, arthroscopy, joint replacement, and dislocations. He is a famous specialist in cancers of orthopedic origin also. He has experience of 15 years as an orthopedic surgeon. He is MBBS. MS (Ortho), DNB, Diploma (Tissue Banking), Fellow. He is currently working in Columbia Asia Hospital (Pune), Pune.<br />\r\nDr. Anil Bhatia<br />\r\nHe is an experienced surgeon whose areas of expertise include treating traumatic musculoskeletal injuries, joint replacements, arthroscopy, and hand surgeries. He is an Orthopaedic Surgeon having experience of 27 Yrs. He is MBBS, MS (Ortho), Fellowship in Hand Surgery (Italy), and working in AIMS Hospital (Aundh), Pune.<br />\r\nDr. Ajit Swamy&nbsp;<br />\r\nDr. Ajit Swamy is a renowned orthopedic doctor in Pune and has experience of 24 years. He is well qualified for his MBBS, MS- Orthopaedic Surgery. Furthermore, he is currently working in Aditya Birla Memorial Hospital Pune. His service includes orthopedic surgery, treatment, and consultation for the bone allied condition and delivers satisfactory results and a success rate of surgery.<br />\r\n<strong>Conclusion</strong>&nbsp;<br />\r\n<strong>Orthopedic doctors</strong> can serve the treatment of bones, muscles, ligaments, and joints. they can also treat chronic bone conditions, including arthritis and lower back pain. If you observe the primary symptoms of the bone allied problems, seek immediate expert advice. The orthopedic doctors can treat your other areas, including spine, hip &amp; knee, hand, and trauma surgery.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/407249885_12_04_2022_05_28_38.jpg','2022-04-12 11:48:57','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(46,'does-gain-in-weight-affect-your-bones','Does gain in weight affect your bones?','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Does gain in weight affect your bones\r\n\r\nResearch shows that being obese can lead to a decrease in bone density which further leads to diseases like o...','<h3>Does gain in weight affect your bones</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Research shows that being obese can lead to a decrease in bone density which further leads to diseases like osteoporosis. The rapid increase in weight often leads to knee pain and also increases the risk of fracture even in those with normal bone density.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Overweight and obesity identify as excessive fat that can lead to many diseases. BMI is a simple ratio of height to weight that is used to differentiate between overweight and obesity. Patients who are obese have a greater risk of falling and breaking bones. It is used to be thinking if you are overweight your bones were support more weight and your bones become better.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>They have greater bone density. Bone density is increased when you do tasks that put stress on the bone structure like weight lifting or in this case carrying around excess weight.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Adipose tissue</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Adipose tissue consists mainly of fat cells which are divided into fat lobules by thin layers of loose connective tissue and are widely distributed in the organs. It is involved in body construction and energy storage and vital endocrine organ. Adipose tissue utilizes a primary function in obesity and related diseases.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>However, since losing weight is so advantageous for health regardless of bone density issues, researchers said that adding supplements in your diet with calcium, vitamin D, vitamin K2, and strontium can also help boost bone density. Age-related reduction in muscle mass can be prevented or reversed with proper exercise.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Osteoarthritis</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Obesity frequently provides soft tissue damage and osteoarthritis&mdash;developing wear and tear disease of the joints. The effect of obesity is especially felt in osteoarthritis of the hip and knee joints. Every pound of body weight places four to six pounds of pressure and force on each knee joint.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Osteosarcopenic</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Abdominal fat (fat found in other places in the body) has a more harmful impact on bone and muscle strength and can also boost swelling. Here are separate tests to gauge obesity, bone density, and muscle mass. so those who have BMI (body mass index) above 30 might be at risk for osteosarcopenic obesity.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Osteoporosis.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>An adult has 206 bones in their body. People can have different numbers of rib bones and bones in their body parts that make doctors average the number of bones in a skeleton. We found when people have Bones Osteoporosis, they have thinning bones so we called that different people had different bones densities. The interesting thing that is justified in this quest is heavy people with a BMI over 33 never get Osteoporosis.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For postmenopausal women, Osteoporosis is considered a major public health problem. After five to seven years of menopause, low estrogenic levels lead to rapid bone loss in women.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Different age groups with different problems with bones</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Childhood obesity is a major problem because it affects the growth patterns of children and adolescents.Children affected by obesity may develop accelerated skeletal maturity and advanced bone age beyond their actual age.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Preventions</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>You must perform the following activities in order to gain bone strength and decrease obesity.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Make time to perform physical activity for at least 20 to 60 minutes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Keep an active behavior, go on a long walk with your friends, and use stairs instead of the lift.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Encourage physical activity in the daily lifestyle, count steps daily and set a target for the next day.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A healthy diet is also important, don&rsquo;t depend solely on exercise.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you have any questions related to any disease or diet, you can always contact us. For more information stay updated on our blogs</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For more updates visit <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-clinic\"><strong>best physiotherapy clinic in pune</strong></a>, you can follow us on Instagram and Facebook. You can also DM us for any query.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/265864532_29_04_2022_05_29_39.jpg','2022-04-29 11:40:09','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(47,'what-causes-varicose-veins-how-to-get-rid-of-them','What Causes Varicose Veins & How to Get Rid of them?','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Varicose veins are basically large, swollen, twisting veins that started to appear blue and darker purple in colors on the skin. Varicose can occur an...','<p>Varicose veins are basically large, swollen, twisting veins that started to appear blue and darker purple in colors on the skin. Varicose can occur anywhere in your body but the legs are the most common area.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In a study, it is found that almost 23% of the adults suffer from this problem, it is not that of a serious problem but it can be uncomfortable &amp; can lead to more serious problems</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What are spider veins?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Spider vein is a milder type of varicose vein, it certainly looks like a sunburst or spider web. They are mostly red or blue and most commonly found on the body parts such as the face, and legs.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What are the reasons for Varicose Veins?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>It generally happens because of the increased blood pressure in the veins. It happens in the veins that are closer to the surface of the skin. What actually happens is, that valves do not work properly making it hard for the muscles to push the blood &ldquo;uphill&rdquo;. Instead of flowing from one valve to the next, blood pools in the vein, raising venous pressure and increasing the risk of congestion while bulging and twisting the vein. Because superficial veins are less supported by muscle than deep veins, they are more prone to varicose veins.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Risk Factors&nbsp;</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>As we have already discussed the increase in pressure in veins causes varicose veins. Other Factors that may lead to varicose veins are: Overweight and Obesity Age factor Females are more prone No Physical Activity Pregnancy Smoking Can you Prevent Varicose veins? Some of the things that you can do to prevent the Varicose Veins: Exercise Regularly: Staying fit is one of the best ways to prevent multiple diseases also this will help you in keeping your leg muscles toned, and also maintains your weight and blood flowing. Avoid tight-wearables Tight clothes constrict blood flow in the waist, groin, and legs which can lead to varicose veins. Avoid high heels Footwear: High heels hinder the blood flow which makes it pool in the veins and causes problems like Varicose Veins. Treatment Legs should be elevated: You may be told to elevate your feet above the level of your heart for 15 minutes three or four times a day. Flexing (bending) your legs every now and then can help keep blood flowing if you have to sit or stand for an extended amount of time. Elevating your legs can help reduce leg swelling and relieve other symptoms if you have mild to moderate varicose veins. Ablation by heat. Varicose veins can be treated using lasers or radiofrequency energy. A catheter is used to inject a small fiber into a varicose vein. The laser or radiofrequency energy is utilized to give heat to the varicose vein wall, destroying it. Transilluminated powered phlebectomy An endoscopic transilluminator, a special light, is threaded through an incision beneath the skin by a doctor to see which veins need to be removed. They next use a suction instrument to cut and extract the target veins through the incision. This treatment can be done with either general or local anesthesia. After the operation, there may be some bleeding and bruising. You can consult us for physiotherapy and Orthopedic services. For more information, you can Follow us on Facebook and Instagram.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Risk Factors</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>As we have already discussed the increase in pressure in veins causes varicose veins. Other Factors that may lead to varicose veins are:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Overweight and Obesity</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;Age factor</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Females are more prone</p>\r\n\r\n<p>No Physical Activity</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Pregnancy</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Smoking</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Can you Prevent Varicose veins?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Some of the things that you can do to prevent the Varicose Veins:</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Exercise Regularly: </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Staying fit is one of the best ways to prevent multiple diseases also this will help you in keeping your leg muscles toned, and also maintains your weight and blood flowing.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Avoid tight-wearables</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Tight clothes constrict blood flow in the waist, groin, and legs which can lead to varicose veins.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Avoid high heels Footwear:</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>High heels hinder the blood flow which makes it pool in the veins and causes problems like Varicose Veins.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Treatment</h2>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Legs should be elevated:</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>You may be told to elevate your feet above the level of your heart for 15 minutes three or four times a day. Flexing (bending) your legs every now and then can help keep blood flowing if you have to sit or stand for an extended amount of time. Elevating your legs can help reduce leg swelling and relieve other symptoms if you have mild to moderate varicose veins.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Ablation by heat.</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Varicose veins can be treated using lasers or radiofrequency energy. A catheter is used to inject a small fiber into a varicose vein. The laser or radiofrequency energy is utilized to give heat to the varicose vein wall, destroying it.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Transilluminated powered phlebectomy</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>An endoscopic transilluminator, a special light, is threaded through an incision beneath the skin by a doctor to see which veins need to be removed. They next use a suction instrument to cut and extract the target veins through the incision.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This treatment can be done with either general or local anesthesia. After the operation, there may be some bleeding and bruising.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You can consult us for physiotherapy and Orthopedic services. For more information, you can Follow us on Facebook and Instagram.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/526704534_25_05_2022_06_39_15.jpg','2022-05-25 05:00:47','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(48,'ways-to-stronger-healthier-and-happier-life','Ways to Stronger, Healthier, and Happier Life!','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Do you usually feel lethargic in the mornings? Have caffeinated beverages become a daily requirement to keep you going? If this sounds like you, it&#3...','<p>Do you usually feel lethargic in the mornings? Have caffeinated beverages become a daily requirement to keep you going? If this sounds like you, it&#39;s time to give up the easy cures and adopt an energy management strategy. Starting may seem scary, but once you start reaping the rewards of a happier, healthier, and more productive lifestyle, you&#39;ll be motivated to keep going.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>To boost your energy and have a happier, healthier, and more productive life, try these 7 tips:</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>1.&nbsp;<strong>Consume Nutritious Food</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>We all know that nutritious food is essential for good health, but it&#39;s usual to think of healthy eating as primarily a means of losing weight. A balanced diet rich in fruits and vegetables, lean protein, low-fat dairy, and whole grains, according to a study is what you need for maximum energy. After all, to some extent, you are what you consume. To acquire a variety of nutrients to invigorate you throughout the day, eat a variety of meals from all dietary categories. Choose nutrient-dense dark, leafy greens and broccoli, as well as orange veggies like carrots and sweet potatoes, from fresh or frozen fruits and vegetables. Fish and legumes come in a variety of shapes and sizes.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>2.&nbsp;<strong>Good Sleep is Important</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Getting more sleep appears to be a healthy habit that many individuals might benefit from. We all know we need at least seven hours of sleep every night, so what&#39;s keeping us from getting it? Consider how you can improve your major sleep disruptors and keep in mind the following: Sleep deprivation can exacerbate existing health problems and have a negative impact on your attitude, motivation, and energy levels. One of the most effective ways to ensure a successful and invigorated day is to prioritize sleep.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>3<strong>&nbsp;Exercise Daily</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Do you find yourself sluggish towards the middle of the day? Have you ever been exhausted by ordinary tasks like grocery shopping or domestic chores? Getting the 150 minutes of weekly exercise advised by the Physical Activity Guidelines can add to your energy account, not deplete it, contrary to popular belief. How? Exercise helps your body operate more efficiently during other physical duties or activities by relieving stress and tension, strengthening muscles, and increasing endurance.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>4. Observe your energy levels.</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Take your energy &quot;temperature&quot; throughout the day and assign it a number between 1 and 10, with 10 being the maximum degree of energy. Pay attention to the small elements of your day so you can pinpoint the individuals or situations that have the most influence on you.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>5.&nbsp;<strong>Make little adjustments.</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Consider your next steps once you&#39;ve identified some of the individuals or circumstances that sap your energy. Instead of addressing everything at once, focus on one area that is essential to you and create reasonable goals. If the chaos in your house is a major cause of everyday stress, for example, instead of cleaning it all at once, choose one cupboard, closet, or drawer to clean out each week. When you&#39;re ready, go on to your next objective.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>6..<strong>No Smoking</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>We used to believe that smoking was harmless or even beneficial to our health (thanks, tobacco lobby!). Doctors smoked and frequently advised their patients to do so to relieve stress or lose weight. Those days, however, are long gone. Smoking raises your risk of lung cancer, as well as other lung and heart illnesses, according to solid data.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The drop-in smoking over the last 50 years or more has contributed significantly to the increase in the average longevity in the United States. That should never be reversed. If you want to live longer, it doesn&#39;t make sense to continue smoking (or vaping, for that matter). Stop doing anything you can.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>These tips will help you in leading a healthy life. If you are dealing with any problems related to joints, bones, or muscles then we have the most experienced, intelligent, and talented physiotherapists and orthopedics in muscles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For any query, you can contact <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><strong>physiotherapy services in pune</strong></a> anytime we are happy to help. For regular updates, you can follow us on Instagram &amp; Facebook.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/561856466_25_05_2022_06_10_41.jpg','2022-05-25 08:51:42','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(49,'best-physiotherapy-services-in-pune','Best Physiotherapy services in Pune','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Injuries are an inevitable part of our lives and you just can&rsquo;t leave your hobby or work because the last time you got an injury. Medications tr...','<p>Injuries are an inevitable part of our lives and you just can&rsquo;t leave your hobby or work because the last time you got an injury. Medications treat short-term pain relief but when you are looking for long-term relief, the injury needs to be treated very carefully and different consultants suggest physiotherapy treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You need to find the best physiotherapy clinic so that you can get the best treatment for the injury. Dr. Sumit is one such amazing physiotherapy clinic in Baner, Pune. Experts who have experience of decades provide you with the best consultations and treatment. Here you can easily minimize your chronic pain, Joint pain, and pain caused by the injury. Physiotherapy also helps you in regaining mobility and also helps the patients post-surgery.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Why Dr. Sumitz for Physiotherapy Treatment?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>You can get treatment from any physiotherapist you want but finding the best one that has expertise is an important factor to consider.&nbsp; We offer you much more than just a solution to your problem. How? Read Below:</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>The efficiency of the Experts</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Dr. Sumitz clinic in Baner, Pune offers efficiency along with the effectivity. Fully Trained Doctors that are experienced for years in providing physiotherapy services.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Convenient and Fast scheduling</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>We at Dr. Sumitz Clinic in Baner, Pune facilitate you with fast and convenient services. You don&rsquo;t have to wait for hours to get treatment. We provide you with early morning services as well as late-night so that you can avail yourself at your convenience. The weekend services are also available for the clients.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Reasonable prices for the services</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Different clinics charge different amounts as per the services they offer. Apparently, clients love working with experts who charges a reasonable amount from them. And this is what we are known for, providing you the best services at the best prices with efficient services.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Equipment &amp; treatment technology used</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The latest technology and modern equipment are used for treatment. It is very important to know how services are administered to you. You can easily the technology and equipment by visiting the hospital. As for us, your trust is the most important factor.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Services we provide</h2>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Physiotherapy Clinic:</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>In case you are suffering from excessive pain, injury, or chronic pain then you can consult us. We make sure that you are getting a timely follow-up to evaluate that you are getting regular sessions.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Physiotherapy Expert</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Find an expert in physiotherapy that provides you with the best solution by researching properly to the root cause. Physiotherapy provides you the long term relief from pain and immobility. We at Dr. Sumit provide you with such services that provide you relief for long life.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Sports Rehabilitation Experts in Baner</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are an athlete or some sports enthusiast who like to continue their journey with proper guidance &amp; improved performance. You can Consult us if you are looking Sports rehabilitation expert in Baner.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Ergonomics Solutions</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>We provide you with the best solution for Ergonomics with a complete understanding of humans and other related elements theory, data, methods, and overall system that ergonomics deals with. Consult for the best ergonomics solutions at Dr. Sumitz Baner, Pune.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Frozen Shoulder</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Frozen Shoulder is a condition that causes discomfort in the shoulder joint. Symptoms and signs normally appear gradually, intensify with time, and then go away within one to three years. The chance of getting a frozen shoulder rises if you are recuperating from a medical illness or operation that stops you from moving your arms, such as a stroke or a mastectomy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\nConsult for the best <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><strong>physiotherapy treatment and services in Baner, Pune. </strong></a>We at Dr. Sumit offer the best services, Consult Now!</p>\r\n','uploads/product/955168761_08_06_2022_06_04_39.jfif','2022-06-08 12:34:39','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(50,'know-the-most-common-physiotherapy-treatments-techniques','Know the most common Physiotherapy Treatments & Techniques!','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','There are different types of techniques used by physiotherapists for treating patients.&nbsp; Usually, doctors suggest physiotherapy after surgery or...','<p>There are different types of techniques used by physiotherapists for treating patients.&nbsp; Usually, doctors suggest physiotherapy after surgery or during treatment to maintain mobility. Physiotherapy also helps people with several ailments such as arthritis, bad posture, and amputations.&nbsp; If you are interested in what are the type of physiotherapy treatment and techniques then just keep scrolling to know.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Some most common physiotherapy treatments &amp; techniques are:</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Range of Motion Exercises:</strong><br />\r\nAlthough relaxation is frequently recommended during the early stages of recovery after broken bones or surgery, prolonged immobility can either slow or stop the healing process. As a result, physiotherapists frequently recommend a range of motion exercises to improve movement, joint mobility, and circulation. Muscle atrophy and accompanying postural difficulties can be avoided by moving the afflicted joints and muscles often. ROM exercises are utilized by a variety of healthcare professionals; for example, in personal support worker training, students learn a range of motion strategies to help patients with limited mobility improve their flexibility and preserve their independence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Soft tissue mobilization</strong><br />\r\nsoft tissue mobilization, also known as therapeutic massage, can assist a patient&#39;s muscles to relax and reduce swelling in specific regions, making it an appropriate treatment for pain associated with sporting injuries. Soft tissue massage also aids in the circulation of blood and lymph fluid, as well as the reduction of tissue swelling around inflammatory joints.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Electrotherapy</strong><br />\r\nElectrotherapy is a relatively recent development in the field of energy-based physiotherapy. Electrical stimulation is performed by attaching electrodes to the skin in this type of therapy. The electrodes induce the muscles to shorten, which helps to avoid atrophy. It&#39;s excellent for people who have paralysis or a limited range of motion. Electrotherapy can be used with laser and ultrasound therapy to achieve the best results.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Thermotherapy and Cryotherapy</strong><br />\r\nPeople with desk jobs and elite athletes both complain about sore, tight muscles. If a patient complains of muscular stiffness anywhere on their body, applying heat or ice to the irritated regions may be therapeutic. The use of heated packs or even paraffin wax can be used in heat treatment. Cryotherapy may include the use of an ice pack or an ice massage.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Kinesio Therapy</strong><br />\r\nYou must have seen the blue tape often used by physiotherapists Kinesio tape is a terrific approach to stabilize the joints and muscles while the patient is undergoing therapy. It may be placed directly on the skin. Furthermore, because the tape is flexible, it does not interfere with range of motion exercises, making it an ideal tool for stretching and flexing muscles.<br />\r\nAcupuncture and dry needling<br />\r\nAcupuncture and dry needling are used to relieve pain and aid in injury recovery. This therapy is an excellent pain treatment for a short period of time.<br />\r\nOur experts utilize this approach to place small single-use needles at specified spots along the meridian. The energy flow is then redirected and repositioned as a result. Finally, it helps to ease tension and stress.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Sports Physiotherapy</strong><br />\r\nIf you are an athlete or your close is an athlete then this portion of the article is for you. Warm-up activities are the first step in the dynamic stretching routine. A general warm-up for a few minutes until you can feel some warmth in your muscles is recommended as part of the ideal pre-exercise regimen. Then, for around 20 to 30 seconds, you do prolonged static stretches.<br />\r\nAs a result, the intensity of stretching develops in a graded manner, and you can do bounce-style workouts that mimic the demands of your activity.<br />\r\nWe are providing all these techniques and treatments including some other best physiotherapy treatments. Contact us for the best physiotherapy treatment or you can also visit our website for more information.<br />\r\nFor more updates, you can follow us on Facebook and Instagram.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/380047353_15_06_2022_06_37_41.jpg','2022-06-15 13:05:37','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(51,'what-are-the-most-common-types-of-orthopedics','What are the most common types of orthopedics?','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Surgeons conduct a wide variety of orthopaedic operations. Even though they are still invasive operations, many of these techniques target various reg...','<p>Surgeons conduct a wide variety of orthopaedic operations. Even though they are still invasive operations, many of these techniques target various regions of the body. Thanks to technological advancements, some are even now just slightly intrusive. Your orthopaedic surgeon will explain the precise procedure you require to you, including what it entails, what the risks are, and whether you have any alternative options.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\nKnowing whether or not your condition is common might be helpful if you&#39;ve been advised that you require surgery. Here are a few of the most popular orthopedic procedures in that regard that are all performed in<a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><strong> Dr. Sumitz Clinic, baner.</strong></a></p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Knee Replacement</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>One of the most frequently utilized joints in the body, the knee is regrettably frequently overused to the point of damage. Partial or complete replacement of the knee joint with an artificial one are both options for knee replacement surgery.<br />\r\nThis is typically required because the joint&#39;s cartilage has been destroyed, limiting motion or making movement extremely uncomfortable. This can be brought on by a variety of factors, such as obesity, bursitis, and knee injuries.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>ACL Surgery</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The anterior cruciate ligament (ACL), which runs diagonally across the front of the knee, is an essential component. When you spin on your leg, it helps keep you stable. Reconstructive surgery is required to restore this damaged ligament.<br />\r\nDuring this procedure, a tendon fragment from another region of the body is cut up and grafted into the ACL&#39;s injured area. The patient may often go home the same day after this little procedure.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Hip Replacement&nbsp;</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The hip is another popular joint that is frequently replaced. The acetabulum (the socket) and femoral head are the components of the hip (the ball).<br />\r\nThe cartilage in the hip ages with time, just like the knee does, especially if it is injured. There are two distinct replacement operations, similar to the knee. The whole joint is frequently replaced. The Birmingham Hip Resurfacing operation, on the other hand, merely repairs the damaged portions of the joint. But this isn&#39;t always a choice.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Shoulder Replacement</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The shoulder is another joint that is frequently replaced by surgery. The shoulder is frequently subjected to a great deal of stress, just like the knee or hip. Typically, a metal ball is used to replace the top portion of the humerus, the bone in the upper arm. The damaged portion of the socket is then replaced with a plastic replacement.<br />\r\nThe socket is often composed of metal, and the arm bone is replaced with plastic if your rotator cuff is also affected.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Arthroscopy</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The operation of arthroscopy can be carried out either on the shoulder or the knee. One of the least invasive orthopaedic treatments enables the doctor to insert a tiny camera close to the joint to obtain a good picture of the injury.<br />\r\nBefore having your knee or shoulder replaced, you might need to have an arthroscopy so the doctor can assess the extent of the injury and determine the precise course of action.<br />\r\nFor best Arthroscopy you can consult us , you can also consult us for other orthopaedic treatment in baner, pune.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Fusion of joints</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>A joint fusion operation can be necessary at some point if you have arthritis. During this procedure, healthy cartilage is removed from an unharmed portion of the body and transplanted on to a damaged location.<br />\r\nThe bones on each side are really cemented together when this is finished to help support the joint. The spine, fingers, foot, and ankles may all be treated with this technique.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Consult Us</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Our teams of experienced doctors are always ready to help you with the best solutions and treatment. You can contact us to book your appointment.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/720513972_06_07_2022_11_58_31.jpg','2022-07-06 05:15:01','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(52,'total-knee-replacement-surgery','Total Knee Replacement Surgery ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','You could find it challenging to carry out basic tasks like walking or climbing stairs if your knee is significantly injured due to arthritis or an in...','<p>You could find it challenging to carry out basic tasks like walking or climbing stairs if your knee is significantly injured due to arthritis or an injury. Even if you are sitting or lying down, you could start to experience discomfort.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Consider complete knee replacement surgery if nonsurgical options like prescribed drugs are no longer effective. Surgery to replace a joint can ease discomfort, treat leg deformity, and help you go back to your regular activities.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Whether you have made up your mind to get a knee replacement done or thoughts are lingering in your mind, this article will help you understand this valuable treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Cause</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Arthritis is the most typical cause of persistent knee pain and impairment. Despite the fact that there are other varieties of arthritis, osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, and post-traumatic arthritis are the three that are most commonly responsible for knee discomfort.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Osteoarthritis:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>This form of arthritis results from &quot;wear and tear&quot; as people age. It often affects persons over the age of 50, while it can sometimes affect younger people. The knee&#39;s protective cartilage deteriorates and softens with time. The subsequent rubbing of the bones results in stiffness and discomfort in the knee.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Rheumatoid arthritis:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>also known as inflammatory arthritis, causes the knee joint&#39;s lining to thicken and swell. Chronic inflammation erodes cartilage, resulting in stiffness and pain.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Post traumatic arthritis:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>commonly referred to as inflammatory arthritis, thickens and swells the lining of the knee joint. Chronic inflammation damages cartilage, causing discomfort and stiffness.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Risk of the Procedure</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Complications can arise during surgery, as they do in other operations. Among other things, the following are a few potential drawbacks:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&bull; Bleeding</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&bull; Infection</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&bull; Blood clots in the legs or lungs</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&bull; Loosening or wearing out of the prosthesis</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&bull; Fracture</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&bull; Continued pain or stiffness</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The artificial knee joint replacement might break, move, or stop functioning as it should. In the future, the joint could need to be changed once again.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Weakness or numbness might be caused by damaged blood vessels or nerves in the surgical region. Surgery might not be able to relieve joint discomfort.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Depending on your particular medical condition, there can be additional dangers. Prior to the operation, be careful to share any worries you have with your doctor.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Patients who suffer the following may benefit from knee surgery:</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Severe knee discomfort or stiffness that makes it difficult for patients to do daily activities like walking, climbing stairs, getting in and out of automobiles, or getting up from a chair.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Knee discomfort is moderate and ongoing, even while sleeping or relaxing.</li>\r\n	<li>Chronic knee edema and inflammation that does not subside with medicine or rest.</li>\r\n	<li>An obvious arch on the inside or outside of the knee is a knee malformation.</li>\r\n	<li>Depression is brought on by a lack of capacity to engage in social or daily activities.</li>\r\n	<li>Surgery could be the best option if all other available treatment options have failed.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Types of Knee Replacement Surgery</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Total replacement Surgery:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Surgery involves the replacement of both sides of the knee joint. It is the most common procedure. The surgery lasts between 1 and 3 hours. The individual will have less pain and better mobility, but there will be scar tissue, which can make it difficult to move and bend the knees.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Partial replacement:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>One side of the knee joint is replaced during partial replacement. The incision is smaller since less bone is taken, but it does not last as long as a complete replacement. People who have knee injuries in one area can benefit from PKR. Recovery after surgery is straightforward, there is less blood loss, and the danger of infection and blood clots is reduced. There is a greater likelihood of more natural movement and the hospital stay and recuperation time are often shorter.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are looking for a Knee Replacement surgery or any other orthopedic or physiotherapy treatment. In that case, you can contact us or you can also check out our website for more information.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/198862952_11_07_2022_07_05_19.jpeg','2022-07-11 13:35:19','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(53,'effective-physiotherapy-treatment-for-some-common-sports-injuries','Effective Physiotherapy Treatment for some Common Sports Injuries    ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','We all have sustained sports Injuries you might have had it while playing gully cricket while I got mine in a basketball match. But most of us have be...','<p>We all have sustained sports Injuries you might have had it while playing gully cricket while I got mine in a basketball match. But most of us have been through fractures and knee injuries. Sports injuries can occur anytime from Cycle races to FIFA World Cup. It is as important to learn the treatment as to play the game. Even professional athletes occasionally get sprains or tears.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sports may frequently result in particular types of injuries depending on the mechanics of the game, such as the amount of body contact, pace, and other environmental elements, whether it be football or cricket.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>When a player is worn out or is involved in an unforeseen high-impact circumstance, such as a tackle or tumble, common sports injuries frequently happen.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Top 10 Sports Injury that a Physiotherapist can easily heal:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Ankle Sprain</li>\r\n	<li>Hamstring Sprain</li>\r\n	<li>Groin Strain</li>\r\n	<li>Knee Injuries</li>\r\n	<li>Stress Fractures</li>\r\n	<li>Tennis Elbow</li>\r\n	<li>Carpel Tunnel Syndrome</li>\r\n	<li>Achilles Injuries</li>\r\n	<li>Neck Injuries</li>\r\n	<li>Shoulder Injuries</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Ankle Sprain</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Whenever the ligaments holding the ankle bones together get torn, an ankle sprain results. These ligaments stabilize the joint and can cause sprains if they are stretched too much. Due to the tension imposed on the joints during activities like twisting, jumping, turning, and quick direction changes, athletes are more prone to ankle sprains. When the foot rotates inward, the ligaments on the outside of the ankle are affected in more than 80% of ankle sprains. Three little ligaments support the joint here, whereas the deltoid ligament, a big and powerful ligament, stabilizes the interior of the ankle joint. Less than 20% of injuries are sprains of the inner ligament.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Consult us for the best <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/sports-injuries\">Physiotherapy treatment </a>for Ankle sprain.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Hamstring Sprain</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Hamstring Sprain is the most common Sports injury. You will suffer sudden pain, tenderness or cramping in the back of your thigh the moment a hamstring sprain occurs. Because hamstring muscles are used for both power and speed, athletes are more likely to suffer hamstring strains. Overuse, weakness, improper stretching technique, or a lack of stretching are the major reasons for hamstring strain quadriceps and hamstrings, as well as gluteal weakness, are other common causes of hamstring strains.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Groin Strain</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>An injury to one of the groin muscles, often one of the five hip adductor muscle groups. Even while any of these adductor muscle groups might be injured, the adductor longus is the most frequently affected. High-intensity exercises, including running, kicking, and rapid direction changes, frequently result in this injury. A groin strain can be minor, moderate, or severe, much like other strains. A groin strain may result in discomfort, inflammation, tight muscles, or difficulty walking, depending on its degree.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Tennis Elbow</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Tennis elbow doesn&#39;t simply affect participants of the game. It affects a lot of sportsmen and sports professionals who hold things improperly and repeatedly for extended periods of time. The muscles that allow the wrist and fingers to extend are impacted by the typical sports injury. The bony bump where the muscles attach is generally the site of the injury on the outside of the elbow.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Carpel Tunnel Syndrome</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>A painful ailment in the hand known as carpal tunnel syndrome is brought on by pressure on the median nerve, which passes through the wrist. Repetitive hand movements can aggravate carpal tunnel syndrome by compressing the nerve and putting pressure on it. Pain, numbness, and pins and needles are the typical symptoms.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Achilles Injury</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The Achilles is a sizable tendon that runs from the calf to the heel and is situated at the rear of the ankle. Running and walking are made possible by the Achilles tendon, which links the heel to the leg muscles and provides the strength to push off.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This is one of the most crippling sports injuries, and it is brought on by a ripping or rupturing of the tendon. This frequently occurs as a result of an excessive load being placed on the tendon, bad footwear, or an abrupt rise in stress and intensity.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are looking for a physiotherapist in Baner or Pune for treating sports Injuries then Dr. Sumitz&#39;s clinic is your place. Here, you will find experts who have years of experience in treating sports Injuries. You can also check our<a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"> website</a> for more information.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For regular updates follow us on <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/drsumitz/\">Instagram</a> and<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/drsumitz\"> Facebook.</a></p>\r\n','uploads/product/779205511_06_08_2022_03_57_36.jpg','2022-08-01 10:04:20','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(54,'orthopedic-treatment-for-frozen-shoulder','Orthopedic Treatment for Frozen Shoulder. ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','A frozen Shoulder is quite bothersome and painful as it causes immobility and stiffness in the shoulder joint. Do you know that the most typical age r...','<p>A frozen Shoulder is quite bothersome and painful as it causes immobility and stiffness in the shoulder joint. Do you know that the most typical age range for frozen shoulders is between 40 and 60? Research also proves that Frozen shoulder is thought to affect 2 to 5 percent of people at some time, and it affects women somewhat more than men.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What is frozen Shoulder?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Adhesive capsulitis, another name for frozen shoulder, results in discomfort and stiffness in the shoulder. The shoulder gets increasingly difficult to move with time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Frozen shoulders often improve after a period of increased symptoms; however complete recovery might take up to 3 years. The main course of treatment for frozen shoulders is physical therapy, with an emphasis on shoulder flexibility.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Why does frozen shoulder occur?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The specific etiology of a main frozen shoulder is unknown. People with thyroid issues and those with diabetes are more likely to experience it. Most likely, not the source of the disease, yet 15% of patients associate it with a minor shoulder injury.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What is likely to happen?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>There are mainly 3 phases:</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Phase 1</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Painful phase (which can last from 2 to 9 months)</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Pain begins to develop slowly at first. It can reach as far as the forearm and the elbow and can be felt on the outside of the upper arm. It can be felt at rest and gets worse when the arm is mobilized. Since laying on it is uncomfortable, sleep is frequently impacted. In this stage, shoulder mobility starts to slow down.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Phase 2</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Stiff Phase (which can last from 4 to 12 months)</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The ball and socket joint gets stiffer with time, especially when performing twisting motions like trying to place your hand behind your back or your head. Even if you try to move the shoulder with your other hand or someone else tries to move the shoulder for you, these motions are still restricted.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The balls and socket joint are rigid whereas the shoulder is not rigid. You could start to notice the shoulder blades (scapula&#39;s) mobility more. The shoulder blade can still freely move across the chest wall.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Phase 3</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Recovery Phase (which can last from 5 to 26 months)</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>During this stage, the pain and stiffness start to go away, allowing you to use your arm more normally. The procedure lasts anything from 12 to 42 months in total, with an average of 30 months.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Although the pain and stiffness might be extremely intense, it is vital to remember that most of the time the issue will go away. You won&#39;t be bothered by it forever! Only when a frozen shoulder is extremely sluggish to resolve is this surgery performed.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What are your treatment options to release frozen shoulder?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The length of time it takes to make a full recovery cannot be shortened by any one accepted kind of treatment. In the end, it appears that the shoulder goes through the three phases mentioned, and no therapy has changed this pattern.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>The passage of time is the main treatment!</li>\r\n	<li>The alleviation of pain is the priority during the difficult phase.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Hopefully, you&#39;ll notice that the movement progressively picks up when the healing period begins. Again, at this point, physical therapy may be beneficial to help you move as much as possible. You can perform some exercises with the help of your physiotherapist.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Here, we&#39;ll go through a couple of shoulder stretches. They may be adjusted to fit your specific shoulder. Regularly exercise 1-2 times every day. After taking a hot shower or bath, you could find them to be simpler. Another option is to use a hot water bottle. You should expect to experience some soreness or stretching while you perform these exercises. But intense pain that lasts for a long time&mdash;more than 30 minutes&mdash;is not typical. Reduce the exercises by performing them less frequently or with less vigor if the discomfort lasts longer.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Stop the workouts if the discomfort is still unbearable and consult us anytime.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For more information visit us on our website or you can also follow us on Facebook and Instagram.</p>\r\n','uploads/product/982072945_08_08_2022_05_58_32.jpg','2022-08-06 10:42:20','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(55,'cerebral-palsy-improving-functional-mobility-by-physical-therapy','Cerebral Palsy - Improving Functional Mobility By Physical Therapy ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Cerebral palsy occurs due to the abnormal development of the brain since birth. From all over the world, there are several cases that have been diagno...','<p><strong>Cerebral palsy </strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">occurs due to the abnormal development of the brain since birth. From all over the world, there are several cases that have been diagnosed, but the cure is not available. </span><em>The surprising fact about cerebral palsy is that - it is more common in boys and children with black skin than in girls and children with white skin.&nbsp;</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">As per the </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><strong>physiotherapy doctor in Pune</strong></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, the early signs of cerebral palsy are - the delayed growth of a child since birth and abnormal movement of the body. In a few cases, children do not even speak or even cry.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">But the majority of people are unaware of this disorder. We are sharing the type of therapy involved and the main cause of this disorder.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What are the types of cerebral palsy?&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">There are four </span><strong>types of Cerebral Palsy</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> and they are mentioned below -</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Spastic cerebral palsy&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Dyskinetic cerebral palsy&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Ataxic cerebral palsy&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Mixed cerebral palsy&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What is exactly cerebral palsy?&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Cerebral palsy occurs due to the abnormal development of the brain since the birth of a child. Cerebral palsy has two words - one is cerebral, which means it is related to the brain; and palsy means the problem in the muscles of the brain. Children with this kind of disease are not allowed to play, move, and walk like other children. This one disease can change the whole life of a child. </span><em>As per the latest statistics on cerebral palsy - per 1000 children, nearly 1 in 4 children are diagnosed with this disease</em><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Here are the following ways to treat the cerebral palsy&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The weird thing about this cerebral palsy is that - there is no medication available on the market for it. But still, there are a few options available that will help to treat cerebral palsy in a better manner. The common ways to treat cerebral palsy are -&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Physiotherapy -</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Physical therapy is an effective remedy to treat muscles that have lost function. This technique involves the movement of the affected muscles and organs to improve strength and mobility. </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-treatment\"><strong>Physiotherapy treatment in Pune</strong></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> does not allow the patient to rely on medicines and operations that may cause pain and expense. Due to physiotherapy, an individual can maintain the body and health alongside. Whether a person is involved in sports or a working professional, this is an effective therapy for everyone. If you are in Pune and are looking for the </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-clinic\"><strong>best physiotherapy clinic in Pune</strong></a><strong>,</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> then connect with us.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Occupational therapy -&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">After physical therapy, occupational therapy is the most effective trending therapy to treat cerebral therapy. In the united states, there are around 200,000 therapists who assist the child suffering from occupational therapy.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Speech therapy -&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Speech therapy is the best therapy for treating the patient in order to speak a bit more effortlessly. This involves the practice of the mobility function for the patient to speak fluently and swallow food.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>The main cause of cerebral palsy&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">At the time of birth or before the pregnancy, if gene mutation, fetal stroke, bleeding into the brain, infant infections, traumatic head injury, and lack of oxygen occur, then the probability of cerebral palsy increases.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Doctors recommend that pregnant women come regularly or every week for check-ups. This will help to diagnose the early signs of cerebral palsy to save the lives of mother and baby both. For a healthy baby&#39;s development, it is crucial to avoid coffee, alcohol, drugs, and fast foods. In order to prevent the child from cerebral palsy, take care of your health and consult a doctor in case of any query.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Wrapping up -&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Cerebral palsy is common among children and it comes straight from birth. Due to this problem, some become paralyzed for their whole life and some need crutches to move from one place to another. These patients can not speak or swallow any food. That is why they need the help of special therapy to kickstart the movement. Unfortunately, cerebral palsy has no cure, and the given therapies can only reduce the pain. </span><strong>&ldquo;</strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapist\"><strong>Physiotherapy near me</strong></a><strong>&rdquo;</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> is the best way to search for any physical therapy in the existing location of the patient.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/458197375_01_10_2022_12_47_48.jpg','2022-10-01 07:17:48','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(56,'principles-of-pediatric-physiotherapy','Principles Of Pediatric Physiotherapy','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThe child&rsquo;s development is the fundamental priority for the parents and the population of paediatric patients is rising every year. To...','<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The child&rsquo;s development is the fundamental priority for the parents and the population of paediatric patients is rising every year. To treat this problem - we have the best </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapist\"><strong>Physiotherapy </strong><strong>doctor in Pune</strong></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> known as Dr. Sumitz.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Changes in lifestyle, routine, and pollution are all major factors to become prey to emerging diseases. Well if you are facing this problem then this is the time to know how it can affect your child and the best ways to get rid of it. Today we have shared the </span><strong>principles of paediatric physiotherapy </strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">and the best possible solutions.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Here are the following principles of paediatric physiotherapy to get to know in-depth about it</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Children who are fond of games and fun, exercises, and other treatments may lose interest. That is why they prefer the best kinds of mobility exercises that boost strength and gross motor skills and also keep them happy and motivated. This is the time to perform physiotherapy while playing!</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Especially for children -&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">A </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/pediatric-orthopaedic-doctor\"><strong>paediatric orthopaedic in pune</strong></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> deals with children who need physical therapy, from infants to teenagers. If your child is suffering from mobility-related issues, malformations, prematurity, or neurology - then this is a warning sign that you need a paediatric physiotherapist for your child. In this therapy, the child is provided with the training and methods to instantly recover from this problem.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Well-experienced therapists&nbsp; -</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Problems include </span><em>congenital malformations, neurology, prematurity, and neuromotor issues</em><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">. This is not everyone&rsquo;s expertise. For this reason, you need to consult with those who are highly experienced in treating pediatric patients. Children are not mature like adults, which is why therapists need to be very conscious about the treatment of children.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Proper assessment -&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">It is therefore necessary to examine the whole body adequately for an effective treatment. With the help of proper assessment, you can diagnose the level of the problem and the mandatory treatment.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>ICF Model -&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The acronym ICF stands for </span><strong>International Classification of Functioning, Disability, and Health</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">. Without using this model, the treatment would be worthless without any results. There are several components in the ICF model, like body functions and personal and environmental factors. Every category reveals the level of seriousness, and then therapists can effortlessly choose the treatment.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Hands-on treatment -&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Paediatric physiotherapy is the only treatment that is both troublesome and challenging. A child with an improperly functioning system acts as a barrier to the child&#39;s development. As a result, you require treatment from experts who are capable of relieving your pain. Because experts are well-experienced in dealing with any kind of complex and risky situation.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Red flags for paediatric physiotherapy&nbsp;</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">There are the following reason on the basis of that you should consult with any paediatric physiotherapist for your child -&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Children are fond of sports and if your child wants to recover from any sports injury then this is a red flag for you.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">If they are not growing as per the growing age</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Weak muscles and lack of stamina&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Issues with neuro muscles</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Wrapping up -&nbsp;</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Paediatric physiotherapy</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> is an effective treatment to treat the flaws in the child&#39;s body regarding posture and coordination. Well, if you are wondering about the best </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopaedic-doctor\"><strong>orthopedic doctor in baner</strong></a><strong>,</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> then you are most welcome at DR. SUMITZ&rsquo;s </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopaedic-surgeon\"><strong>orthopedic clinic in baner</strong></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">This is the best clinic for </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/orthopaedic-treatment\"><strong>orthopedic treatment in baner</strong></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> and the same for physiotherapy treatment as well.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/986375387_17_10_2022_11_05_24.jpg','2022-10-13 11:53:38','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(57,'orthopedic-treatment-for-all-your-joints-and-bones-problems','Orthopedic Treatment For All Your Joints And Bones Problems ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','As per the current statistics, the orthopedic and sports markets are expected to grow in the years 2022 to 2027, and more than 900,000 patients perfor...','<p><em>As per the current statistics, the orthopedic and sports markets are expected to grow in the years 2022 to 2027,</em><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> and more than 900,000 patients perform knee replacement surgery in the U.S. every year. These statistics are not to make sound creepy - this is a sign that if there is a problem then there we have the solution of the best </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopaedic-center\"><strong>orthopedic clinic in Pune</strong></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">An </span><strong>orthopedic surgeon </strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">is not only concerned with bone fractures and injuries but also with helping patients maintain bone health and strength for the rest of their lives. A healthy diet, proper sleep, and exercise enable the circulation of blood flow in the body and improve posture. Along with this, if you are someone who has problems related to bones and needs to know more about the treatment, bone problems, and their symptoms. Today we are covering the whole topic here to get proper awareness.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Here are the following bones problem that you should not ignore</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Osteoporosis -&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Osteoporosis</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> is a kind of bone problem that affects humans in multiple ways. The main reason for this problem is the loss of density, and the body loses too much tissue from the bones. This is a common problem in the hip, spine, and wrist nowadays, and generally occurs in women more than in men. As age increases, so do the chances of falling into this trouble.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Symptoms -&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Loss of height&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Back pain</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Stooped posture&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Breakage bones&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Paget&rsquo;s disease -</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">This is a notorious problem, and the reason we are saying this is that it interferes with the recycling process of bones. For this reason, replacing the old bone tissues with new ones becomes impossible. The most affected bones in this disease are - </span><em>the pelvis, skull, spine, and legs</em><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">. As per the</span><strong> </strong><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> - the mainstay of Paget&rsquo;s disease is the lack of bisphosphonates.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>The symptoms</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> of Paget&rsquo;s disease are unknown, but if you are getting pain in the following bones, then you need to consult a doctor.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Pelvis&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Spine&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Skull&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Leg&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">You need to go to a doctor if you are experiencing pain in the bones, tingling and weakness, bone deformities, and hearing loss.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Bone infection -&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>The bone infection is also known as osteomyelitis</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">. This problem occurs due to the bacteria and fungi affecting the bones. These bacteria and fungi develop when the wound is left open or enters the body for other reasons. This disease makes the bones hollow, and one day they break down.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Symptoms -&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Fever and chills&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Redness, irritation</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Stiffness&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Swelling&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Risk for the people who have -&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Diabetes&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Hemodialysis&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Peripheral arterial disease ( PAD)&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Smoking addiction&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h3><strong>Osteonecrosis -&nbsp;</strong></h3>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Osteonecrosis</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> is a problem that occurs when the bone doesn&rsquo;t get a proper supply of blood flow like other parts of the body. People over the age of 30 or 40 are more likely to be affected by this problem. Injuries to any bone that doesn&rsquo;t allow blood flow are more prone to this disease, as are people with excessive use of alcohol and tobacco. As per the </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/orthopedic-treatment-for-frozen-shoulder\"><strong>orthopedic surgeon in Pune</strong></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, there is no specific treatment for this disease, but early diagnosis is helpful to cure this problem.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Following symptoms that you should not ignore in the body -&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Pain in the bone like in the femur</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Stiffness&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Lose its range of motion</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Best place to go for treatment of your joints and bones&nbsp;</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">After searching on Google for </span><strong>&ldquo;</strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><strong>orthopedic physiotherapy near me</strong></a><strong>,&rdquo;</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> - you may get multiple options for orthopedic surgeons. But here we have the best surgeon to cure all the bones related problems - Dr. Sumit. He is an expert at treating all the bones connected issues and giving proper suggestions to deal with them in the future if you haven&rsquo;t experienced them yet. The good news for the locals of Pune is that Dr. Sumit has developed an </span><strong>orthopedic clinic in Pune</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> so they don&rsquo;t need to move randomly here and there for the bones-related issue.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Wrapping Up -&nbsp;</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Dr. Sumit is an expert orthopedic and physiotherapist in Pune, and he has the best team to elimin