nknown things about the physiotherapists in Pune that only 1% of people may know.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">A degree is a must -&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If you want to become a physiotherapist, then it is necessary to hone your skills in the field of biology and earn a bachelor&#39;s degree. The better scores help to get admission to a recognized university for further studies in this field. Residency, getting a doctorate in physical therapy, and taking the National Physical Therapy Examination all take a long time. To be successful in this field, you need a passionate mind and a lot of patience. It also costs a lot. If a doctor doesn&#39;t have a license, he or she can&#39;t keep practicing medicine. If a doctor doesn&#39;t have a license, he or she can&#39;t keep practicing medicine. Because of this, a medical student stays a student even after getting more education until he or she gets a license. Also, they have to renew their license from time to time; otherwise, it doesn&rsquo;t remain valid.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Need to treat challenging patients as well -&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">At first, a physiotherapist may treat patients who are difficult to help so that they can study how they do it and learn more about how to treat such patients. Every operation is overseen by senior physiotherapists to ensure that nothing goes wrong with the patients.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Documentation -&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">As in engineering, we have to complete assignments every semester. In the same way, here, a new physiotherapist needs to do a lot of paperwork after treating a patient. This becomes hectic, but this is also part of their duty, which they have to complete on time and submit to the seniors.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Must have a zeal for earning -&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">In this field, you can earn the maximum after getting proper experience and finishing your education at the core level. But the majority of the people lose hope and faith in between, and that is why they can&rsquo;t take advantage of the sweetness of its future fruit. So if you have a burning desire to come into this field, then only take your first step; otherwise, it would be a waste of time.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Loan situation -&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The costs of studying physiotherapy at a good university, getting certified, getting a license, and working under the supervision of an expert are very high. Due to this reason, many students fall under a heavy load of bank loans and their interests, which creates more risk for their families.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Wrapping Up -&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">&nbsp;Never judge a book by its cover&mdash;the majority of patients believe a doctor is just a person with a degree. This is not just a degree; to achieve that position, they have to spend millions of dollars and their valuable time and age. Doctors have the most reputable job these days, and they treat us like family, so we should be grateful for them all the time. Dr. Sumitz runs a well-known </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">physiotherapy clinic in Pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">. Their team of doctors has the most experience and sees most of their patients every day. So if you have any bone- and joint-related issues, you can come to us.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<quillbot-extension-portal></quillbot-extension-portal>','uploads/product/798921418_27_01_2023_04_25_36.jpg','2023-01-27 10:55:36','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(68,'pinched-nerve-causes-and-treatment-from-the-orthopedic-centre-in-baner','Pinched Nerve: Causes and Treatment from the Orthopedic Centre In Baner ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','As per the experts of the orthopedic treatment in baner, when anything changes in your body and result in a bone, muscle, cartilage or tendon putting...','<p>As per the experts of the<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>orthopedic treatment in baner</strong></a>, when anything changes in your body and result in a bone, muscle, cartilage or tendon putting in a bone, muscle, cartilage or tendon puts too much pressure on a nerve, you may experience pain, tingling, or numbness.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This is known as a &ldquo;pinched nerve,&rdquo; and you may have had one without realizing it. Here&rsquo;s what you need to know if you think you have a pinched nerve.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Causes of Pinched nerve </strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The<strong>&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>orthopedic center in baner</strong></a>&nbsp;says that - we tend to believe that a pinched nerve only occurs in the back, but in actuality, it may occur anywhere in the body and be caused by a variety of factors, including:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Injury&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Herniation&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Carpal tunnel syndrome&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Stress from repetitive work&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Inflammation stemming from various causes&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Arthritis in the back that causes bones to get larger&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Instability of the spine, pushing one vertebrae a little forward&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Don&rsquo;t Put Off Treatment</strong><span style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you feel shooting pains down your leg, you may suspect you have sciatica. However, if you feel the desire to lean to one side, you may be doing so to make space for a pinched nerve. Not all leg discomfort is caused by a sciatic nerve being compressed. It could be caused by lumbar radiculopathy, which is a condition that affects the lower back. Cervical radiculopathy refers to pain that originates in your neck, and this condition specifically stems from the cervical spine. Seeking treatment for <strong><a href=\"https://medium.com/@sumitzlab/understanding-cervical-neck-pain-causes-symptoms-and-treatment-options-5f8691b2174c\">Cervical Neck Pain</a></strong> earlier may improve your quality of life.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The disease resolves itself in one to two weeks for half of the people who have a pinched nerve. In addition, 90 percent of those who have a pinched nerve recover within six to twelve weeks. However, depending on the severity of the damage, those weeks or months can be painful. If the pain is too severe for you to work, you should consult an <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>orthopedic clinic in pune</strong></a><strong>.</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Your doctor will most likely start you on a nerve pain medication to help you bear the pain until a nest treatment can be decided upon.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A corticosteroid injection, which decreases inflammation far faster than it would on its own, is one of the most effective treatment option your doctor would recommend. Typically, the steroid begins to reduce inflammation within three days.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>A surgical procedure is an option</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If medicine and corticosteroid injections do not help, or if these therapies produce weakening, surgery may be the next step. If the pinched nerve is caused by a herniated or ruptured disc, a neurosurgeon may need to conduct a treatment called a microdiscectomy. A more invasive operation, such as fusion or decompression, may be required at times.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To choose the best orthopedic treatment in Baner, our doctor will most likely prescribe an electromyography nerve conduction study, also known as an EMG - NCS, to identify what is going on in your body. This is a method of determining the location of a blockage or injury in the nerves by testing the electrical activity in the nerves.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Physiotherapy for Pinched Nerve</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Physical therapy may be recommended after any course of treatment for a pinched nerve. Your physical therapy approach will most likely focus on your back muscles and core, and may involve the following components:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Teaching you correct movement techniques, such as picking things up.&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Showing you how to stretch your spine using your muscles.&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Making a home fitness routine.&nbsp;</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Sticking to the exercises, like with any physical treatment or exercise plan, is the greatest way to stay healthy and prevent future injuries.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/684466145_28_01_2023_12_59_59.jpg','2023-01-28 07:28:12','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(69,'here-we-have-the-dietary-recommendation-by-dietician-in-baner','Here We Have The Dietary Recommendation By Dietician In Baner','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','The proper understanding of the right nutrition at the right time has a significant impact on the body. As the body gets older, the diet routine also...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The proper understanding of the right nutrition at the right time has a significant impact on the body. As the body gets older, the diet routine also changes because the body makes more demands to fulfill its requirements. The Dr. Sumitz Clinic is the </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><strong>physiotherapy clinic in Pune</strong></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, and they have an excellent team that has in-depth knowledge about nutrition at the time of physiotherapy treatment and orthopedic surgery. Here we have breakdown the list of </span><strong>dietary recommendations by the dietician in Baner</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> and this is important to read the whole -</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Here is the list of foods that are recommended for the orthopedic patients</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Dairy products like milk and cheese&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Kale, spinach, broccoli</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Salmon, Tuna, and sardines&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Figs, Walnuts, almonds&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Tofu, red kidney beans</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Soybean, QUINOA, and seafood</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Things to avoid -&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Sugar rich foods&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Excess salt in foods</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Refined carbohydrates&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Packaged food products&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Alcohol and caffeine&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">In work, an individual must avoid heavy lifting, minimize screen time, avoid stairs, and don&rsquo;t avoid pain.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Here is the list of foods that are recommended for the physiotherapy patients</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Fruits, vegetables, and dietary fibers&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Cereals like maize, and rice&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Meat, fish, and eggs; legumes&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Unsaturated vegetable oils&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Things to avoid:&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Consume less meat.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Minimize the excess salt and sugar in foods&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Avoid processed, fried, and baked foods.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Health Advice That Orthopedic Doctors Recommend For The BONES AND JOINTS&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The orthopedic doctors of the </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\"><strong>orthopedic clinic in Baner</strong></a><span style=\"background-color:rgb(246, 247, 247); color:rgb(241, 99, 52)\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">&nbsp;have given suggestions to make your bones healthy and strong.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong>Never skip a meal -&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Healthy foods are vital to making bones strong, and a balanced diet of high-quality foods will keep your health in good shape. But the majority of people skip meals due to work and procrastination habits. As a result, it weakens the bones and joints of the body because the body is unable to get proper nutrition when it needs it most.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong>Mobility is important -&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Physical activity is as important as food and water in an individual&#39;s life. Statistics show that people who are physically active are less likely to get hurt in an accident. Physiotherapists do the same thing; they encourage the physical movement of the bones and joints.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong>Avoid excess medicine -&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">For a normal cold and cough, it is the habit of an individual to take medicine to get instant relief. Excessive intake of medicine causes problems with the kidney and liver, diabetes, allergies, dizziness, and many more. Also, people tend to avoid medicines after a certain age because they can&#39;t take them correctly. Physiotherapy comes to the rescue, and this therapy alleviates the pain and improves functionality.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong>Avoid alcohol and cigarette -&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The dangerous chemicals in alcohol and cigarettes make the bones weaker and hurt their health. Try to avoid these two things as much as possible; the more you avoid them, the better your bone health will be.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><strong>Stay connected with any orthopedic doctor.&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Certain differences in food, daily activities, and other factors occur as the body ages. As a result, maintaining contact with a physiotherapist or orthopedic doctor is critical. Bone problems will be less likely to happen if you follow their advice and get checked regularly.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wrapping Up -&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Dr. Sumitz provides the best </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-treatment\"><strong>physiotherapy treatment in Pune</strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">,</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> and they have an expert team in their clinic that helps make you strong enough. Most people still don&#39;t know what to eat when they have problems with their bones and joints. The whole point of this article is to tell you in detail what the dietician in Baner suggested for your diet.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<quillbot-extension-portal></quillbot-extension-portal>','uploads/product/11466638_28_01_2023_02_37_07.jpg','2023-01-28 09:07:07','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(70,'the-causes-and-treatment-of-sciatica-pain','The Causes and Treatment of Sciatica Pain ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Up to forty percent of the world&#39;s population suffers from sciatica, making it one of the most widespread causes of nerve pain. Rather than being...','<p>Up to forty percent of the world&#39;s population suffers from sciatica, making it one of the most widespread causes of nerve pain. Rather than being a disorder of its own, the discomfort is actually a sign of various other lower back and spinal conditions. The condition has gained attention because Grammy-winning singer Adele revealed to fans that she has had sciatica and other back problems since she was a teenager. The 34-year-old performer sought an explanation for why she has recently started &quot;wobbling&quot; on stage.The sciatic nerve, which is the longest and thickest nerve in your body, becomes inflamed or irritated. The nerve starts in your buttock region and travels down your legs before branching into your foot and toes. The nerve really starts as five spinal nerve roots. A wide range of medical issues can lead to sciatica. It is one among the more prevalent signs and symptoms of lower back conditions, including situations where a disk presses against a spinal nerve. From one individual to the next, pain and symptoms might differ greatly. There could be excruciating pain that travels down one or both legs.&nbsp; There could be a throbbing ache that starts in the buttocks and extends to the knee and ankle. Many various positions can cause discomfort, but for some people, standing with more weight on one side than the other might trigger it. Additionally, some patients report having tingling and numbness in their toes, foot, and legs.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Sciatica is associated with numerous risk factors, including:</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Smoking&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Osteoarthritis&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Inactive lifestyle&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Being overweight&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Lower back or spinal injuries&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Poor weight-lifting technique&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Diabetes (causes nerve damage)&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Job (particularly those requiring heavy lifting)&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Weak core muscles (in the abdomen and back)&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Aging (degeneration of bone tissue and spinal disk)&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Sciatica treatment</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sciatica is a sign of other issues, which is an essential fact to keep in mind. Therefore, attempting self-diagnosis and therapy may be detrimental. Finding the cause of the issue is one of the first objectives of treatment.&nbsp; The answer to that question can help determine treatment.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sciatica can often be treated at home with ice/cold packs, mild stretches, and over-the-counter painkillers for swelling, discomfort, and inflammation. However, waiting two months before seeking medical attention can significantly delay recovery time. Due to this reason booking an instant appointment with the <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">orthopaedic surgeon in baner</span></a> for relief is recommended&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment options include:</strong><span style=\"color:rgb(31, 78, 121)\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>&gt; Physical therapy: </strong>Your therapist will work with you on a range of potential solutions. &quot;Directional preferences&quot; may be utilized to find postures that reduce pain and other symptoms if disk compression is to blame. To prevent an imbalance that results in muscular tension, you can utilize stretches and exercises to improve the stability of your core. Another approach is &quot;dry needling,&quot; in which muscle trigger points are reduced by inserting tiny, flexible needles into the muscle belly. This can assist lower muscular tension.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>&gt; The prescription medications: </strong>More stronger medications can aid in the battle against pain, inflammation, and muscle spasms that may be causing your sciatica.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>&gt; Spinal injections: </strong>Steroids may decrease the discomfort and swelling near the nerves. These frequently offer relief for three months or longer.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:rgb(31, 78, 121)\">&gt;</span><strong> Surgery:</strong> Different surgical techniques could be offered if other therapies are unsuccessful in relieving the symptoms.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Does it last forever?</strong><span style=\"color:rgb(31, 78, 121)\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Thankfully, sciatica is usually curable without surgery. The majority of patients (80% to 90%) can overcome it with the help of physical therapy and medicines. Younger individuals often recover fully in one to two months; elderly patients typically take longer to do so.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The illness unfortunately has an 80% recurrence rate. You must thus continue practicing good posture, stretches, and exercises even after a sciatica episode has passed. The <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">orthopedic doctor in baner</span></a> of DR. SUMITZ clinic can assist you in creating a daily regimen at home to reduce the chances of a flare-up.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You will also learn to recognize early warning signs that can help you avoid a debilitating episode. For instance, you can have stiffness in your buttocks muscles after a long day spent in amusement parks, which could cause more inflammation. You&#39;ll be able to recognize when it&#39;s appropriate to stretch more to assist those muscles to relax.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopaedic-center\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">orthopedic clinic in Pune</span></a> and <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy clinic in pune</span></a> &ndash; DR. SUMITZ comes in the list of &ldquo;highly search clinic in Pune and Baner&rdquo; for physiotherapy and orthopedics.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<quillbot-extension-portal></quillbot-extension-portal>','uploads/product/736324056_04_02_2023_12_46_37.jpg','2023-02-04 06:20:25','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(71,'rhabdo-the-negative-effects-of-intense-workout','Rhabdo: The Negative Effects of Intense Workout ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Most of us are aware that injuring oneself by rushing into an extreme workout after several months of inactivity. For weekend warriors, that often tra...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Most of us are aware that injuring oneself by rushing into an extreme workout after several months of inactivity. For weekend warriors, that often translates to pulled muscle or shin splints.&nbsp; Rest, a heating pad or ibuprofen are often effective treatments for most of these adverse effects.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Not so with rhabdomyolysis, sometimes known as rhabdo, a terrible side-effect of intense exercise that most gym goers are unaware of.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Cases of this are rare but serious ailments, formerly thought to afflict only hardcore athletes, fitness fanatics, or military warriors, have grown increasingly widespread as strenuous exercise pursuits like extreme weightlifting, ultrarunning, and spinning gain popularity.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Rhabdo: What Is It?</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Rhabdomyolysis, as it is often known, is a potentially fatal condition characterized by excessive muscle breakdown. Some muscle degradation is common after frequent exercises. This breakdown causes the muscles to regenerate and become stronger.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">When your body Is under too much stress, the muscular fibers are damaged, and rhabdo might occur. The majority of occurrences of this illness occur when a person pushes himself too hard in a new sports activity. Newcomers to a spine class, CrossFit facility, or session with a fitness trainer may overdo it without realizing it.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Here are the tell-tale signs</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">The most noticeable sign of rhabdo is dark, tea-colored urine that appears one to three days after intense activity. Many individuals misinterpret this symptom for hematuria, which is blood in the urine produced by overstretching a muscle.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">This discoloration, however, is caused by a poisonous protein called myoglobin in rhabdo. These toxic proteins are released into the circulation as overused muscles break down. When these proteins accumulate in the kidneys, they might cause lasting damage. Acute renal failure is the most significant consequence of rhabdo, occurring in around 15% of people diagnosed with the illness.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Rhabdo may cause compartment syndrome, a painful disease that develops when pressure within the damaged muscles accumulates to hazardous levels, producing significant swelling and decreased blood flow. Surgery is frequently required to restore normal blood flow and prevent muscle tissue from dying from compartment syndrome.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">The following are other symptoms of rhabdo:</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Alcohol abuse</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Certain medications</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Illicit drug use</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Muscle diseases</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Muscle trauma</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">The treatment of rhabdo</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Don&#39;t be panic if you feel any aches and pains after your workout. You&#39;re probably alright if you&#39;re aching all over and you can take help of a physiotherapist, to know more about your pain and get rid of it. Dr.Sumitz is one of the best&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">physiotherapy doctor in Baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\"> who can help you to deal with it. Rhabdo symptoms are more concentrated. However, if you are concerned that you may have rhabdo, please consult your doctor. Rhabdo can be fatal if left untreated.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">If your doctor diagnoses rhabdo, treatment will involve significant volumes of fluids, including IV treatment, to flush the kidneys and help avoid damage. Most patients recover if caught early, and rhabdo is not considered a chronic illness. Hydration, an exercise break, and gradually resuming exercises under the supervision of a doctor are typically enough.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Keeping yourself safe at the gym</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">A difficult workout will not send most of us to the hospital on its own. However, there are a few basic things you may do to reduce your risk of rhabdo. </span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">You can consult to a physiotherapist and work according to his guidance to keep yourself away from rhabdo and if you are</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">&nbsp;looking for </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">physiotherapy clinic in Pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\"> then you are at the right place.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">To reduce the possibility of damage, ease into the new exercise routine gradually. It&#39;s okay to be new in class.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">If you&#39;ve taken a break from exercising, don&#39;t return with the same intensity as you went. Begin with less weights or a slower speed and gradually work your way back up to where you were.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Hydrate, hydrate, and then some more. Most persons who get rhabdo as a result of strenuous exercise are also dehydrated. Drink plenty of water before, during, and after any workout routine</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Know your limitations and stick to them. If you are having difficulty, slow down or stop. It is OK to stop a class or request that a trainer reduces the intensity.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Before working out, avoid taking excessive dosages of creatine supplements or drinking caffeinated energy beverages.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">Avoid exercising in hot and humid conditions</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n','uploads/product/647032351_07_02_2023_12_42_14.jpg','2023-02-07 07:12:14','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(72,'sports-injuries-how-to-avoid-them','Sports Injuries: How to Avoid Them ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','You can&#39;t avoid the risk of injury whether you jog, lift weights, play golf, or participate in another sport. It&#39;s not always terrible luck. H...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">You can&#39;t avoid the risk of injury whether you jog, lift weights, play golf, or participate in another sport. It&#39;s not always terrible luck. However, there are measures to protect yourself against harm, such as:</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Warming up</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Stretching</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Cooling down</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Not doing too much, too fast</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Listening to your body</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Too much time and focus devoted to a single activity, especially for younger athletes, might make you prone to injury.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">People sometimes underestimate the importance of cross-training, which may help your body prepare for the stress and strains of sports.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">With that in mind, let&rsquo;s take a look at some of the most prevalent injuries in seven major sports and how to reduce your chances of being wounded.</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Tennis</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Tennis elbow is, predictably, the most common injury (lateral epicondylitis). This painful ailment is caused by an inflammation or micro-tearing of the tendons that link the forearm muscles on the outside of the elbow. Overuse and poor technique can also contribute to injury.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">You can protect yourself against this injury by not overdoing it.&nbsp; However, it is more vital to ensure that you are practicing good swing technique and that your racket suits you. Rackets that are overly heavy or have an incorrectly sized grip can put additional strain on your forearm. For more detailed information you can contact dr.sumitz </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy clinic in pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Biking</span>&nbsp;</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Aside from inevitable accidents, lower back and knee injuries are among the most prevalent dangers to bikers. Both are caused by a mix of overuse, incorrect sitting posture, and equipment difficulties.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">To avoid them, work on improving your core strength and riding posture. Also, make sure your bike fits you properly. A saddle that is excessively low might place unnecessary strain on the front of your knee or the kneecap. Your hamstrings might be strained if your saddle is too high.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Running</span>&nbsp;</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Plantar fasciitis and IT band syndrome are two common ailments among runners. However, one of the most common injuries is a stress fracture, which is a tiny crack or bruise in one of the foot&#39;s numerous bones. It&#39;s an overuse injury that happens to runners who don&#39;t know when to cut back or take a break. Stress fractures can also develop in elderly runners with compromised bone health.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Several techniques can help you lower your risk of stress fractures: Make sure you&#39;re using excellent running shoes with good shock absorption; eat a diet high in Vitamin D and calcium; and don&#39;t push your body (or your feet) too hard or too fast. If you are still struggling with pain and looking for&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">orthopedic clinic in pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">then you are at right place.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Lifting weights</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">&nbsp;</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Weightlifters frequently suffer from muscular strains and lower back ailments. Lifting weights is all about technique. Take deadlifting as an example. The weightlifter looks to be bent over the barbell, preparing to raise it off the ground to the untrained eye. However, this strategy is hazardous to your back. Instead, the weightlifter is using his arms to stabilize the barbell while attempting to force his feet through the floor.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">The key to preventing injury is to focus on core strengthening workouts with a strong emphasis on body mechanics and appropriate weightlifting form. If you are struggling with body pain then it&#39;s best to see a physiotherapist or visit Dr.Sumitz for </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">orthopedic doctor in baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Swimming</span>&nbsp;</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Shoulder injuries are one of the most common dangers to swimmers. This includes rotator cuff strains, tendinitis, and shoulder impingement. Overtraining, combined with poor stroke mechanics, breathing skills, and flexibility, can all lead to these ailments.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">To avoid these ailments, make sure you give your body sufficient time to heal between workouts. Use workouts to strengthen your core and ensure appropriate stroke mechanics.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:rgb(57, 56, 57)\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<quillbot-extension-portal></quillbot-extension-portal>','uploads/product/291688357_20_02_2023_03_49_58.jpg','2023-02-20 10:17:42','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(73,'the-role-of-physical-therapy-in-orthopaedic-treatment-importance-benefits-and-more',' The Role of Physical Therapy in Orthopaedic Treatment - Importance, Benefits, and More ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Orthopaedic injuries and conditions can cause pain, discomfort, and restrict mobility. They can be debilitating and have a significant impact on one&r...','<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Orthopaedic injuries and conditions can cause pain, discomfort, and restrict mobility. They can be debilitating and have a significant impact on one&rsquo;s quality of life. Orthopaedic treatment is the specialized care for these conditions, and </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:windowtext\">physiotherapy </span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">plays a vital role in it. In this blog, we will discuss the importance and benefits of physical therapy in orthopaedic treatment, and why you should consider visiting an orthopaedic clinic in Pune that offers physiotherapy services.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Importance of Physical Therapy in Orthopaedic Treatment</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Physical therapy is an essential component of orthopaedic treatment because it helps to improve mobility, flexibility, and strength, while also reducing pain and inflammation. A </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">orthopedic doctor near me</span></a><span style=\"color:windowtext\"> </span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">can help you recover from injuries or conditions affecting bones, joints, muscles, tendons, and ligaments. Physical therapy may be recommended by an orthopaedic surgeon in Baner or a general practitioner, depending on the nature of the injury or condition.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Benefits of Physical Therapy in Orthopaedic Treatment</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Reduces Pain and Inflammation: Physical therapy can help reduce pain and inflammation in the affected area. Therapeutic exercises, stretching, and massage can improve blood circulation, increase range of motion, and reduce inflammation.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Improves Mobility and Flexibility: Physical therapy can help improve mobility and flexibility, making it easier to perform everyday tasks. By targeting specific muscles and joints, physical therapy can help you regain strength and stability.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Enhances Strength and Endurance: Physical therapy can help enhance strength and endurance. Strengthening exercises can help increase muscle mass, while aerobic exercises can help improve cardiovascular health.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Speeds up Recovery: Physical therapy can help speed up recovery by promoting healing and reducing the risk of complications. By working with a physiotherapy doctor in Baner, you can recover faster from your injury or condition.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Prevents Future Injuries: Physical therapy can help prevent future injuries by strengthening the affected area and correcting any imbalances or weaknesses. By improving your overall physical condition, you can reduce the risk of reinjury.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Choosing an Orthopaedic Clinic in Pune that Offers Physical Therapy</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">If you are experiencing pain, discomfort, or mobility issues due to an orthopaedic condition or injury, it is important to seek timely treatment. An&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">orthopedic clinic in baner</span></a><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;that offers physical therapy services can help you achieve optimal recovery outcomes.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">When choosing an orthopaedic clinic in Pune, consider the following factors:</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Expertise: Choose a clinic that has experienced orthopaedic surgeons and </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">orthopaedic center in baner</span></a><span style=\"color:windowtext\"> who specialize in treating your condition.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Range of Services: Look for a clinic that offers a comprehensive range of services, including diagnosis, treatment, surgery, and physical therapy.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Reputation: Check the clinic&rsquo;s reputation by reading patient reviews and ratings online.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Facilities: Look for a clinic that has modern facilities and equipment to provide the best </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-treatment\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">physiotherapy treatment in pune</span></a><span style=\"color:windowtext\">.</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Conclusion</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:windowtext\">Physical therapy is a crucial aspect of orthopaedic treatment, and it can help reduce pain, and inflammation, and improve mobility, strength, and flexibility. If you are looking for an orthopaedic clinic in Pune that offers physical therapy services, consider Dr. Sumitz,&nbsp;Our team of experienced orthopaedic surgeons and&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\">physiotherapy doctor in baner</span></a><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;specialize in treating a wide range of orthopaedic problems, and we use the latest techniques and equipment to ensure optimal recovery outcomes. Contact us to schedule an appointment today!</span><span style=\"color:windowtext\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<quillbot-extension-portal></quillbot-extension-portal>','uploads/product/180686211_22_02_2023_02_16_53.jpg','2023-02-22 08:46:53','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(74,'how-physiotherapy-prevents-and-heals-sports-injuries','How physiotherapy prevents and heals sports injuries ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','&nbsp;\r\n\r\nAthletes are prone to injuries, and those injuries can significantly impact their performance, causing them to miss training, competition, o...','<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Athletes are prone to injuries, and those injuries can significantly impact their performance, causing them to miss training, competition, or even retire. While injuries are a common occurrence in the world of sports, they don&#39;t have to be a death sentence. Physiotherapy is a specialized field of healthcare that can help athletes prevent and recover from injuries. If you are a Athlete and looking for&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy clinic in pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;then you are at right place.&nbsp;In this blog, we will explore how physiotherapy can help athletes prevent and recover from injuries.</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(209, 213, 219)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(209, 213, 219)\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Preventing Injuries with Physiotherapy</span>&nbsp;:-</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Prevention is always better than cure. A physiotherapist can help an athlete reduce their risk of injury by identifying areas of weakness, imbalance, or overuse. By performing a thorough assessment of an athlete&#39;s physical condition, a physiotherapist can determine what areas need to be strengthened and what exercises can help improve the athlete&#39;s performance.&nbsp;In this way, the physiotherapist can help an athlete prevent injuries before they occur.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">One of the most effective ways physiotherapy can help prevent injuries is through the development of a personalized exercise program, </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy Baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"> can help you with personalized exercise program. The program will be tailored to the athlete&#39;s specific needs and will focus on strengthening areas that are prone to injury. For example, a runner may need to work on their glutes, hips, and quads to improve their running technique and prevent knee injuries. Similarly, a basketball player may need to work on their ankle strength to reduce the risk of ankle sprains.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Recovering from Injuries with Physiotherapy</span>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Injuries are almost inevitable in the world of sports. However, with proper care and treatment, an athlete can recover from an injury and return to their sport with improved performance. Physiotherapy can play a crucial role in an athlete&#39;s recovery by helping to manage pain, swelling, and inflammation. A physiotherapist can also provide guidance on when it is safe to return to training and competition.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">One of the most important things a physiotherapist can do to help an athlete recover from an injury is to provide rehabilitation exercises. Rehabilitation exercises are designed to help an athlete regain their strength, flexibility, and range of motion. These exercises are tailored to the athlete&#39;s specific injury and are often progressive in nature. As the athlete progresses through the rehabilitation program, the exercises become more challenging, allowing the athlete to regain their fitness gradually.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Physiotherapy Techniques for Athletes</span>&nbsp;-</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Physiotherapists use a range of techniques to help athletes prevent and recover from injuries. Some of the most common techniques used include:</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Manual therapy &ndash; This involves hands-on techniques such as massage, stretching, and mobilization of joints and soft tissues. Manual therapy can help improve blood flow to injured areas, reduce pain and stiffness, and improve range of motion.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Exercise therapy &ndash; Exercise therapy involves specific exercises designed to strengthen weak areas, improve flexibility, and restore range of motion. These exercises are often tailored to the athlete&#39;s specific sport and injury.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Cryotherapy &ndash; Cryotherapy involves the use of cold therapy to reduce pain and inflammation. This can be done through ice packs or ice baths.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Conclusion</span>&nbsp;</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">In conclusion, physiotherapy can play a crucial role in an athlete&#39;s performance. By helping to prevent injuries and providing rehabilitation for injuries that do occur, physiotherapy near me can help athletes stay healthy and achieve their goals. If you&#39;re an athlete, consider incorporating physiotherapy into your training program to prevent injuries and optimize your performance. Remember, prevention is always better than cure.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/444835652_15_03_2023_04_55_20.jpg','2023-03-15 11:25:20','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(75,'the-importance-of-x-rays-for-knee-and-leg-injuries','The Importance of X-Rays for Knee and Leg Injuries ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','When you suffer from a knee or leg injury, it can be challenging to determine what is happening inside your body. While some injuries may be visible o...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">When you suffer from a knee or leg injury, it can be challenging to determine what is happening inside your body. While some injuries may be visible on the surface, others may be hidden beneath the skin. This is where X-rays come in. X-rays are a powerful tool that can help doctors get a better understanding of what is going on inside your body. In this blog post, we will discuss the importance of X-rays for knee and leg injuries. If you live in Pune and are looking for the best </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy clinic in Pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"> then you are at the right place, continue reading this blog to know the importance of X-rays for knee and leg injuries.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Quick and Easy Diagnosis</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">X-rays are a quick and easy way to diagnose knee and leg injuries. They are non-invasive and can be done in a matter of minutes. X-rays use a small amount of radiation to create images of the inside of your body. These images can help doctors see if there are any fractures, dislocations, or other abnormalities that may be causing your pain or discomfort.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Accuracy: X-rays are extremely accurate. They can detect even the smallest of fractures or abnormalities that may not be visible to the naked eye. This means that doctors can get a more accurate diagnosis and create a more effective treatment plan. Without an accurate diagnosis, it can be difficult to treat knee and leg injuries properly, which can lead to further pain and discomfort down the road.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Monitoring the Healing Process: X-rays are also important for monitoring the healing process of knee and leg injuries. By taking X-rays at regular intervals, doctors can see how the injury is healing and make any necessary adjustments to the treatment plan. This ensures that the injury is healing properly and that you are on the right track to a full recovery.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Prevention of Further Injury</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">X-rays can help prevent further injury. If there is an underlying issue that is causing your knee or leg pain, an X-ray can help identify it. This means that doctors can create a treatment plan that addresses the root cause of your pain, rather than just treating the symptoms.</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Treatment Plan: An accurate X-ray diagnosis can help doctors create a treatment plan that is tailored to your specific injury. This means that you will receive the appropriate treatment for your injury, which can help speed up the healing process and reduce pain and discomfort.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Identifying Hidden Injuries: In some cases, knee and leg injuries may not be visible on the surface. X-rays can help identify hidden injuries that may be causing your pain or discomfort. By identifying these injuries, doctors can create an appropriate treatment plan and prevent further injury.</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Conclusion</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">X-rays are an essential tool for diagnosing and treating knee and leg injuries. They are quick, accurate, and non-invasive, making them an ideal tool for doctors. X-rays can help identify fractures, dislocations, and other abnormalities that may not be visible to the eyes. They can also help monitor the healing process and prevent further injury. If you are experiencing knee or leg pain and looking for&nbsp; </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/x-ray-center\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">X-ray center in Pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">, then you are at the right place. It is important to see a doctor and get an X-ray to ensure an accurate diagnosis and effective treatment plan.</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<quillbot-extension-portal></quillbot-extension-portal>','uploads/product/896280775_22_03_2023_03_29_03.jpg','2023-03-22 09:59:03','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(76,'the-importance-of-posture-in-spine-health','The Importance of Posture in Spine Health ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Your posture is the position in which you hold your body while standing, sitting, or lying down. It is an essential aspect of overall health, particul...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Your posture is the position in which you hold your body while standing, sitting, or lying down. It is an essential aspect of overall health, particularly spine health. Poor posture can lead to a range of health problems, including back pain, neck pain, and even headaches. In this blog, we will discuss the link between posture and spine health, the benefits of good posture, tips for improving posture, and the impact of poor posture on spine health.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">The Link Between Posture and Spine Health</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">The spine is the foundation of the body, and good posture is essential for maintaining its health. When you have poor posture, it puts extra stress on your spine, which can lead to misalignment and even injury. Over time, this can cause chronic pain and other health problems. Poor posture can also affect the discs, muscles, and ligaments in your spine, making them more susceptible to wear and tear.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">The Benefits of Good Posture</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Maintaining good posture has a range of benefits for overall health, including improved circulation, reduced risk of injury, and better breathing. Good posture can also help you look and feel more confident, as it is associated with a positive and assertive attitude. Other benefits of good posture include:</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Reduced risk of back pain: good posture helps distribute the weight of the body evenly, reducing the strain on the spine and reducing the risk of back pain.</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Improved digestion: good posture helps the digestive organs function properly, reducing the risk of digestive problems.</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Better balance and coordination: good posture helps improve balance and coordination, reducing the risk of falls and other injuries.</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Improved mood: good posture is associated with a positive mood and reduced stress levels.</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Tips for Improving Posture</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">If you are looking for </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy clinic in Pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"> to improve your posture, then you are at the right place. Here are some tips by our experts to improve your posture -</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Always be </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">mindful of your posture throughout the day.</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Pay attention to how you are standing, sitting, and walking, and make corrections as needed.</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Keep your shoulders back and down and engage your core muscles to support your spine.</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Take frequent breaks if you sit or stand for long periods. Stretch, move around, and change your position to reduce the strain on your spine.</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Use ergonomic furniture and equipment to support good posture, such as an ergonomic chair and a standing desk.</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Exercise regularly to strengthen your core and back muscles, which can help support good posture.</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">The Impact of Poor Posture</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Poor posture can have serious consequences for spine health. It can lead to spinal misalignment, herniated discs, and chronic pain. Poor posture can also affect other areas of the body, such as the shoulders, neck, and hips. Over time, the damage caused by poor posture can become irreversible. Poor posture can also lead to a range of other health problems, including digestive problems, poor circulation, and reduced lung capacity. To protect yourself from the impact of poor posture you can consult&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">orthopedic doctor in baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;or local physiologists in your area.</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Conclusion</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Good posture is essential for maintaining spine health and overall health. By being mindful of your posture and making corrections as needed, you can reduce the risk of injury and chronic pain and improve your quality of life. If you are experiencing back or neck pain, consult with a healthcare professional to determine the underlying cause and develop a treatment plan that includes good posture practices. With proper attention to your posture, you can enjoy a healthier and more comfortable life.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<quillbot-extension-portal></quillbot-extension-portal>','uploads/product/186733599_27_03_2023_01_51_59.jpg','2023-03-27 08:21:59','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(77,'common-spine-conditions-causes-symptoms-and-treatment-options','Common Spine Conditions: Causes, Symptoms, and Treatment Options','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','The spine is an essential part of our body that provides support and stability to our upper body. It consists of a series of bones called vertebrae, w...','<p>The spine is an essential part of our body that provides support and stability to our upper body. It consists of a series of bones called vertebrae, which are separated by discs that act as cushions between them. However, spine conditions can arise due to numerous factors that can cause pain, discomfort, and mobility issues. In this blog, we will discuss the most common spine conditions, their causes, symptoms, and treatment options and if there are some questions in your mind like - <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/how-physiotherapy-prevents-and-heals-sports-injuries\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy doctor near me</span></a> or <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/orthopedic-treatment-for-all-your-joints-and-bones-problems\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">orthopedic doctor near me</span></a> then you are at the right place.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Herniated Disc:&nbsp;</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>A herniated disc is a condition where one of the discs in the spine slips out of place and presses on a nerve, causing pain, numbness, and weakness in the arms or legs. This condition can occur due to age-related wear and tear or injury. If you live in Baner and are looking for <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy Baner</span></a> then you are in the right place.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Symptoms of a herniated disc include:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Pain in the neck, back, arms, or legs&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Numbness or tingling sensation in the affected area&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Weakness in the affected area&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Difficulty in walking or standing&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Treatment options for a herniated disc include:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>physical therapy&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>pain management&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>surgery.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Spinal Stenosis:&nbsp;</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Spinal stenosis is a condition where the spaces within the spine narrow, putting pressure on the nerves and spinal cord, Spinal stenosis occurs most often in the lower back and the neck. This condition can occur due to age-related degeneration, injury, or genetic factors. If you live in Pune and are looking for <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/general-physical-therapy\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy treatment in Pune</span></a> then you are at the right place, you can also visit your local physiotherapist and consult with them.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Symptoms of spinal stenosis include:&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Pain in the neck, back, arms, or legs&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Numbness or tingling sensation in the affected area&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Weakness in the affected area&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Difficulty in walking or standing&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Treatment options for spinal stenosis include:&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>physical therapy&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>pain management&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>surgery</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Scoliosis:&nbsp;</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Scoliosis is a condition where the spine curves to the side, causing an abnormal posture. This condition can occur due to genetic factors or unknown reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Symptoms of scoliosis include:&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Uneven shoulders or waist&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>A visible curve in the spine&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Back pain or discomfort&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Treatment options for scoliosis include:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>physical therapy&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Bracing&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>surgery&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Degenerative Disc Disease:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Degenerative disc disease is a condition where the discs between the vertebrae in the spine break down, causing pain and stiffness in the back. This condition can occur due to age-related wear and tear or injury.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Symptoms of degenerative disc disease include:&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Pain in the back or neck&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Stiffness in the back or neck&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Numbness or tingling sensation in the arms or legs&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Treatment options for degenerative disc disease include&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>physical therapy&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>pain management&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>surgery</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Osteoporosis:&nbsp;</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Osteoporosis is a condition where the bones become weak and brittle, making them more susceptible to fractures. This condition can occur due to age-related bone loss or hormonal changes.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Symptoms of osteoporosis include:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Back pain or discomfort&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Loss of height&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>A stooped posture&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Treatment options for osteoporosis include:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Medication&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>lifestyle changes&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>surgery.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Conclusion:&nbsp;</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Spine conditions can be debilitating and affect your quality of life. However, early diagnosis and treatment can help manage the symptoms and prevent further damage. If you experience any of the symptoms mentioned above, consult a spine specialist for a proper diagnosis and treatment plan. Remember to maintain a healthy lifestyle by exercising regularly, eating a balanced diet, and avoiding smoking and excessive alcohol consumption to prevent spine conditions.&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/700887206_28_03_2023_05_15_43.jpg','2023-03-28 11:45:43','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(78,'how-to-choose-the-right-orthopedic-surgeon','How to Choose the Right Orthopedic Surgeon ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','\r\n\r\nOrthopedic injuries or conditions can cause immense pain and discomfort, and finding the right orthopedic surgeon is crucial to ensure timely and...','<p><quillbot-extension-portal></quillbot-extension-portal></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Orthopedic injuries or conditions can cause immense pain and discomfort, and finding the right orthopedic surgeon is crucial to ensure timely and effective treatment. With so many options available, it can be overwhelming to choose the right one. If you&#39;re looking for an orthopedic doctor near you, this article will guide you through the process of selecting the right orthopedic surgeon for your needs.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Look for experience and qualifications</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The first step in choosing an orthopedic surgeon is to check their qualifications and experience. Look for a surgeon who has completed residency in orthopedics and has several years of experience in the field. The more experience a surgeon has, the more likely they are to have encountered and treated a wide range of orthopedic conditions.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ask for referrals</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Ask for referrals from your primary care physician, friends, family members, or colleagues who have received treatment for orthopedic conditions in the past. They can recommend an orthopedic surgeon based on their personal experience. You can also check online reviews and ratings to get a better idea of the surgeon&#39;s reputation.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Check for hospital affiliations</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Check for hospital affiliations of the orthopedic surgeon you are considering. A surgeon who is affiliated with a reputable hospital has access to advanced medical technology, and their practice is likely to be up to date with the latest techniques and procedures.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Consider the surgeon&#39;s communication style</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A good orthopedic surgeon should be able to communicate with their patients in a clear and concise manner. They should be willing to answer any questions you may have and explain the treatment plan in detail. If a surgeon rushes through the appointment or doesn&#39;t listen to your concerns, it may be best to consider another surgeon.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Look for a surgeon who specializes in your condition</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Orthopedic surgeons may specialize in specific areas of the body, such as the knees, hips, or shoulders. Look for a surgeon who specializes in treating your specific condition. For example, if you need <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/how-to-find-the-best-physiotherapy-clinic-in-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy treatment in Pune</span></a>, you can search for an<span style=\"background-color:transparent\"> </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">orthopedic surgeon in Baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent\"> </span>who specializes in physiotherapy. This ensures that you receive the most effective treatment for your condition.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Check for availability</strong>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Finally, consider the surgeon&#39;s availability. You don&#39;t want to wait weeks or months for an appointment, especially if you&#39;re experiencing severe pain or discomfort. Choose a surgeon who has a flexible schedule and can see you at a time that is convenient for you.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Physiotherapy is an important part of the recovery process for many orthopedic conditions. If you&#39;re looking for a<span style=\"background-color:transparent\"> </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">physiotherapy clinic in Baner</span></a>, look for a clinic that has experienced physiotherapists and modern equipment. You can also ask for referrals from your orthopedic surgeon.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In conclusion, finding the right orthopedic surgeon can make all the difference in the outcome of your treatment. Take the time to research and consider multiple options before deciding. Remember to consider experience, qualifications, communication style, hospital affiliations, specialization, and availability. By doing so, you can choose an orthopedic surgeon who will provide the best possible care for your condition.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/706356349_19_04_2023_03_39_03.jpg','2023-04-19 10:09:03','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(79,'the-role-of-nutrition-in-orthopedic-health-and-physiotherapy-recovery','The Role of Nutrition in Orthopedic Health and Physiotherapy Recovery ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Orthopedic problems can be difficult to manage, especially when it comes to healing. Physiotherapy can help people recover from injuries, but it invol...','<p>Orthopedic problems can be difficult to manage, especially when it comes to healing. Physiotherapy can help people recover from injuries, but it involves more than just exercise. Nutrition is critical to orthopedic health and physiotherapy recovery. Here are some advice from the leading <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">orthopedic doctor in baner</span></a> on how to combine healthy nutrition to encourage a speedier and more efficient recovery.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h2>Protein-rich foods:&nbsp;&nbsp;</h2>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Protein is required for muscle repair following an injury. Protein-rich foods such as Sunflower seeds, flax seeds, fish, eggs, lentils, beans, and nuts can help speed up the healing process. To assist recuperation, the finest orthopedic specialist in Pune recommends ingesting at least 1g of protein per kilogram of body weight every day.&nbsp; Protein&#39;s healing ability should not be underestimated. Including these foods in your diet will help you heal faster and more effectively.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h2>Vitamins and minerals:&nbsp;&nbsp;</h2>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Calcium, vitamin D, and magnesium are vital nutrients for strong bones and joints. These nutrients are also important in lowering inflammation and supporting recovery. These nutrients can be obtained by eating foods such as dairy, leafy greens, nuts, and seeds.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h2>Omega-3 fatty acids:&nbsp;</h2>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Omega-3 fatty acids are well-known for their anti-inflammatory effects. These fatty acids can aid in the reduction of inflammation and discomfort associated with orthopedic injuries. Foods high in omega-3 fatty acids include fatty fish, flaxseeds, and chia seeds.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h2>Hydration:&nbsp;</h2>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Hydration is essential for normal physical function, and it is especially critical during the recovery process. Drinking plenty of water and other hydrating liquids such as coconut water, lemon water, and fresh juices will assist your body stay hydrated and encourage recovery.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h2>Fiber-rich foods:&nbsp;</h2>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Including fiber-rich foods in your diet, such as fruits and vegetables, whole grains, and legumes, can help regulate digestion and promote gut health. A healthy stomach is necessary for nutrition absorption, which is critical during the healing process.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In addition to these suggestions, it is critical to avoid processed meals, excessive sugar, and alcohol while in recovery. These foods can impede healing and increase inflammation, making it more difficult for your body to recover from an injury.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Physiotherapy, in addition to nutrition, can play an important role in orthopedic healing. Physiotherapy clinics in Pune provide a variety of services to assist people in recovering from injuries. Manual therapy, exercise therapy, electrotherapy, and other therapies are available. For those seeking specialist services such as sports physiotherapy or pediatric physiotherapy, a physiotherapy clinic in Baner is an ideal choice.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In conclusion, nutrition is critical to orthopedic health and physiotherapy recovery. You can encourage speedier healing and recovery by include protein-rich foods, vitamins and minerals, omega-3 fatty acids, water, and fiber-rich foods in your diet. Along with proper nutrition, physiotherapy can help persons heal rapidly and return to their normal life. Consult the <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopaedic-doctor\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:rgb(5, 99, 193)\">best orthopedic doctor in Pune</span></a> or a physiotherapy clinic in Pune for personalized advice and guidance.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/943790745_29_04_2023_05_04_48.jpg','2023-04-29 11:34:48','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(80,'5-reasons-why-physiotherapy-is-beneficial-for-orthopaedic-patients-in-baner','5 Reasons Why Physiotherapy is Beneficial for Orthopaedic Patients in Baner','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Accidents are unpredictable, and every doctor recommends surgery or an operation in every circumstance. This type of operation alters the patient&#39;...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Accidents are unpredictable, and every doctor recommends surgery or an operation in every circumstance. This type of operation alters the patient&#39;s existence and suspends all activities. However, every problem has a solution.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">Physiotherapy Baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> is the most effective method for dealing with this pitiful situation. Today, we will discuss the reasons why Baner orthopedic patients benefit from physiotherapy.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Increases flexibility-</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The greatest benefit of physiotherapy for orthopedic patients is increased mobility and flexibility of afflicted bones and body parts. The physiotherapist determines the frequency of sessions based on the type of surgery or procedure. In this session, they execute rehabilitative and mobility-enhancing exercises to restore strength. Most patients anticipate that they will be unable to move freely after any bone surgery or operation. However, physiotherapy is beneficial for them and ensures body flexibility.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Among the highlights of the exercises and techniques used to restore motion to the affected body part are the following:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Motion range exercises</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Stretching workouts</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Strength training</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Yoga&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Pilates&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Manual treatment</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Aquatic treatment</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Every exercise and training session is conducted in accordance with the degree of complication and the type of surgery. This is why you need a physiotherapist who is an expert in all aspects, including comfort.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Reduces discomfort and swelling</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">When performing operations or procedures on a patient&#39;s body parts, pain and inflammation are common. In physiotherapy, techniques such as ice or heat therapy, ultrasound, strapping, and electrical stimulation are used to reduce inflammation and pain. Due to the surgery or operation, the blood flow in that location is minimal, resulting in a deficiency of oxygen and nutrients. Physiotherapy makes everything possible and aides in the healing process. To accomplish the desired results, physiotherapists also educate their patients about posture, body mechanisms, and ergonomics.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Enhance the balance and coordination -</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Before surgery, the equilibrium and coordination of body parts are significantly better than after surgery. After any type of surgery on body parts, they become debilitated and unable to move freely, necessitating increased caution on the part of the patient. To restore balance and coordination, every orthopedic surgeon recommends consulting a physical therapist. Every session of physiotherapy results in changes in the mobility and function of the affected body regions. Tai chi or yoga, vestibular rehabilitation techniques, gait training, and other balance exercises alleviate problems by enhancing balance and coordination. The procedure will take time, but you must prepare for what lies ahead. For a period of time, you require assistance from walking and standing aids. However, it is all worthwhile.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Prevents subsequent injuries-</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Injuries are less likely to occur if the body&#39;s elements are resilient. Therefore, it is recommended to conduct exercises that restore strength and increase flexibility. Physiotherapy consists of a variety of exercise-based techniques and procedures designed to restore strength and prepare the body for future injuries. The following are some of the techniques that every patient encounters during physiotherapy sessions:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Physical therapy</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Functional exercise</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Neuromuscular re-education</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Taping&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Ergonomic appraisal-</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">With the aid of these techniques, the circulation of the body parts is enhanced and bone density is increased, thereby preventing the bones from breaking and collapsing.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">enhances the quality of existence overall</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Most patients favor physiotherapy over medical or equipment-based treatment methods in recent years. Another treatment causes the patient agony and discomfort, which disturbs their mental equilibrium. Physiotherapy is the solution to all problems, whether they involve sports injuries or post-surgery recovery. The exercises in the physiotherapy sessions assist you in achieving your goals after surgery.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Conclusion-</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Physiotherapy is an effective method for healing and restoring bone health. After surgery, it may be difficult for a person to stand on their own, both emotionally and physically. When the situation becomes severe, it will be impossible to treat fractured bones, fractures, etc. without surgery. However, after surgery, you should never neglect physiotherapy because the techniques involved will help you overcome the trauma of surgery. In addition to being the </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/orthopaedic-process\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">orthopedic center in Baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, Dr. Sumitz also has a team of physiotherapists in Baner. In this </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">physiotherapy clinic in Baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, patients have access to all the necessary amenities to improve their self-esteem and alleviate their discomfort.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/797066384_29_04_2023_05_15_57.jpg','2023-04-29 11:45:43','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(81,'how-to-find-the-best-orthopedic-doctor-near-you-tips-and-tricks','How to Find the Best Orthopedic Doctor Near You: Tips and Tricks','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Problems never knock on the door; they arrive unexpectedly and at any moment. To prepare for the problem, it is preferable to discover a solution befo...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Problems never knock on the door; they arrive unexpectedly and at any moment. To prepare for the problem, it is preferable to discover a solution beforehand. Similarly, it is crucial to locate the best orthopedic doctor prior to any accident. A sportsperson cannot refuse to play because their sport is their livelihood, and in the event of injury, no one can treat them better than an orthopedic physician. This blog discusses all of the pertinent tips and techniques for finding the best orthopedic doctor in your area.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Referrals-</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Bone and joint treatment is not everyone&#39;s cup of tea. There are numerous orthopedic physicians who claim to be experts, but the actuality is much different. Patients eventually experience these symptoms, but it is a waste of time, money, and effort to treat them. Referrals play an important role in this situation, and you can discover a trustworthy and qualified physician through the recommendations of family, friends, and healthcare professionals. Before you, they had already acquired experience and would only recommend you if it was worthwhile.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The sole purpose of online ratings and reviews is to acquire popularity and attract customers&#39; attention. Therefore, it is preferable to conduct research, attempt to interact with them and evaluate the orthopedic doctor&#39;s competence.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Investigating the Doctor&#39;s Qualifications-</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">In the minds of the patients, one&#39;s knowledge and specialization in a particular field make them credible. The degree, overall training, certifications, and mentors demonstrate their dedication. Additionally, verify if any malfeasance or disciplinary actions are imprinted on the documents. Validate their credentials and certifications thoroughly. The following are credentials that every orthopedic physician must possess:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Medical Degree</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Board accreditation</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Fellowship education</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Licensure&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Continuous training</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Professional affiliation</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If possible, attempt to acquire all of these credentials to establish their academic reputation. You can also contact them directly and request testimonials, training, the number of cases, success rates, and numerous other specifics.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Hospital Connections-</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">One can learn more about the doctor&#39;s specialized equipment and the number of patients they have treated as a result of hospital affiliations. In a hospital, they serve as assistants to their supervisors and manage a number of complex cases. When their mentors deem them qualified, they become senior agents and begin managing all cases independently. The hospital issues the doctor&#39;s affiliation only if they have served with complete dedication and cooperation. Additionally treated complex bone-related issues without error and met the objective. This hospital affiliation can be found in the directory of the same hospital.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Communication and convenience-</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The reason a patient expects their physicians to listen to them is that they have listened to everyone and found no solution. Every physician must attend to a patient&#39;s concerns about a particular complication. When a person listens to their patients more, the final decision he makes is appropriate and beneficial to them. In addition, the doctor&#39;s demeanor should be cheerful and cordial so that the patient never feels uneasy. The more at ease a patient feels, the more easily they can describe their distress to the physician.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Conclusion-</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The right&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-treatment\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250, 251, 251); color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">physiotherapy treatment in pune</span></a><span style=\"color:#1155cc\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250, 251, 251)\">&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">will aid you in overcoming almost all bone-related complications and prevailing in all of life&#39;s conflicts. Whether you are an athlete or a regular worker, bone-related complications are a prevalent occurrence in everyone&#39;s life. In the same way that athletes need coaches to improve their game, they also need an orthopedic physician to treat bone issues. However, finding a trustworthy doctor is a difficult task, which is why we are providing the following advice to help you discover the best </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250, 251, 251); color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">physiotherapy baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Also, visit our page for more details about their&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-clinic\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(246, 247, 247); color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">physiotherapy clinic in Pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, and call with any questions.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/271403131_01_05_2023_11_58_32.jpg','2023-05-01 06:28:32','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(82,'role-of-physiotherapy-treatment-in-sports-performance-optimization','Role of Physiotherapy Treatment in Sports performance optimization ','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Sports are beneficial to the mental and physical health of the body. These activities enhance both on-the-ground performance and overall well-being. M...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Sports are beneficial to the mental and physical health of the body. These activities enhance both on-the-ground performance and overall well-being. Maintaining physical fitness and health is a requirement for a sportsperson. Physiotherapy plays a crucial role in the life of an athlete by optimizing athletic performance. People have the misconception that </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/the-role-of-physical-therapy-in-orthopaedic-treatment-importance-benefits-and-more\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">physiotherapy treatment in pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> is only used to treat injuries or pain in the joints or bones. However, this is not the case. The fundamental purpose of physiotherapy is to strengthen bones or prevent injuries to bones and joints. Physiotherapists also guarantee the speedy recovery of minor and major sports injuries.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Today, we will discuss the significance of physiotherapy in optimizing athletic performance. Continue reading.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Understanding the requirements of the athlete</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Every athlete is quite unique, as is their sport. Some activities require the use of the hands, while others require the use of the legs. Depending on the sport, athletes&#39; requirements for optimizing performance vary. Physiotherapists in sports analyze the athlete&#39;s demands and develop a plan to meet those needs. Understanding the physical activity requirements of an individual athlete is essential for maximizing their performance. Physiotherapists evaluate an athlete&#39;s weaknesses and strengths and prescribe the best ways to improve their performance.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Injury Prevention-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">In sports, injuries are common, and these injuries may be minor or severe. From the first day of injury through the recovery process, sports physiotherapists lavish care on athletes. They utilize both manual and technical techniques to improve recovery and maintain game speed. After identifying the type of injury, he develops an individualized treatment plan consisting of physiotherapy exercises and modalities. They use a variety of pain management techniques, including cold, heat, and compression. Most of the time, trainers, </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-clinic\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">physiotherapy clinic in pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, and sports physicians collaborate for optimal results.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Conditioning and health improvement-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Doping is prohibited in sports, so athletes must now condition their bodies to recover rapidly from injuries and perform better on the field. </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/5-reasons-why-physiotherapy-is-beneficial-for-orthopaedic-patients-in-baner\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">Physiotherapy baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> constantly record the prior medical history of their athletes&#39; patients in order to assess the likelihood of a problem. After customizing the plan based on history and previous records, the sessions continue. Every athlete must perform at their highest level, which is why physical endurance and flexibility are required. Obtaining assistance from a skilled physiotherapist will resolve their issues and enable them to make a valiant entrance into the arena.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Recuperation and rehabilitation-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Once an athlete sustains an injury, coping with the pain and tension in order to return with the same level of enthusiasm becomes a major concern. In addition, playing with wounds or injuries is prohibited, according to the sports authorities&#39; legal committees. According to the injury, a variety of rehabilitation and recovery processes are being implemented. Ultrasound, heat or cold therapy, transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation (TENS), resistance, a rehabilitation program, and several manual therapy techniques.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">In the lives of athletes, suffering, and recovery coexist. Athletes can become anxious as a result of this type of mental stress if they cannot endure the agony of separation from the field. In this circumstance, a physiotherapist comprehends the mental condition of the athletes and offers psychological support.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Biomechanical Investigation-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The biomechanical analysis includes the mobility and pliability of muscles following injuries and impairments. This type of analysis promotes well-optimized performance and increases athletic efficiency. This analysis is necessary if you want to maintain your strength despite the prevalence of sports injuries. Everything, from corrective techniques to educational training, is continually evaluated. There is always a restriction on returning to the ground unless there is final approval from the sports trainer, coach, or sports physiotherapist experts.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Conclusion-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Players are a source of national pride because they utilize their physical prowess to promote the country&#39;s reputation. It is a privilege for physiotherapists to make individuals fit and healthy. The physiotherapist is responsible for everything, from the injury to the diet. Every session is designed to increase endurance and build strength for enhanced performance. Injuries affect the athlete both physically and psychologically. A sports physiotherapist works diligently to restore mental and physical balance. Therefore, if you are an athlete, you must employ a sports physiotherapist to improve your game and body. Regarding the </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-treatment\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">physiotherapy clinic in baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/206577288_31_05_2023_01_04_27.jpg','2023-05-31 07:30:12','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(83,'preventing-osteoporosis-through-proper-nutrition-building-strong-bones-for-life','Preventing Osteoporosis through Proper Nutrition: Building Strong Bones for Life','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThe bones provide the body with structure and support for daily activities. Without bones, it is impossible to create equilibrium on the lan...','<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The bones provide the body with structure and support for daily activities. Without bones, it is impossible to create equilibrium on the land. However, modern lifestyles and dietary behaviors are destroying the health of bones, resulting in osteoporosis and other bone disorders. This is a prevalent bone condition in the United States, affecting approximately 53 million individuals.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">This widespread misconception holds that women are most likely to be affected by this issue. Due to their thin and tiny bones, they are susceptible to this issue, but men also experience it. Because diseases do not discriminate based on gender, both men and women should be aware of this issue. Today, we are going to highlight a great deal about the osteoporosis causes, and the nutrients that you must consume to cover all of its gaps.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">What exactly is osteoporosis? Risk factors and numerous others</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Osteoporosis is a type of bone disease caused by a decrease in estradiol hormone levels. Loss of bone mass and density causes this type of bone disorder. A single sneezing can fracture a person&#39;s bones, making this situation potentially lethal. Similar to a silent heart attack, osteoporosis is referred to as a &quot;silent bone disease&quot; because it can deteriorate the bones without causing any symptoms. It predominantly affected elderly men and women in their 30s. At a certain age, the rate of bone formation and replacement by newer bones is accelerated. However, this is not always the case, and after the age of 30, the body&#39;s capacity decreases. This is the region where the likelihood of confronting bone-related diseases increases.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Osteoporosis warning signs you should be aware of</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Insufficiency of oxygen</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Slouching position</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Chronic ache</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">decreased height</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Fracture more frequently</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">These are the risk factors for osteoporosis that you should be aware of&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Lifestyle habits:</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Osteoporosis is significantly affected by lifestyle choices. Men and women with poor lifestyle practices are more susceptible to developing this condition. Unhealthy food, erratic sleep, and a lack of physical activity are the worst lifestyle choices. According to an </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/orthopaedic-process\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">orthopedic doctor in baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, physically active individuals do not experience bone-related issues.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Hormonal dysfunction</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The underlying cause of hormonal imbalances is an unhealthy lifestyle. Ingestion of toxic foods and sleep disturbances can disrupt the hormone&#39;s function. This results in numerous health issues, including osteoporosis.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Consuming alcoholic beverages and smoking</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The worst situation begins with smoking and alcohol, both of which contain ingredients that weaken bones. For the benefit of your bones, you must therefore abstain from consuming alcohol and smoking.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Genetics</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The primary cause of osteoporosis is genetics or parental history. It has been observed that the majority of osteoporosis cases are inherited from the patient&#39;s parents or ancestors.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Best Nutrients for Bone Health in Osteoporosis</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Milk, yogurt, cheese, asparagus, cucumber, almonds, hard-boiled eggs, tofu, salmon, etc. all contain calcium.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Cereals, oats, citrus juice, eggs, and mushrooms all contain vitamin D.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Dark leafy green vegetables, almonds, quinoa, avocado, black legumes, and dark chocolate are rich in magnesium.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Vitamin K: green fruits, green grapes, kiwis, limes, broccoli</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The diet should be as per the weight, age, and height of an individual, so if you are planning the right diet plan, then it is required to visit the best orthopedic and physiotherapist in Pune for detailed insight. Bone health is dependent on a healthy diet, and physicians have recommended the ideal amounts of these nutrients. If an individual consumes less than the prescribed amount, bone-related issues such as a crackling sound, strain, and more frequent fractures develop. Strong bones are the foundation of a person&#39;s existence, which is why a healthy diet is also required for lifelong vitality.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Adapting a healthy lifestyle for powerful bones</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">In addition to diet and medication, there are a variety of health practices that physicians recommend for healthy bones. Physiotherapy is a type of treatment that is not only appropriate for bone fractures but also helps to strengthen bones. Consequently, physiotherapy is a universal treatment that relieves bone discomfort and maintains the body&#39;s equilibrium. In addition to weight-bearing exercises and avoiding alcohol and tobacco, weight-bearing exercises and avoiding alcohol and tobacco are additional recommendations for strengthening bones. Sunlight and maintaining a healthy weight are two of the finest practices.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Conclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">For improved bone health, a healthy lifestyle is necessary. A healthy diet, daily exercise or outdoor activity, and adequate rest are some of the best practices that every individual should adhere to. Patients can surmount osteoporosis by consulting with an orthopedic and physiotherapy specialist. Maintaining a healthy weight and diet can help you avoid this problem, even though it is impossible to detect it early. The proper physician will guide you in the best way possible and will not allow you to endure for so long. Contact Dr. Sumitz, a physiotherapist and </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/how-to-choose-the-right-orthopedic-surgeon\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">orthopaedic surgeon in baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, with any questions regarding the bones.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/507099422_31_05_2023_02_48_38.jpg','2023-05-31 09:18:38','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(84,'understanding-osteoarthritis-causes-symptoms-and-risk-factors','Understanding Osteoarthritis: Causes, Symptoms, and Risk Factors','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','Osteoarthritis is a degenerative bone disease that has been affecting people worldwide. After polio, this is another prevalent disease that causes dis...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Osteoarthritis is a degenerative bone disease that has been affecting people worldwide. After polio, this is another prevalent disease that causes disability in the people of India. Deficiency of required nutrients for bones, major injuries, and an inactive lifestyle are the reasons behind this issue in men and women. Today we are highlighting the main causes and symptoms of osteoarthritis in detail. Precaution is better than cure, and if you want to prevent yourself from developing this bone disease, then this blog will help you raise awareness.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">What is osteoarthritis?&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Osteoarthritis primarily affects the bones and degrades the cartilage of the bones. As a result, the bones rub against each other during the movement, which causes pain, stiffness, and a lack of mobility. As per the orthopedic doctor in Pune, the cure for this issue is still under investigation. That is why it is recommended to eat a balanced diet and have some outdoor activity for the health of your bones.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Causes of Osteoarthritis</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">As people get older, the strength of their bones gets reduced, and at some point, they are unable to recover from injuries by themselves. The exact causes of osteoarthritis are still unidentified, but here are some factors that may contribute to this issue.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">&nbsp;Aging of people: The primary cause of this issue is age and the chances of osteoarthritis increase with age.&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Joint Injury: This may occur in the sportsperson such as fractures or ligament tears.&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Obesity: If a person is having obesity then the whole body weight fall on the joints and hip. This leads to the breakdown of cartilage.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Genetics: Genetic factors may influence an individual&#39;s susceptibility to osteoarthritis, including the structure and composition of their cartilage.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Symptoms of Osteoarthritis&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The symptoms of osteoarthritis can vary depending on the affected joint(s) and the severity of the condition. Common symptoms include:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Joint pain:&nbsp; Persistent or intermittent pain in the affected joint(s), which may worsen with movement or weight-bearing activities.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Stiffness: Joint stiffness, especially after periods of inactivity or upon waking up in the morning.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Reduced range of motion: Difficulty moving the affected joint(s) fully, leading to limitations in daily activities.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Swelling: Mild to moderate swelling around the affected joint(s), typically caused by inflammation.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Joint instability: A sensation of joints giving way or feeling unstable during movement.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Risk Factors for Osteoarthritis</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Certain factors can increase an individual&#39;s risk of developing osteoarthritis, including:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Age and gender: The risk of osteoarthritis increases with age, and women are more likely than men to develop the condition.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Obesity: Excess weight puts additional stress on the joints, increasing the risk of cartilage damage and osteoarthritis.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Occupation and joint overuse: Jobs that involve repetitive movements or joint overuse can contribute to joint degeneration over time.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Joint injuries: Previous joint injuries, such as sports-related injuries or accidents, can accelerate the onset of osteoarthritis.</span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">Genetics and family history: Certain genetic factors may make an individual more susceptible to osteoarthritis, and a family history of the condition can increase the risk.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Conclusion&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Osteoarthritis is a common and debilitating condition that affects the joints, causing pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility. By understanding its causes, symptoms, and risk factors, individuals can take proactive steps to manage and reduce the impact of osteoarthritis on their daily lives. Dr. Sumit is the </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/how-physiotherapy-prevents-and-heals-sports-injuries\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">physiotherapy doctor in baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, and if you are looking for </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/physiotherapy-clinic\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">physiotherapy clinic in pune</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, then this is the best place to look out for. For more informative content - stay connected. </span></p>\r\n<quillbot-extension-portal></quillbot-extension-portal>','uploads/product/590633928_31_05_2023_06_47_09.jpg','2023-05-31 13:17:09','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(85,'preventing-workplace-injuries-the-role-of-ergonomics-and-physiotherapy','Preventing Workplace Injuries: The Role of Ergonomics and Physiotherapy','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','In today&#39;s fast-paced work environment, workplace injuries have become increasingly prevalent. By incorporating proper ergonomics and utilizing th...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">In today&#39;s fast-paced work environment, workplace injuries have become increasingly prevalent. By incorporating proper ergonomics and utilizing the expertise of physiotherapy, businesses can significantly reduce the risk of injuries among their employees. In this blog post, we will explore the crucial role of ergonomics and </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">physiotherapy baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> in preventing workplace injuries, highlight their benefits, and provide practical tips for creating a safer and healthier work environment.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Understanding Workplace Injuries-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">To effectively prevent workplace injuries, t is important to first understand their causes and consequences. Workplace injuries can range from musculoskeletal disorders to repetitive strain injuries and falls. These injuries not only lead to physical pain and suffering but also result in decreased productivity, increased absenteeism, and financial burdens for both employees and employers.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The Significance of Ergonomics -</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Ergonomics is the science of designing and arranging workspaces, equipment, and tasks to fit the individual worker. By implementing ergonomic principles, businesses can optimize the interaction between workers and their work environment, reducing the risk of injuries and promoting overall well-being. Proper ergonomics can address issues such as poor posture, improper lifting techniques, and repetitive motion, which are common causes of workplace injuries.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Workstation Ergonomics-</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">This subsection will discuss the importance of ergonomic workstations, including proper desk and chair setup, monitor and keyboard placement, and lighting considerations. It will also provide tips for maintaining good posture and avoiding strains and discomfort during prolonged computer work.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Manual Handling and Lifting Techniques-</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Here, we will explore the correct techniques for manual handling and lifting, emphasizing the importance of proper body mechanics, the use of assistive equipment, and team lifting. Practical tips and guidelines will be provided to help employees reduce the risk of strains and injuries while performing manual tasks.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">The Role of Physiotherapy-</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Physiotherapy Baner plays a crucial role in preventing workplace injuries by promoting strength, flexibility, and overall physical well-being. Physiotherapists are skilled in assessing and addressing musculoskeletal issues, providing personalized treatment plans, and educating employees on injury prevention strategies.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Individualized Assessment and Treatment-</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">This subsection will highlight the importance of individual assessments conducted by physiotherapists to identify specific areas of concern and develop tailored treatment plans. It will also discuss various physiotherapy techniques, such as manual therapy, therapeutic exercises, and modalities like heat and cold therapy, to address workplace-related injuries and promote healing.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Education and Prevention Strategies-</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The majority of an employee&#39;s day is spent seated in a chair and staring directly at a computer screen. Physiotherapists play a vital role in educating employees about proper body mechanics, stretching exercises, and ergonomic practices. This subsection will emphasize the significance of physiotherapy-led education programs in preventing workplace injuries and empowering employees to take an active role in their own well-being.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Conclusion -</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">By prioritizing ergonomics and incorporating physiotherapy interventions, businesses can create a safer and healthier work environment, significantly reducing the occurrence of workplace injuries. Investing in ergonomic workstations, providing training on proper lifting techniques, and involving physiotherapists in injury prevention programs can lead to happier, healthier, and more productive employees. Together, let us strive to prevent workplace injuries and foster a culture of well-being in the workplace. Dr. Sumitz is the best </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">physiotherapy clinic in Baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> and provides the best </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">physiotherapy treatment in baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">. With the excellent team at the workspace, they are relieving the pain and bringing happiness to the face.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/194398974_02_06_2023_12_50_33.jpg','2023-06-02 07:10:43','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(86,'bone-and-joint-treatment ','Tips for maintaining your bone and joint health','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','In recent situations, we need to work hard every day to improve our standard of living, and having strong bones can help us fight off situations that...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">In recent situations, we need to work hard every day to improve our standard of living, and having strong bones can help us fight off situations that are impossible to overcome. Our strong bones are essential for carrying out daily activities like walking and picking up the cab before leaving the stop.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">However, there are instances when we demand more of our bodies while giving them nothing in return, such as a balanced diet and regular exercise. As a result, we encounter a number of disorders that weaken bone density and reduce the suppleness of the body. We are describing the entire approach here in order to prevent bone-related problems and restore lost bone strength.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Dietary Balance for Bone Strength</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The diet is crucial for developing stronger bones. To keep active as you age, consume a diet high in nutrients and bone-strengthening vitamins and minerals. According to an orthopedic surgeon in Pune, children between the ages of 9 and 18 need 1400 mg of calcium and 700 IU of vitamin D each day to have stronger bones. Adults and older adults, on the other hand, need to regularly ingest about 1200 mg of calcium and about 800 IU of vitamin D. Dairy products, leafy green vegetables, almonds, bread, and fish are just a few of the meals that promote bone density and strength. Regular consumption of these meals won&#39;t ever weaken or add heft to the bones.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Bone-strengthening workout</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The finest workouts for good bone health include gymnastics, walking, running, hopscotch, skipping, football, leaping, and climbing. Regular participation in these exercises will help prevent future minor and major injuries while also enhancing flexibility and stamina. The lack of time is a popular justification for most individuals, among many others, though. For this reason, people who don&#39;t participate in physical activities have a higher risk of falling and getting hurt. Such non-participative individuals require more time to heal from any sprain, fracture, or other injury.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">If you don&#39;t have enough time, you can design a routine depending on your body&#39;s capabilities and requirements. You require a physiotherapy and orthopedic consultant for all of this accurate advice.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Healthy Weight management</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">According to the WHO, more than 1 billion individuals worldwide are obese, which causes a number of health problems, including problems with the bones. The bones and joints bear the weight of the entire body, and carrying more weight than is healthy can cause discomfort and injuries. The average human weight, according to physicians, should be between 60 and 80 kg for both men and women. Maintaining a healthy weight will undoubtedly be aided by regular exercise and a balanced diet. One can avoid bone-related injuries by using weight management strategies. The body&#39;s structure will be kept in check by keeping everything under control and performing routine inspections.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Ergonomics and Posture</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">It has been shown that individuals with poor posture are more prone to bone problems, such as trauma, and poor body composition. A healthy body posture promotes blood flow and allows nutrients to continuously flow to all parts of the body. The bones and joints become stronger as a result of the constant flow of strength and energy. A body in proper alignment improves its reputation in the workplace and adds value to life. Learn the finest exercises to enhance posture and alignment, as well as ergonomic principles.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Preventing falls and injuries</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">It&#39;s not difficult to keep the body from getting hurt, but you can still do it at your own pace. The injury prevention strategy will help you avoid being hurt and prevent falls. Make your house and place of employment fall-proof, learn to sit and walk with a balanced posture, and practice your strength and balance. To avoid falls or mishaps, put on comfortable shoes and try to stay away from alcohol and drugs.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(67, 67, 67)\">Routine examinations and screenings</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Each month, keep an eye on your health. This will facilitate early detection and enable the use of preventative actions to address the problem. To receive essential health advice to maintain good health at any age, keep in touch with your orthopedic and physiotherapist. To keep active for the long term, consider therapies like acupuncture, massages, and physiotherapy sessions.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Conclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">A healthy physique encourages an active way of life and also improves personality. After retirement, this is not necessary to maintain a healthy lifestyle; one can begin today. Our health is in our own hands, so it should be a top priority to avoid doing things that may weaken our bones. According to the doctor&#39;s advice, children above the age of 12 should engage in outdoor activities and consume a balanced diet. All the elements you need to take into account for keeping your bones and joints healthy in 2023 are listed above. For further information, keep in touch with Dr. Sumitz, an </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/blogs/best-way-to-choose-orthopedic-near-me-from-baner-pune\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">orthopedic doctor in Baner</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">, and if you have any bone-related worries, search for an </span><a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopaedic-doctor\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(17, 85, 204)\">orthopedic doctor near me</span></a><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> and make an appointment for a consultation.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">FAQs</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">How can I strengthen my bones?</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">A person should consume plenty of nutrients, fruits, and green leafy vegetables while avoiding caffeine, alcohol, and smoking in order to improve bone strength. The bones and joints can become more resilient with regular exercise and sound sleep.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h2><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Which physician is best for joints and bones?</span></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">A specialist in evaluating the condition of bones and joints is an <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopaedic-doctor\">orthopedic physician</a>. They assist, inform, keep tabs on the patient&#39;s problems, and recommend the most effective course of action.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">How often should I visit an orthopedic surgeon?</span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Consult with an experienced <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/services/orthopaedic-doctor\">orthopedic specialist in Pune</a> if you experience persistent pain in your bones and joints, are unable to move normally, or have any other bone-related problems.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','uploads/product/486558156_09_06_2023_12_56_13.jpg','2023-06-08 19:17:53','2026-07-14 08:35:27','2026-07-14 08:35:27',NULL),(87,'prevent-sports-injuries-guide-from-best-orthopedic-and-physiotherapy-clinic-in-baner-drsumitz','Prevent Sports Injuries: Guide From Best Orthopedic and Physiotherapy Clinic In Baner - Dr.Sumitz','Orthopedics & Physiotherapy','The drive to succeed in any sport comes from the athlete&#39;s dedication to a certain objective. The majority of newbie athletes disregard their heal...','<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(37, 37, 37)\">The drive to succeed in any sport comes from the athlete&#39;s dedication to a certain objective. The majority of newbie athletes disregard their health and make a number of blunders that lead them nowhere. Overtraining, doping, omitting meals, and long hours of practice are some of the ways in which they push themselves to the limit in pursuit of success. The blog continues its focus on common errors that athletes make during the training period and shares one solution to avoid them in an effort to reduce the risk of injury.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(37, 37, 37)\">Overtraining syndrome-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(37, 37, 37)\">Athletes need to perform at a well-optimized level in their games; therefore, they practice relentlessly and rarely take breaks. They put their health on the back burner so they can perform at the top of their game every time. Fatigue, soreness, an inability to focus, and injury are the end results of overtraining and inadequate rest. It&#39;s important to give some thought to whether or not your body can handle overtraining. Unless you know this fact, never step forward because it leads to complications</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Bad form and technique-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Each sport calls for a unique set of skills, and each demands that you put extra focus on a specific set of muscles to gain endurance and strength. Additionally, if a qualified <strong>physiotherapist</strong> is coaching you, they will teach you the proper form and technique. Whether it&#39;s an elbow flick or a leg kick, you&#39;ll need to master these skills if you want to perform better. Sportsmen and women who have mastered proper technique have a lower risk of injury and consistently superior results.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Negligence of warm-up and cool-down&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Getting the body up and ready for action is important, which is why it is required to perform warm-up and cool-down exercises. Flexibility, range of motion, and blood flow can all benefit from this type of exercise. Stretching is a kind of warm-up exercise that athletes perform before hitting the sports equipment. In most cases, they avoid warm-ups, which can increase the likelihood of injury during workouts and play. Cool-down exercises afterward will keep the blood pumping and the muscles limber for the next round of competition or workout.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Putting off strength training-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Timely exercise, sufficient rest, and a healthy diet all contribute to <a href=\"https://www.drsumitz.com/treatments/general-physical-therapy\">physical fitness</a>. The desire to keep one&#39;s strength up is universal, whether one is engaged in athletics or physical exercise. Overtraining and anxiety can reduce strength and movement quality, so body conditioning is necessary for building muscular strength and stability. In order to improve their performance, an individual should consult their coach and ask for specific advice tailored to their body and sport.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Inadequate Safety Precautions-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">In sports, disregarding the importance of safety gear can lead to injuries and a halt in the game. Learning about and practicing safety precautions is essential for avoiding harm of any kind. The purpose of protective gear like helmets and gloves in sports is to keep you safe while you play. Participants in physical activity programs should only engage in their activities under the watchful eye of trained professionals to provide a safe and accident-free environment. Learn self-defense to lessen the likelihood of getting hurt while participating in sports.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Subpar diet and lack of water-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Compromises in nutrition and diet may cause serious problems while the body is engaged in high-performance activities. Sprains and fractures are more likely to occur when the body is undernourished and dehydrated. Food and water provide the body with the nutrients it needs to function optimally and are therefore the primary sources of energy. Getting enough of the right nutrients can help you work harder, heal faster, and enhance the performance of your bones and joints. Athletes need a balanced diet that includes carbs, lipids, proteins, and vitamins C and D.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Ignoring discomfort and carrying on-</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Athletes are accustomed to pushing their bodies to the limit in pursuit of greater success; as a result, they often continue to engage in painful activities despite experiencing significant discomfort. Because of this, it could cause them to slow down and prepare for sleep. Pay attention to how you feel, and if you need more help, talk to your sports mentor.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"background-color:transparent; color:rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Conclusion :</span></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"backg